1
00:00:00,507 --> 00:00:01,960
(Second set, Shujitsu High 24:
Wonder Dogs 14)

2
00:00:01,961 --> 00:00:03,528
Set point for Shujitsu High School
in the second set.

3
00:00:06,591 --> 00:00:08,791
(Ho Bin's serve)

4
00:00:10,539 --> 00:00:11,639
(Service error)

5
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:14,519
And that wraps up the second set.

6
00:00:15,019 --> 00:00:16,352
- Come on.
- What?

7
00:00:16,504 --> 00:00:18,238
No mistake, at least!

8
00:00:18,752 --> 00:00:20,985
(This can't be happening.)

9
00:00:20,985 --> 00:00:23,251
(Second set, Shujitsu High 25:
Wonder Dogs 14)

10
00:00:23,252 --> 00:00:25,285
Shujitsu takes the second set as well.

11
00:00:25,285 --> 00:00:27,277
(Set score, 2:0)

12
00:00:29,235 --> 00:00:31,185
(Third-set timeout)

13
00:00:34,585 --> 00:00:38,385
Why do you keep making
unforced errors like that?

14
00:00:38,385 --> 00:00:40,785
We get a free ball, and then
we just give it right back to them.

15
00:00:40,785 --> 00:00:42,485
Why does that keep happening?

16
00:00:42,485 --> 00:00:43,952
What's the issue right now?

17
00:00:46,819 --> 00:00:48,285
We can't waste the ball.

18
00:00:49,885 --> 00:00:52,152
Look at their outside hitters.
Their defense is solid.

19
00:00:52,152 --> 00:00:53,485
When you try too hard to force the kill,

20
00:00:53,485 --> 00:00:54,719
you just end up racking up errors.

21
00:00:55,552 --> 00:00:57,952
You don't have to win every single point
on your own.

22
00:00:59,619 --> 00:01:02,919
Why are you trying to carry
the whole load?

23
00:01:02,919 --> 00:01:04,519
- Right.
- There are six of us out here.

24
00:01:05,952 --> 00:01:10,452
Was "Flame Deer" always this vocal?

25
00:01:10,685 --> 00:01:12,385
She just said something really great.

26
00:01:12,719 --> 00:01:15,785
"Why are you trying to do it
all yourself?"

27
00:01:15,785 --> 00:01:17,985
"Remember,
there are six of us on the court."

28
00:01:18,552 --> 00:01:21,519
Right now, the players are putting
way too much pressure on themselves...

29
00:01:21,519 --> 00:01:23,619
because they feel like they have
to shoulder everything alone.

30
00:01:24,452 --> 00:01:27,152
As a veteran,
she's seeing the bigger picture out there.

31
00:01:27,152 --> 00:01:30,119
They can afford to take a breath
and trust each other.

32
00:01:30,119 --> 00:01:32,752
(There are six players together
on the court.)

33
00:01:32,752 --> 00:01:33,885
It's not my team.

34
00:01:33,885 --> 00:01:34,752
It's our team.

35
00:01:35,752 --> 00:01:37,852
Play like it's your last set.

36
00:01:37,852 --> 00:01:39,685
- Okay.
- Okay.

37
00:01:39,952 --> 00:01:42,085
Feeling a little less nervous now?

38
00:01:42,085 --> 00:01:44,119
- Yes.
- Starting to feel manageable?

39
00:01:44,119 --> 00:01:44,919
You got this?

40
00:01:45,319 --> 00:01:47,219
Nothing to be nervous about.
One mistake is fine.

41
00:01:47,219 --> 00:01:48,585
It's the unforced errors...

42
00:01:48,585 --> 00:01:50,052
The easy ones.

43
00:01:50,052 --> 00:01:52,385
There were so many balls
we could've kept in play.

44
00:01:52,385 --> 00:01:54,252
Let's just clean those up one by one.

45
00:01:54,252 --> 00:01:55,519
It's fine. We reset from zero.

46
00:01:55,519 --> 00:01:58,519
It's okay. We can do this.

47
00:01:59,319 --> 00:02:00,552
Let's go!

48
00:02:00,552 --> 00:02:02,452
- Fight until the final whistle!
- We can do this!

49
00:02:02,452 --> 00:02:03,985
- One, two, three!
- Let's go!

50
00:02:03,985 --> 00:02:04,819
Let's go!

51
00:02:06,352 --> 00:02:07,452
(Episode 3)

52
00:02:07,452 --> 00:02:09,352
Clean slate, let's go!

53
00:02:09,352 --> 00:02:12,119
(Episode 3: Learning from their mistakes)

54
00:02:13,719 --> 00:02:16,352
Play as you did in the first set.
Stay locked in.

55
00:02:17,819 --> 00:02:19,952
Shujitsu High School is looking
for the sweep here.

56
00:02:19,952 --> 00:02:21,285
There's a change in their lineup.

57
00:02:21,719 --> 00:02:24,285
Number 11, Uchida Riona,
who caused huge problems...

58
00:02:24,285 --> 00:02:27,052
for the Wonder Dogs last year,
checks into the match.

59
00:02:28,352 --> 00:02:30,619
(Uchida was at the heart...)

60
00:02:30,619 --> 00:02:32,952
(of last year's reverse sweep.)

61
00:02:36,152 --> 00:02:39,985
(Immediately after Uchida came in,
they gave up four points on her serve.)

62
00:02:45,285 --> 00:02:49,552
(They eventually surrendered
nine straight points.)

63
00:02:50,119 --> 00:02:52,785
(The key player behind the reverse sweep
that still haunts them)

64
00:02:53,285 --> 00:02:58,252
(They meet again across the net.)

65
00:02:58,919 --> 00:02:59,852
Let's do this!

66
00:03:00,085 --> 00:03:01,219
They're already down two sets.

67
00:03:01,219 --> 00:03:02,519
Here begins the third set.

68
00:03:03,085 --> 00:03:04,185
Let's go!

69
00:03:08,119 --> 00:03:10,252
(The ball goes to Uchida.)

70
00:03:10,852 --> 00:03:11,685
Hard swing out of the middle!

71
00:03:12,085 --> 00:03:13,052
And she puts it down!

72
00:03:14,452 --> 00:03:16,185
Uchida checks in and immediately puts...

73
00:03:16,185 --> 00:03:17,452
the first point on the board.

74
00:03:18,719 --> 00:03:21,385
Why do our hands keep
getting used like that?

75
00:03:21,385 --> 00:03:22,462
The timing is the problem.

76
00:03:23,985 --> 00:03:25,552
Your positioning is fine.
Just press your hands over!

77
00:03:26,485 --> 00:03:27,519
Hyo Rim!

78
00:03:27,519 --> 00:03:29,852
Feed Enkhsoyol more. Don't hesitate.

79
00:03:31,285 --> 00:03:32,819
Nice!

80
00:03:34,119 --> 00:03:35,252
The score is 1 to 0.

81
00:03:35,252 --> 00:03:36,952
(Yoshimoto's serve)

82
00:03:40,019 --> 00:03:42,219
(Is Yeon Joo getting ready to attack?)

83
00:03:44,085 --> 00:03:45,385
Enkhsoyol!

84
00:03:45,385 --> 00:03:46,185
She scores.

85
00:03:47,152 --> 00:03:48,985
If we can isolate her
with a single block like that,

86
00:03:48,985 --> 00:03:51,252
Enkhsoyol will put the ball away
every time.

87
00:03:51,252 --> 00:03:54,752
They're going to start shading
toward Yeon Joo now too.

88
00:03:56,119 --> 00:03:57,119
Nice receive.

89
00:03:57,119 --> 00:03:59,052
Great set, Hyo Rim!

90
00:04:01,885 --> 00:04:04,019
(A good start!)

91
00:04:04,885 --> 00:04:07,985
If we get a free ball,
run it through the middle.

92
00:04:07,985 --> 00:04:08,752
Got it.

93
00:04:09,852 --> 00:04:10,885
Tied at 1 to 1.

94
00:04:11,185 --> 00:04:12,052
Enkhsoyol to serve.

95
00:04:12,052 --> 00:04:13,752
(They handle the tough serve!)

96
00:04:14,752 --> 00:04:16,352
(Attack through the middle!)

97
00:04:17,085 --> 00:04:17,919
Middle quick.

98
00:04:18,685 --> 00:04:19,585
Tool off the block and out!

99
00:04:19,585 --> 00:04:20,819
(An immediate point through the middle)

100
00:04:21,252 --> 00:04:23,852
(Shujitsu's strategy works too.)

101
00:04:25,452 --> 00:04:27,219
Gosh.

102
00:04:29,219 --> 00:04:30,052
Chae Rim!

103
00:04:30,652 --> 00:04:32,519
When you're in Zone Four,
they're shading inside,

104
00:04:32,519 --> 00:04:34,319
so line to Zone One is
wide open right now.

105
00:04:34,919 --> 00:04:35,752
Got it.

106
00:04:35,752 --> 00:04:36,852
(The instruction is to push it
toward Zone One.)

107
00:04:38,052 --> 00:04:39,319
Enkhsoyol!

108
00:04:39,319 --> 00:04:41,085
There we go!

109
00:04:41,319 --> 00:04:42,119
I got it!

110
00:04:42,652 --> 00:04:44,719
(As planned, the ball goes to Chae Rim.)

111
00:04:45,785 --> 00:04:46,919
She pushes the ball in!

112
00:04:46,919 --> 00:04:47,919
Nice!

113
00:04:48,685 --> 00:04:50,019
- Great shot!
- Nice!

114
00:04:50,019 --> 00:04:51,585
(The strategy works.)

115
00:04:55,919 --> 00:04:56,885
(She sells the cross-court shot...)

116
00:04:56,885 --> 00:04:57,719
(then changes direction.)

117
00:04:57,719 --> 00:05:01,019
- She found the open court beautifully.
- Exactly.

118
00:05:04,285 --> 00:05:05,252
Nice!

119
00:05:05,585 --> 00:05:07,319
- Wonder Dogs!
- Wonder Dogs!

120
00:05:08,919 --> 00:05:09,919
Hyo Rim!

121
00:05:10,219 --> 00:05:12,552
Run the B quick more. It's working.

122
00:05:12,552 --> 00:05:13,352
Okay.

123
00:05:14,852 --> 00:05:17,452
(Third set,
Shujitsu High School 3: Wonder Dogs 3)

124
00:05:18,519 --> 00:05:20,085
Uchida back to serve.

125
00:05:21,219 --> 00:05:23,019
- Watch the short serve!
- Okay, I will.

126
00:05:23,485 --> 00:05:24,552
Stay ready!

127
00:05:28,352 --> 00:05:29,485
Clips the tape and rolls over!

128
00:05:29,785 --> 00:05:31,052
Run the B quick more. It's working.

129
00:05:31,400 --> 00:05:32,585
(As instructed,
the ball goes to Yeon Joo.)

130
00:05:32,585 --> 00:05:33,719
(Bait bitten!)

131
00:05:34,952 --> 00:05:36,285
Spike!

132
00:05:36,691 --> 00:05:38,525
- Put away!
- That's it!

133
00:05:39,519 --> 00:05:42,219
It was her signature cross-court swing!

134
00:05:43,252 --> 00:05:45,552
Great set, Hyo Rim!

135
00:05:45,552 --> 00:05:47,019
(A fierce battle for every single point)

136
00:05:48,785 --> 00:05:49,852
Wonder Dogs lead 4 to 3.

137
00:05:50,185 --> 00:05:51,885
Looking to build momentum
with Yeon Joo serving.

138
00:05:52,119 --> 00:05:53,585
(Yeon Joo's serve)

139
00:05:57,352 --> 00:05:59,052
- Pipe attack from the back row!
- Up for the block!

140
00:06:01,407 --> 00:06:02,519
Touch out!

141
00:06:02,519 --> 00:06:03,485
(Block touch out)

142
00:06:03,784 --> 00:06:06,318
(The score is tied again.)

143
00:06:06,319 --> 00:06:07,452
(What a shame.)

144
00:06:07,452 --> 00:06:08,919
Guys!

145
00:06:08,919 --> 00:06:10,452
Let's just get one clean block!

146
00:06:10,452 --> 00:06:12,685
Block and dig!

147
00:06:12,685 --> 00:06:14,919
Just one block, one dig, please!

148
00:06:15,319 --> 00:06:16,252
Okay!

149
00:06:16,819 --> 00:06:18,452
Let's get one right back!

150
00:06:18,452 --> 00:06:20,385
- Let's make a stop!
- All tied up at 4 to 4.

151
00:06:21,485 --> 00:06:24,252
They have to stay sharp
during Onishi's serve rotation.

152
00:06:24,252 --> 00:06:25,019
Right.

153
00:06:26,119 --> 00:06:27,052
Heavy serve coming.

154
00:06:27,485 --> 00:06:28,819
Overpass!

155
00:06:30,052 --> 00:06:30,985
(Stopping)

156
00:06:32,585 --> 00:06:35,852
(Overpass kill)

157
00:06:36,985 --> 00:06:41,585
The timing...

158
00:06:42,019 --> 00:06:44,619
(Why does the coach keep
emphasizing the blocking timing?)

159
00:06:45,852 --> 00:06:48,252
(The blocking strategy against Shujitsu)

160
00:06:48,252 --> 00:06:50,852
If you jump when they jump,
you'll be late on the way down.

161
00:06:50,852 --> 00:06:53,385
They hang in the air,

162
00:06:54,052 --> 00:06:56,485
so you can't match their takeoff.

163
00:06:58,085 --> 00:06:59,285
Wait for the hitter to leave the ground,

164
00:06:59,285 --> 00:07:01,119
then count one, two, three.

165
00:07:01,319 --> 00:07:03,419
The moment you think "Now,"
that's when you press. Got it?

166
00:07:04,985 --> 00:07:10,252
(She kept emphasizing the blocking timing
throughout the earlier sets.)

167
00:07:12,385 --> 00:07:15,819
I kept drilling it into them,
but it just wasn't clicking.

168
00:07:16,119 --> 00:07:19,119
Eventually, I put down the clipboard...

169
00:07:20,219 --> 00:07:21,385
and realized I had to...

170
00:07:22,585 --> 00:07:23,714
step in directly.

171
00:07:29,685 --> 00:07:30,552
Guys!

172
00:07:30,952 --> 00:07:33,185
Take 1, 2, 3.
Delay your jump on count three.

173
00:07:33,185 --> 00:07:34,119
Take your time!

174
00:07:35,019 --> 00:07:35,852
- Okay!
- Okay!

175
00:07:37,019 --> 00:07:38,485
Onishi serves.

176
00:07:41,485 --> 00:07:42,685
Another rocket.

177
00:07:44,685 --> 00:07:46,352
Handled on the left.

178
00:07:46,852 --> 00:07:47,985
Pipe attack!

179
00:07:47,985 --> 00:07:49,119
In 1, 2...

180
00:07:49,385 --> 00:07:50,452
(And 3!)

181
00:07:51,104 --> 00:07:52,152
Dug up! Beautiful!

182
00:07:52,152 --> 00:07:52,952
Going middle, right?

183
00:07:55,370 --> 00:07:56,903
(Shujitsu's counterattack)

184
00:07:57,196 --> 00:07:58,263
In 1, 2...

185
00:07:58,758 --> 00:07:59,770
(And 3!)

186
00:07:59,870 --> 00:08:01,237
That's it!

187
00:08:01,237 --> 00:08:03,570
Great dig! Transition opportunity!

188
00:08:03,570 --> 00:08:05,337
- Chae Rim!
- That was a bit loose.

189
00:08:05,337 --> 00:08:06,337
(Shujitsu's free ball)

190
00:08:07,103 --> 00:08:08,103
There!

191
00:08:08,737 --> 00:08:09,903
She keeps it alive!

192
00:08:10,070 --> 00:08:11,303
Couldn't turn it into a swing, though.

193
00:08:11,303 --> 00:08:13,503
Slow it down.

194
00:08:13,637 --> 00:08:15,270
Free ball for Shujitsu again.

195
00:08:16,637 --> 00:08:17,637
Roll shot!

196
00:08:17,803 --> 00:08:18,803
The ball...

197
00:08:19,170 --> 00:08:20,703
- She saved it!
- Set it up!

198
00:08:20,703 --> 00:08:22,037
(Relentless defense)

199
00:08:22,037 --> 00:08:23,170
Kept alive and pushed over!

200
00:08:24,870 --> 00:08:26,670
Hey! In, 1, 2!

201
00:08:27,070 --> 00:08:28,103
Up for the block!

202
00:08:28,570 --> 00:08:29,570
That's it!

203
00:08:30,370 --> 00:08:31,370
Kept in play!

204
00:08:31,370 --> 00:08:32,603
(Set it up.)

205
00:08:32,670 --> 00:08:33,670
Back Attack!

206
00:08:33,803 --> 00:08:35,003
- Free ball!
- One, two!

207
00:08:37,603 --> 00:08:38,737
She sails it long!

208
00:08:38,737 --> 00:08:39,737
(Onishi's attack error)

209
00:08:40,037 --> 00:08:42,137
- That's the timing right there!
- Exactly.

210
00:08:42,903 --> 00:08:44,570
Good! Keep pushing!

211
00:08:44,570 --> 00:08:47,637
Don't scoop it,
just push it deep into the corners.

212
00:08:47,637 --> 00:08:48,770
(A solid block forces an error.)

213
00:08:48,770 --> 00:08:51,203
- The energy has completely shifted!
- It really has!

214
00:08:51,670 --> 00:08:53,537
- Too quick!
- Nice!

215
00:08:53,537 --> 00:08:55,570
Send it over cleanly,
and we'll get our chance.

216
00:08:55,570 --> 00:08:56,570
(Push it over for the chance.)

217
00:08:56,570 --> 00:08:58,103
- Okay.
- Let's stay error-free.

218
00:08:58,103 --> 00:08:59,870
Just like Yeon Joo said,
send it deep, and we'll get the chance.

219
00:08:59,870 --> 00:09:01,370
- Let's create that chance.
- Just get it over clean.

220
00:09:01,370 --> 00:09:02,403
Got it.

221
00:09:02,637 --> 00:09:04,837
Enkhsoyol, great catch!

222
00:09:04,837 --> 00:09:05,837
Get up on the block!

223
00:09:06,137 --> 00:09:08,670
Just one stuff block! Dial in the timing!

224
00:09:10,703 --> 00:09:11,703
Watch the block. Got it.

225
00:09:12,637 --> 00:09:14,570
All tied up at 5 to 5.

226
00:09:16,603 --> 00:09:19,570
(Let's turn the tables!)

227
00:09:22,470 --> 00:09:23,470
One, two!

228
00:09:23,870 --> 00:09:24,903
(Three!)

229
00:09:25,037 --> 00:09:27,003
There!

230
00:09:27,003 --> 00:09:28,437
- Dug up! Clean pass!
- Put it away!

231
00:09:28,437 --> 00:09:29,737
(They save the chance.)

232
00:09:32,737 --> 00:09:34,403
(Trying to counterattack)

233
00:09:34,537 --> 00:09:35,937
Stay calm and 1, 2.

234
00:09:36,403 --> 00:09:37,670
(And 3!)

235
00:09:37,870 --> 00:09:38,870
Spike!

236
00:09:39,670 --> 00:09:41,670
- Long!
- Out! That's out!

237
00:09:41,670 --> 00:09:42,670
It's wide!

238
00:09:43,770 --> 00:09:46,537
(They forced another error.)

239
00:09:46,970 --> 00:09:48,837
When we take away their angles,

240
00:09:48,903 --> 00:09:50,670
- they start forcing errors!
- Exactly!

241
00:09:52,037 --> 00:09:54,203
(With the block perfectly timed,)

242
00:09:54,937 --> 00:09:57,203
(the hitter couldn't find an angle...)

243
00:09:57,203 --> 00:09:58,837
(and hit it out.)

244
00:10:00,037 --> 00:10:01,670
(Flustered)

245
00:10:01,670 --> 00:10:04,637
- Shujitsu is getting rattled now.
- Right.

246
00:10:04,970 --> 00:10:06,437
Let's go!

247
00:10:06,437 --> 00:10:07,870
Wonder Dogs take the lead!

248
00:10:08,603 --> 00:10:09,603
Chae Rim!

249
00:10:09,870 --> 00:10:10,937
Drive the serve deep!

250
00:10:11,237 --> 00:10:12,503
Deep to the end line!

251
00:10:14,670 --> 00:10:15,670
(Understood)

252
00:10:15,670 --> 00:10:16,737
Now that it's 6 to 5,

253
00:10:17,570 --> 00:10:19,770
we can't give away free points here.

254
00:10:21,203 --> 00:10:23,137
(Chae Rim serves.)

255
00:10:25,370 --> 00:10:26,603
Let's go!

256
00:10:26,603 --> 00:10:27,703
(Out)

257
00:10:27,703 --> 00:10:29,437
(Whoa!)

258
00:10:29,437 --> 00:10:30,603
(Glancing)

259
00:10:33,937 --> 00:10:35,637
You just called for that.

260
00:10:36,037 --> 00:10:37,070
My bad.

261
00:10:38,703 --> 00:10:41,537
(Tied again after the error)

262
00:10:41,737 --> 00:10:43,337
Shake it off! Get the side-out right back!

263
00:10:43,337 --> 00:10:46,070
It's fine! Win back the serve!

264
00:10:46,070 --> 00:10:47,103
(Let's bounce back.)

265
00:10:47,737 --> 00:10:49,437
(Nogami Yuina serves.)

266
00:10:49,437 --> 00:10:50,437
Mine!

267
00:10:51,003 --> 00:10:52,503
Put up a clean set!

268
00:10:57,270 --> 00:10:59,337
(They make an attack error next.)

269
00:11:00,337 --> 00:11:01,337
Slow your approach!

270
00:11:02,237 --> 00:11:05,703
Hit it deep!

271
00:11:06,003 --> 00:11:08,837
Enkhsoyol's swings are landing
too shallow.

272
00:11:08,837 --> 00:11:10,637
Right. She needs to push the ball deep...

273
00:11:10,637 --> 00:11:12,437
- and swing with conviction.
- Exactly.

274
00:11:14,468 --> 00:11:15,827
Shujitsu High School up 8 to 7,

275
00:11:16,137 --> 00:11:19,670
taking us into the first technical timeout
of the third set.

276
00:11:19,670 --> 00:11:21,137
(Technical timeout)

277
00:11:21,337 --> 00:11:24,670
Keep your eyes on the scoreboard.

278
00:11:24,670 --> 00:11:26,837
We had multiple opportunities
to run our offense.

279
00:11:26,837 --> 00:11:28,470
What did I emphasize
about the transition play?

280
00:11:28,470 --> 00:11:29,603
- Hit it deep.
- Hit it deep.

281
00:11:29,603 --> 00:11:31,003
Don't catch the tape.
Aim for the back line.

282
00:11:31,037 --> 00:11:33,203
If you're going to miss, miss long.

283
00:11:33,403 --> 00:11:34,603
Understand? Push it deep.

284
00:11:34,603 --> 00:11:35,870
- Got it?
- Yes!

285
00:11:36,137 --> 00:11:37,170
- Let's get this!
- Let's do this!

286
00:11:37,170 --> 00:11:38,203
Let's go!

287
00:11:38,503 --> 00:11:39,503
One, two, three!

288
00:11:39,870 --> 00:11:40,970
You've got this!

289
00:11:42,237 --> 00:11:43,570
The score is 8 to 7, just a one-point gap.

290
00:11:43,570 --> 00:11:44,803
(Kato Uta serves.)

291
00:11:48,603 --> 00:11:49,603
Rip it!

292
00:11:49,770 --> 00:11:50,803
Rip it!

293
00:11:51,570 --> 00:11:52,603
Here comes Enkhsoyol!

294
00:11:52,837 --> 00:11:53,837
Stuffed at the net!

295
00:11:54,003 --> 00:11:55,837
Hold on. Take your time!

296
00:11:55,937 --> 00:11:57,370
Go right back to her!

297
00:11:59,037 --> 00:12:00,070
Setting her again!

298
00:12:00,437 --> 00:12:01,903
- Drive it deeper. Got it?
- Yes!

299
00:12:03,803 --> 00:12:04,803
(A touch)

300
00:12:06,203 --> 00:12:07,503
Wiped off the block and out!

301
00:12:07,737 --> 00:12:10,270
(I got it.)

302
00:12:10,270 --> 00:12:11,270
There we go!

303
00:12:17,337 --> 00:12:18,437
Tied at 8 to 8!

304
00:12:18,837 --> 00:12:20,470
Now's the time to break away!

305
00:12:26,270 --> 00:12:29,137
- Great hustle on defense!
- Over there!

306
00:12:29,137 --> 00:12:30,170
Mine!

307
00:12:30,870 --> 00:12:32,092
Back to Enkhsoyol!

308
00:12:32,970 --> 00:12:34,270
Push it deep!

309
00:12:34,270 --> 00:12:35,270
Swing!

310
00:12:36,403 --> 00:12:37,403
Enkhsoyol!

311
00:12:38,337 --> 00:12:39,503
Answering right back!

312
00:12:39,937 --> 00:12:42,437
That's what I'm talking about!

313
00:12:43,470 --> 00:12:44,903
- Yes!
- Great dig!

314
00:12:44,903 --> 00:12:46,803
- Beautiful!
- Huge kill, Enkhsoyol!

315
00:12:46,803 --> 00:12:47,837
Great shot!

316
00:12:48,070 --> 00:12:50,570
Enkhsoyol, keep driving it deep
just like that!

317
00:12:50,570 --> 00:12:52,403
Great swing. That was executed perfectly.

318
00:12:53,503 --> 00:12:55,070
Wonder Dogs take back the lead, 9 to 8!

319
00:12:55,237 --> 00:12:57,103
Time to build a cushion!

320
00:12:57,270 --> 00:12:59,137
(Back in the lead)

321
00:12:59,470 --> 00:13:01,003
(Let's keep scoring!)

322
00:13:01,003 --> 00:13:02,903
(Enkhsoyol! Deep-soyol!)

323
00:13:04,170 --> 00:13:06,037
Wonder Dogs lead 9 to 8.

324
00:13:10,003 --> 00:13:11,170
A miscommunication on that play.

325
00:13:11,537 --> 00:13:12,844
There. Shake it off, you're fine.

326
00:13:13,570 --> 00:13:14,803
Free ball for us!

327
00:13:15,203 --> 00:13:17,270
(To Deep-soyol once again)

328
00:13:17,270 --> 00:13:18,737
Enkhsoyol!

329
00:13:27,570 --> 00:13:28,670
Tool off the block!

330
00:13:29,270 --> 00:13:31,470
(Three points in a row)

331
00:13:31,470 --> 00:13:34,403
Enkhsoyol has completely
bought into the deep-court attack...

332
00:13:34,403 --> 00:13:37,070
that Coach Kim called for.

333
00:13:37,470 --> 00:13:39,470
That's three consecutive points for her!

334
00:13:39,470 --> 00:13:41,503
(Quickly apologizing)

335
00:13:42,303 --> 00:13:43,570
- I've got the short roll!
- That felt incredible.

336
00:13:43,770 --> 00:13:46,203
Everything we worked on is paying off.

337
00:13:46,570 --> 00:13:48,070
We weren't about to drop this set.

338
00:13:48,370 --> 00:13:49,437
Free ball!

339
00:13:49,437 --> 00:13:50,737
Enkhsoyol again!

340
00:13:57,137 --> 00:13:59,470
Another block touch out!

341
00:14:00,037 --> 00:14:01,903
There it is!

342
00:14:03,103 --> 00:14:06,570
(We're on a roll now!)

343
00:14:06,570 --> 00:14:08,703
("Let's go, Wonder Dogs!")

344
00:14:09,537 --> 00:14:12,370
(Third set, Shujitsu High 10:
Wonder Dogs 11)

345
00:14:13,070 --> 00:14:15,670
They keep using our hands!

346
00:14:21,969 --> 00:14:23,966
Setting to the outside.
Seal the line and cover!

347
00:14:23,967 --> 00:14:24,942
Yes, Coach!

348
00:14:28,826 --> 00:14:31,542
(Onishi is on the left.)

349
00:14:33,156 --> 00:14:34,456
(Glancing)

350
00:14:35,437 --> 00:14:36,637
Left side!

351
00:14:37,203 --> 00:14:39,470
Left! Watch the pin!

352
00:14:40,570 --> 00:14:43,070
The timing! Press over!

353
00:14:43,070 --> 00:14:44,170
Watch your timing!

354
00:14:45,403 --> 00:14:46,437
Slow down the takeoff.

355
00:14:46,437 --> 00:14:48,037
(Resetting the block)

356
00:14:49,237 --> 00:14:51,203
(Deep-soyol serves.)

357
00:14:52,637 --> 00:14:53,703
Great serve!

358
00:14:53,703 --> 00:14:55,403
Take it! Ball's yours!

359
00:14:57,470 --> 00:14:58,803
Going out to Onishi!

360
00:14:59,270 --> 00:15:00,637
High ball outside. One, two!

361
00:15:02,637 --> 00:15:04,603
(Failed to block)

362
00:15:05,070 --> 00:15:07,470
They need to be closer to the seam!

363
00:15:08,403 --> 00:15:10,503
Yeon Joo, one more!

364
00:15:11,503 --> 00:15:13,470
- She is lethal out on that wing.
- Absolutely.

365
00:15:14,370 --> 00:15:16,103
(Satisfied)

366
00:15:17,370 --> 00:15:19,437
(Tied again)

367
00:15:22,070 --> 00:15:23,070
Mine!

368
00:15:23,937 --> 00:15:24,937
Good pass!

369
00:15:26,570 --> 00:15:27,670
Yeon Joo!

370
00:15:27,670 --> 00:15:28,970
(With ease)

371
00:15:30,903 --> 00:15:33,871
Big swing, great touch on defense!
Clean second touch!

372
00:15:35,137 --> 00:15:37,003
(Shujitsu's free ball)

373
00:15:37,703 --> 00:15:39,237
(To Onishi this time)

374
00:15:41,603 --> 00:15:42,670
Barely rolls it over!

375
00:15:44,837 --> 00:15:45,903
(Her push is blocked again.)

376
00:15:45,903 --> 00:15:46,937
Stay composed!

377
00:15:47,370 --> 00:15:48,403
Yeon Joo!

378
00:15:50,003 --> 00:15:51,103
Yeon Joo tips to the open floor!

379
00:15:51,103 --> 00:15:52,103
(An impenetrable defense)

380
00:15:52,103 --> 00:15:54,437
(Straight to Onishi)

381
00:15:54,703 --> 00:15:56,803
Stay composed! One, two!

382
00:15:57,270 --> 00:15:58,437
Spike! Roofed at the net!

383
00:15:58,903 --> 00:16:01,037
Going right back to her! One, two!

384
00:16:04,703 --> 00:16:06,470
Spike! Tools the block!

385
00:16:06,470 --> 00:16:07,637
(Block touch out)

386
00:16:08,203 --> 00:16:09,437
Your hands split!

387
00:16:09,837 --> 00:16:11,037
They keep spreading their hands.

388
00:16:12,203 --> 00:16:13,237
Wiped it right off your hands!

389
00:16:14,970 --> 00:16:16,003
(The game continues.)

390
00:16:16,003 --> 00:16:17,737
- Off the dig! Free ball!
- Transition!

391
00:16:19,803 --> 00:16:23,003
Pipe attack! Sails out!

392
00:16:23,003 --> 00:16:24,503
(Out)

393
00:16:25,070 --> 00:16:27,803
We can't let them go on a run here.

394
00:16:28,470 --> 00:16:30,203
They have to stay sharp in this rotation.

395
00:16:31,103 --> 00:16:33,270
They claw right back
every time we pull ahead.

396
00:16:33,270 --> 00:16:34,503
Go again!

397
00:16:34,503 --> 00:16:35,570
(Shujitsu pulls away again.)

398
00:16:35,770 --> 00:16:38,937
Team, if we don't convert
our block-and-digs, we don't win this set!

399
00:16:39,103 --> 00:16:41,437
We can't win without solid block defense!

400
00:16:41,770 --> 00:16:44,903
Bo Been, your block timing
is everything right now!

401
00:16:44,970 --> 00:16:47,103
- Seal your hands, don't leave a gap!
- Yes, Coach!

402
00:16:47,470 --> 00:16:48,870
Block and dig!

403
00:16:48,870 --> 00:16:51,070
Keep them tight.
Don't let your arms drift!

404
00:16:53,403 --> 00:16:56,370
(Third set, Shujitsu High 13:
Wonder Dogs 13)

405
00:16:59,470 --> 00:17:00,770
Shaky first pass. Scramble set!

406
00:17:01,737 --> 00:17:04,370
High out-of-system ball. Don't rush!

407
00:17:07,570 --> 00:17:09,170
Slow your approach!

408
00:17:10,670 --> 00:17:13,237
- Set it high!
- Controlled!

409
00:17:13,370 --> 00:17:14,937
- Kept alive! Yeon Joo!
- Yeon Joo!

410
00:17:15,003 --> 00:17:16,037
Big swing!

411
00:17:17,670 --> 00:17:18,703
Out to Onishi!

412
00:17:18,703 --> 00:17:20,903
Delay the jump!

413
00:17:22,103 --> 00:17:23,103
Roofed!

414
00:17:23,203 --> 00:17:24,670
There!

415
00:17:24,803 --> 00:17:25,837
Cover, cover!

416
00:17:25,837 --> 00:17:27,770
Onishi calling for the set again!

417
00:17:27,770 --> 00:17:28,803
One, two!

418
00:17:31,337 --> 00:17:32,603
(Got through!)

419
00:17:35,070 --> 00:17:36,103
Hard cross!

420
00:17:37,503 --> 00:17:38,903
(Chae Rim's super dig)

421
00:17:39,603 --> 00:17:41,203
(But it's Shujitsu's free ball.)

422
00:17:42,437 --> 00:17:43,503
Watch number five!

423
00:17:44,103 --> 00:17:45,970
Shut down in the middle!

424
00:17:45,970 --> 00:17:47,003
What a save!

425
00:17:47,003 --> 00:17:48,570
There it is!

426
00:17:49,137 --> 00:17:50,137
Chae Rim, let's go!

427
00:17:50,137 --> 00:17:51,137
(Our turn now.)

428
00:17:51,138 --> 00:17:52,774
- Drive it deeper. Got it?
- Yes.

429
00:17:55,453 --> 00:17:57,453
A crushing spike!

430
00:17:57,819 --> 00:17:58,929
The Wonder Dogs score!

431
00:18:00,186 --> 00:18:01,186
Thank you!

432
00:18:02,086 --> 00:18:03,319
That's it!

433
00:18:03,686 --> 00:18:06,653
(Applauding)

434
00:18:06,653 --> 00:18:08,086
Wonder Dogs lead, 14 to 13!

435
00:18:08,519 --> 00:18:09,919
The Wonder Dogs reclaim the lead.

436
00:18:09,920 --> 00:18:11,897
(Clapping)

437
00:18:12,786 --> 00:18:15,186
(Right there at every crucial moment)

438
00:18:15,919 --> 00:18:17,719
(Backing them up from the sidelines)

439
00:18:18,453 --> 00:18:20,286
(Kim Yeon Koung, their seventh player)

440
00:18:20,853 --> 00:18:21,953
Nice block.

441
00:18:21,953 --> 00:18:24,786
Great timing!

442
00:18:26,019 --> 00:18:27,686
Block and dig!

443
00:18:34,919 --> 00:18:36,286
Watch your timing!

444
00:18:36,686 --> 00:18:38,053
In 1, 2...

445
00:18:38,053 --> 00:18:38,886
Onishi!

446
00:18:40,186 --> 00:18:42,719
There you go!

447
00:18:42,719 --> 00:18:45,386
Stuffed!

448
00:18:45,386 --> 00:18:47,219
And they score off the block!

449
00:18:47,219 --> 00:18:48,819
What a monster block!

450
00:18:49,653 --> 00:18:52,286
There you go!

451
00:18:58,353 --> 00:19:05,553
(Bo Been's family is out in full force!)

452
00:19:09,019 --> 00:19:10,753
(Overwhelmed with joy)

453
00:19:10,753 --> 00:19:11,553
(Trying not to squeal)

454
00:19:11,719 --> 00:19:12,753
Kim Bo Been the Light!

455
00:19:13,886 --> 00:19:14,853
She's shining bright!

456
00:19:15,486 --> 00:19:16,919
Bo Been puts it away with a block!

457
00:19:16,919 --> 00:19:17,919
Wonder Dogs up, 15 to 13.

458
00:19:17,919 --> 00:19:20,386
(Dazzling Bo Been lights up the court.)

459
00:19:20,753 --> 00:19:22,119
(The match continues.)

460
00:19:23,386 --> 00:19:25,019
Here comes Bo Been!

461
00:19:25,019 --> 00:19:26,386
That's it.

462
00:19:29,219 --> 00:19:31,953
- Hammered on a quick attack!
- There you go!

463
00:19:31,953 --> 00:19:34,453
There you go!

464
00:19:35,353 --> 00:19:36,919
(Gulping)

465
00:19:38,119 --> 00:19:38,953
(The momentum has shifted.)

466
00:19:38,953 --> 00:19:40,853
Great execution!

467
00:19:40,853 --> 00:19:41,819
Bo Been scores on the quick!

468
00:19:41,819 --> 00:19:43,019
Now 16 to 15.

469
00:19:43,853 --> 00:19:45,553
(The match continues.)

470
00:19:48,453 --> 00:19:49,286
Big swing!

471
00:19:49,286 --> 00:19:50,453
Chae Rim pops it up!

472
00:19:50,453 --> 00:19:51,853
- Go, that's it!
- That's right!

473
00:19:54,553 --> 00:19:55,453
She pushes it over.

474
00:19:57,453 --> 00:19:58,453
Handled by Yoshimoto.

475
00:19:58,853 --> 00:20:00,319
Close the gap!

476
00:20:04,453 --> 00:20:07,319
Another roof at the net!

477
00:20:07,319 --> 00:20:08,819
Bo Been with the stuff block!

478
00:20:09,286 --> 00:20:10,986
That's it, Bo Been!

479
00:20:12,219 --> 00:20:13,553
See? You can do it!

480
00:20:14,619 --> 00:20:16,619
Bo Been is dominating...

481
00:20:16,619 --> 00:20:19,286
both on the block and out of the middle.

482
00:20:19,286 --> 00:20:20,886
And it's not just her offense.

483
00:20:20,886 --> 00:20:23,219
She's reading the hitters so well
right now.

484
00:20:23,886 --> 00:20:27,119
She's playing so well you'd think
she's been doing this all season.

485
00:20:27,119 --> 00:20:28,586
She's been phenomenal today.

486
00:20:28,586 --> 00:20:29,486
Absolutely.

487
00:20:29,819 --> 00:20:30,719
Nice job.

488
00:20:31,053 --> 00:20:31,886
Thanks.

489
00:20:31,886 --> 00:20:34,086
(Third set, Shujitsu High 16:
Wonder Dogs 19)

490
00:20:35,686 --> 00:20:36,586
Heavy swing!

491
00:20:36,586 --> 00:20:37,353
Great dig!

492
00:20:37,353 --> 00:20:38,786
Feed Bo Been! That's it!

493
00:20:38,986 --> 00:20:39,886
Run!

494
00:20:40,619 --> 00:20:41,586
(Sprinting over)

495
00:20:41,586 --> 00:20:42,453
Swing!

496
00:20:42,453 --> 00:20:43,519
Here comes the transition attack!

497
00:20:43,519 --> 00:20:44,786
Slide attack behind the setter!

498
00:20:44,786 --> 00:20:45,786
(A point off the slide attack)

499
00:20:45,786 --> 00:20:47,453
She puts it away!

500
00:20:47,453 --> 00:20:48,386
Kim Bo Been the Light!

501
00:20:48,919 --> 00:20:49,953
Let's go!

502
00:20:54,586 --> 00:20:58,653
- Bo Been!
- Bo Been!

503
00:20:59,719 --> 00:21:03,353
(A four-point lead)

504
00:21:06,086 --> 00:21:07,253
Timeout!

505
00:21:08,753 --> 00:21:09,786
(Shujitsu High calls a timeout.)

506
00:21:09,786 --> 00:21:12,186
Timeout called by Shujitsu High.

507
00:21:27,986 --> 00:21:29,153
Stay locked in.

508
00:21:29,919 --> 00:21:31,886
We're giving away
too many unforced errors.

509
00:21:31,886 --> 00:21:33,719
Serve receive, defensive coverage.

510
00:21:33,719 --> 00:21:35,086
We're handing them free points out there.

511
00:21:35,086 --> 00:21:36,719
I told you to stay alert.

512
00:21:36,719 --> 00:21:39,386
Clean up those unforced errors.

513
00:21:40,419 --> 00:21:42,186
Keep that in mind.

514
00:21:42,186 --> 00:21:44,986
We're letting scoring chances slip away.
We need to capitalize.

515
00:21:44,986 --> 00:21:46,819
Execute with precision.

516
00:21:47,619 --> 00:21:49,619
Target number three on the serve.

517
00:21:50,153 --> 00:21:52,286
Keep putting pressure on the serve.

518
00:21:54,153 --> 00:21:55,519
And don't back down.

519
00:22:00,319 --> 00:22:01,419
Let's go!

520
00:22:01,419 --> 00:22:03,053
Let's get this side-out!

521
00:22:04,353 --> 00:22:05,486
The Wonder Dogs lead 21-18.

522
00:22:07,086 --> 00:22:08,819
(Kato Uta serves.)

523
00:22:09,519 --> 00:22:10,519
Just like that.

524
00:22:17,586 --> 00:22:19,019
Chae Rim.

525
00:22:23,419 --> 00:22:24,753
(A quiet word about the game plan)

526
00:22:24,753 --> 00:22:25,919
Got it.

527
00:22:32,053 --> 00:22:33,053
Swing!

528
00:22:34,553 --> 00:22:35,519
Enkhsoyol!

529
00:22:36,586 --> 00:22:37,486
Swing through!

530
00:22:38,619 --> 00:22:39,619
Mine!

531
00:22:39,619 --> 00:22:41,419
(Chae Rim keeps the ball alive.)

532
00:22:41,653 --> 00:22:42,486
That's it.

533
00:22:45,119 --> 00:22:45,986
Bump set!

534
00:22:45,986 --> 00:22:47,319
Drive it deep!

535
00:22:47,686 --> 00:22:48,686
Swing!

536
00:22:49,286 --> 00:22:50,353
She unloads from the outside!

537
00:22:50,353 --> 00:22:51,386
Dug up in the back row!

538
00:22:53,753 --> 00:22:54,586
Heavy swing!

539
00:22:56,553 --> 00:22:57,453
That's it!

540
00:22:58,153 --> 00:22:59,586
Chae Rim with the dig on the left!

541
00:23:00,753 --> 00:23:02,053
(Great defense creates...)

542
00:23:03,186 --> 00:23:04,386
(a great chance to attack.)

543
00:23:04,386 --> 00:23:05,253
Push it deep!

544
00:23:06,586 --> 00:23:07,619
Nice cut!

545
00:23:07,619 --> 00:23:10,119
Enkhsoyol puts it down!

546
00:23:10,119 --> 00:23:13,586
That's how you do it! Great work!

547
00:23:17,786 --> 00:23:18,786
Chae Rim.

548
00:23:19,286 --> 00:23:20,153
Great job.

549
00:23:23,119 --> 00:23:24,286
(The secret game plan revealed)

550
00:23:24,286 --> 00:23:25,619
Enkhsoyol is not perfect with receptions.

551
00:23:25,619 --> 00:23:27,626
If she gets targeted on serve,
slide over and cover for her.

552
00:23:28,819 --> 00:23:31,986
Chae Rim showed
incredible ball control there.

553
00:23:31,986 --> 00:23:34,853
This has always been
the identity of the Wonder Dogs.

554
00:23:34,853 --> 00:23:36,519
- Exactly.
- Scrapping for every loose ball...

555
00:23:36,519 --> 00:23:37,519
and refusing to let it drop.

556
00:23:37,858 --> 00:23:39,758
That's the brand of volleyball
they need to play.

557
00:23:39,759 --> 00:23:40,739
Without a doubt.

558
00:23:43,319 --> 00:23:45,186
Prepare for the block.

559
00:23:45,186 --> 00:23:46,486
Dial in your timing.

560
00:23:46,953 --> 00:23:49,519
Enkhsoyol, press your hands across!

561
00:23:49,519 --> 00:23:50,853
Time your jump!

562
00:23:50,853 --> 00:23:51,786
(Still drilling them on blocking)

563
00:23:51,786 --> 00:23:52,786
It's 22 to 18.

564
00:23:53,186 --> 00:23:54,886
(Hyo Rim serves.)

565
00:23:57,286 --> 00:23:58,086
Right side!

566
00:23:59,953 --> 00:24:01,053
One, two!

567
00:24:01,486 --> 00:24:02,953
Roofed! Shut down at the net.

568
00:24:03,786 --> 00:24:04,619
Going right back to the pin.

569
00:24:05,153 --> 00:24:06,019
One, two.

570
00:24:06,786 --> 00:24:07,586
Big swing!

571
00:24:08,086 --> 00:24:09,553
Yeon Joo gets a hand under it.

572
00:24:10,453 --> 00:24:11,386
(The ball...)

573
00:24:11,386 --> 00:24:12,319
(goes to Enkhsoyol.)

574
00:24:12,319 --> 00:24:13,086
Deep!

575
00:24:15,386 --> 00:24:16,486
You've got to take a full swing!

576
00:24:17,086 --> 00:24:19,053
Enkhsoyol gets just a fingertip on it!

577
00:24:19,053 --> 00:24:20,886
And it drops right into no man's land!

578
00:24:21,919 --> 00:24:23,153
Are you kidding me?

579
00:24:23,919 --> 00:24:25,386
Why did you leave the floor so early?

580
00:24:25,386 --> 00:24:26,319
(That was way too close!)

581
00:24:26,319 --> 00:24:27,853
Didn't catch any of it cleanly.

582
00:24:27,853 --> 00:24:28,819
(As if nothing happened)

583
00:24:29,219 --> 00:24:31,619
(An incredulous smile)

584
00:24:31,619 --> 00:24:34,919
She barely got a piece of that ball.

585
00:24:36,819 --> 00:24:38,953
Literally touched it with her fingernails.

586
00:24:39,419 --> 00:24:40,986
By the time her hands came through,

587
00:24:40,986 --> 00:24:42,486
the ball was practically behind her.

588
00:24:42,819 --> 00:24:44,086
(Startled)

589
00:24:44,086 --> 00:24:45,219
(Playing it cool)

590
00:24:47,219 --> 00:24:50,386
(A lucky point that scared everyone)

591
00:24:51,986 --> 00:24:53,353
(A point's a point!)

592
00:24:53,353 --> 00:24:54,486
We'll gladly take it.

593
00:24:55,519 --> 00:24:56,586
Now 23 to 18.

594
00:24:56,586 --> 00:24:57,919
Wonder Dogs up by five.

595
00:24:59,686 --> 00:25:02,686
(What a headache!)

596
00:25:05,786 --> 00:25:07,853
Right side!

597
00:25:07,853 --> 00:25:08,719
Got it!

598
00:25:09,353 --> 00:25:10,619
One ball at a time!

599
00:25:12,619 --> 00:25:13,486
Right side!

600
00:25:13,486 --> 00:25:16,719
(Bringing in Yoshimoto cannon
on the right)

601
00:25:21,886 --> 00:25:23,053
Right side!

602
00:25:23,586 --> 00:25:25,186
(Yoshimoto steps up as planned.)

603
00:25:25,486 --> 00:25:26,819
One, two.

604
00:25:27,486 --> 00:25:29,286
(Three!)

605
00:25:29,986 --> 00:25:31,119
Spike!

606
00:25:31,119 --> 00:25:32,353
Yoshimoto Kanade!

607
00:25:35,286 --> 00:25:37,819
(A formidable attacking duo)

608
00:25:37,819 --> 00:25:38,586
That's it!

609
00:25:40,519 --> 00:25:41,686
Shake it off.

610
00:25:42,753 --> 00:25:43,853
Now 23 to 19.

611
00:25:47,386 --> 00:25:48,286
Overhand set.

612
00:25:49,986 --> 00:25:50,953
Quick push into the middle!

613
00:25:50,953 --> 00:25:51,986
The seam is wide open on the left!

614
00:25:52,953 --> 00:25:53,919
(Their last hope is a block.)

615
00:25:53,919 --> 00:25:55,019
One, two.

616
00:25:55,019 --> 00:25:56,053
Spike!

617
00:25:56,053 --> 00:25:59,019
(Another failed block)

618
00:25:59,819 --> 00:26:01,619
You're still jumping too early!

619
00:26:01,619 --> 00:26:04,319
Watch their approach! Delay your jump!

620
00:26:04,319 --> 00:26:06,953
They just have no answer...

621
00:26:06,953 --> 00:26:09,119
- for Uchida Riona on the attack.
- Exactly.

622
00:26:09,119 --> 00:26:11,919
Just two more points!

623
00:26:12,919 --> 00:26:15,419
(Shujitsu is closing the gap.)

624
00:26:16,319 --> 00:26:18,586
(They can't let Shujitsu get any closer.)

625
00:26:19,086 --> 00:26:22,186
Solo block on this pin. Just you, Minato!

626
00:26:22,186 --> 00:26:23,019
Got it!

627
00:26:23,786 --> 00:26:24,686
Let's close the gap!

628
00:26:29,753 --> 00:26:31,186
Yoshimoto Kanade back to serve.

629
00:26:32,253 --> 00:26:33,353
Short serve!

630
00:26:33,653 --> 00:26:34,553
Clean pass!

631
00:26:35,186 --> 00:26:36,686
(A solo block, just as instructed)

632
00:26:36,686 --> 00:26:37,553
You've got this, Yeon Joo!

633
00:26:37,886 --> 00:26:38,919
Yeon Joo!

634
00:26:42,786 --> 00:26:44,319
Roofed on the pin!

635
00:26:45,453 --> 00:26:47,653
(Roaring in triumph)

636
00:26:47,886 --> 00:26:48,853
That's what I'm talking about!

637
00:26:53,886 --> 00:26:55,519
(Deflated)

638
00:26:57,153 --> 00:27:00,919
(Shut down by a solo block)

639
00:27:01,519 --> 00:27:03,453
Run it back.

640
00:27:03,453 --> 00:27:05,119
Onishi, take the line by yourself!

641
00:27:08,353 --> 00:27:10,586
That one stung.

642
00:27:11,486 --> 00:27:12,619
I can't stand losing.

643
00:27:12,853 --> 00:27:14,163
I was determined to put that ball away.

644
00:27:23,919 --> 00:27:25,253
Swing! Run it fast!

645
00:27:25,253 --> 00:27:26,686
(An easy ball sent over)

646
00:27:26,686 --> 00:27:27,586
Set the outside!

647
00:27:28,319 --> 00:27:29,453
(Inching toward the net)

648
00:27:31,053 --> 00:27:32,386
(Onishi moves in.)

649
00:27:32,386 --> 00:27:33,219
One, two.

650
00:27:33,619 --> 00:27:34,819
(Three!)

651
00:27:36,186 --> 00:27:38,653
- Spike!
- Nice touch, Yeon Joo!

652
00:27:40,786 --> 00:27:43,419
(That's how it's done!)

653
00:27:44,553 --> 00:27:45,953
She pays her right back!

654
00:27:45,953 --> 00:27:48,019
What an answer! What a statement!

655
00:27:48,019 --> 00:27:49,619
Yeon Joo comes right back
with a monster stuff block!

656
00:27:49,619 --> 00:27:50,953
(A solo block answered with another)

657
00:27:50,953 --> 00:27:52,153
Yeon Joo!

658
00:27:53,889 --> 00:27:55,556
- Hwang Yeon Joo!
- Hwang Yeon Joo!

659
00:27:56,205 --> 00:27:58,573
(A bitter return)

660
00:27:58,621 --> 00:27:59,955
Wonder Dogs lead 24 to 21!

661
00:27:59,956 --> 00:28:01,456
(Third set, Shujitsu High 21:
Wonder Dogs 24)

662
00:28:01,457 --> 00:28:02,924
Wonder Dogs' set point.

663
00:28:02,925 --> 00:28:05,160
(Third set, Shujitsu High 21:
Wonder Dogs 24)

664
00:28:05,361 --> 00:28:06,428
Let's go!

665
00:28:06,429 --> 00:28:08,096
This is our moment!

666
00:28:08,097 --> 00:28:08,997
(One more point to go.)

667
00:28:08,998 --> 00:28:11,933
I refuse to live
through that heartbreak again.

668
00:28:13,035 --> 00:28:15,804
(The day we let victory
slip through our fingers)

669
00:28:15,805 --> 00:28:17,839
We came up so agonizingly short last time.

670
00:28:18,273 --> 00:28:21,042
That was never a match
we should have let slip away.

671
00:28:22,211 --> 00:28:25,113
(They waited a year for this.)

672
00:28:25,881 --> 00:28:27,181
For an entire year...

673
00:28:27,784 --> 00:28:29,884
all I could think about
was getting our revenge.

674
00:28:31,253 --> 00:28:33,421
Let's take this third set and get it done.

675
00:28:34,924 --> 00:28:36,224
I want this win so badly.

676
00:28:42,765 --> 00:28:43,765
Get inside!

677
00:28:45,068 --> 00:28:46,331
They are going to the right!

678
00:28:47,436 --> 00:28:48,302
Chae Rim!

679
00:28:48,303 --> 00:28:49,158
(Single-block threat)

680
00:28:49,505 --> 00:28:51,072
Right now!

681
00:28:51,073 --> 00:28:51,940
Back Chae Rim!

682
00:28:51,941 --> 00:28:53,575
That was all on me here.

683
00:28:54,401 --> 00:28:55,867
(Attack comes from Uchida.)

684
00:28:55,911 --> 00:28:57,578
One, two...

685
00:28:57,579 --> 00:28:58,279
(Cheering)

686
00:29:06,655 --> 00:29:07,521
There it is!

687
00:29:07,623 --> 00:29:08,590
Yes!

688
00:29:08,591 --> 00:29:12,060
Roofed at the net!

689
00:29:12,761 --> 00:29:14,562
(We won!)

690
00:29:15,631 --> 00:29:17,899
Wonder Dogs take the third set!

691
00:29:17,900 --> 00:29:18,833
(Cheering)

692
00:29:23,239 --> 00:29:24,439
That's it!

693
00:29:24,774 --> 00:29:26,595
What an incredible feeling.

694
00:29:27,877 --> 00:29:31,046
Somewhere in the middle of that third set,
I actually started having fun out there.

695
00:29:31,646 --> 00:29:32,970
I reminded myself,
"The job's not done yet."

696
00:29:33,383 --> 00:29:36,217
Let's carry this fire
straight into the fourth.

697
00:29:36,819 --> 00:29:38,620
(Let's get on the vibe!)

698
00:29:39,722 --> 00:29:41,956
(Joy ahoy)

699
00:29:45,894 --> 00:29:47,862
(Quietly returning to his position)

700
00:29:50,065 --> 00:29:52,099
(Disappointed gesture?)

701
00:29:52,801 --> 00:29:55,236
(No, she's just picking up the ball.)

702
00:29:56,372 --> 00:29:58,740
(What was the first thing that came
to your mind after the first victory?)

703
00:29:58,874 --> 00:30:00,007
We got the set,

704
00:30:01,043 --> 00:30:02,944
but there's no time to celebrate.

705
00:30:03,479 --> 00:30:05,180
We have to step right into set four.

706
00:30:05,581 --> 00:30:06,748
The real battle starts now.

707
00:30:07,616 --> 00:30:10,785
(Strategy meeting for the fourth set)

708
00:30:11,020 --> 00:30:15,790
What do you think made the difference
compared to the earlier sets?

709
00:30:15,791 --> 00:30:16,824
- Our block discipline.
- The block.

710
00:30:16,825 --> 00:30:19,427
Exactly,
our blocking completely transformed.

711
00:30:19,428 --> 00:30:21,662
And we stopped giving
away free unforced errors.

712
00:30:21,663 --> 00:30:23,230
That turned the whole set around.

713
00:30:23,999 --> 00:30:25,933
We have to stay locked in
on our block-and-dig game.

714
00:30:25,934 --> 00:30:27,001
Expect every rally
to take multiple swings.

715
00:30:27,002 --> 00:30:28,202
Their floor defense is incredible.

716
00:30:28,203 --> 00:30:29,670
All you need to do is reset
and plan your next approach.

717
00:30:29,671 --> 00:30:32,173
"Next time, I'll hit that seam."

718
00:30:32,275 --> 00:30:33,709
Keep your mindset that simple.

719
00:30:33,710 --> 00:30:35,277
- Understood!
- Then it'll be just fine.

720
00:30:35,278 --> 00:30:36,212
Got it!

721
00:30:36,213 --> 00:30:38,247
Everything flows so much better
when we establish an early lead.

722
00:30:38,248 --> 00:30:40,149
Let's jump on them early and
trade side-outs to close this out.

723
00:30:40,150 --> 00:30:40,982
Yes!

724
00:30:41,216 --> 00:30:42,249
Stay one step ahead
in your decision-making.

725
00:30:42,250 --> 00:30:43,250
Leave everything on the floor!

726
00:30:43,652 --> 00:30:46,254
(Meanwhile in Shujitsu)

727
00:30:55,462 --> 00:30:59,165
Well, keep playing like that
right into the fifth set.

728
00:31:01,772 --> 00:31:03,873
Our attack angles have
become completely predictable.

729
00:31:04,174 --> 00:31:07,410
Go back to the variety you had in
the first set. Use your heads out there.

730
00:31:07,411 --> 00:31:09,345
If you just mindlessly swing,
they're going to roof you every time.

731
00:31:09,346 --> 00:31:11,380
Change up your tempo and attack rhythm.

732
00:31:15,724 --> 00:31:18,626
The Wonder Dogs pull off
a dramatic comeback to win the third set.

733
00:31:18,627 --> 00:31:21,162
Now the real match begins.

734
00:31:21,163 --> 00:31:22,129
(Set score, 2:1)

735
00:31:22,130 --> 00:31:23,097
I'll do the same.

736
00:31:27,235 --> 00:31:28,168
Locked in!

737
00:31:29,437 --> 00:31:31,204
(Fourth set, Shujitsu High 0:
Wonder Dogs 0)

738
00:31:31,573 --> 00:31:33,741
Fourth set gets underway
with Kato Uta back to serve.

739
00:31:35,377 --> 00:31:36,344
Enkhsoyol!

740
00:31:37,746 --> 00:31:38,679
Heavy swing!

741
00:31:39,180 --> 00:31:40,447
(Long bounce)

742
00:31:41,282 --> 00:31:43,183
(Breaking down)

743
00:31:43,184 --> 00:31:44,484
Overpass coming back!

744
00:31:45,253 --> 00:31:46,954
Yeon Joo!

745
00:31:49,457 --> 00:31:51,191
Yeon Joo scores!

746
00:31:51,426 --> 00:31:52,359
There it is!

747
00:31:52,360 --> 00:31:54,495
(Hits an opening)

748
00:31:54,496 --> 00:31:56,864
(Go, auntie!)

749
00:31:58,466 --> 00:32:02,202
(Fourth set, Shujitsu High 0:
Wonder Dogs 1)

750
00:32:03,004 --> 00:32:04,037
Enkhsoyol to serve.

751
00:32:07,742 --> 00:32:09,543
(Shaky reception)

752
00:32:10,612 --> 00:32:11,478
Tip.

753
00:32:12,081 --> 00:32:14,259
- Dives and pops it up!
- Yeon Joo.

754
00:32:14,716 --> 00:32:15,549
Heavy swing!

755
00:32:15,550 --> 00:32:16,617
(Yeon Joo's spike)

756
00:32:17,886 --> 00:32:18,853
Shifting to the right pin!

757
00:32:19,754 --> 00:32:20,754
Tipped over!

758
00:32:21,189 --> 00:32:22,189
She digs it up!

759
00:32:22,457 --> 00:32:23,390
Go, Yeon Joo!

760
00:32:25,393 --> 00:32:26,226
Drive it deep to the corner!

761
00:32:26,227 --> 00:32:27,661
They keep it alive and send it over.

762
00:32:27,829 --> 00:32:29,596
(Quickly getting back to position)

763
00:32:31,499 --> 00:32:32,632
One, two...

764
00:32:33,835 --> 00:32:34,868
(Touch)

765
00:32:34,937 --> 00:32:37,204
Yoshimoto Kanade puts it down!

766
00:32:37,205 --> 00:32:39,473
Please, out! Oh.

767
00:32:39,474 --> 00:32:40,441
(Clapping)

768
00:32:40,442 --> 00:32:43,010
It's okay. We can make the next point.

769
00:32:44,212 --> 00:32:45,979
(Yoshimoto serves.)

770
00:32:47,148 --> 00:32:49,216
Her ball is not that fast.

771
00:32:49,951 --> 00:32:51,552
Pass it high!

772
00:32:52,554 --> 00:32:53,387
Hyo Rim sets!

773
00:32:53,655 --> 00:32:54,521
There we go!

774
00:32:54,956 --> 00:32:55,756
Hwang Yeon Joo!

775
00:32:59,394 --> 00:33:01,695
(The chance goes to Onishi.)

776
00:33:01,830 --> 00:33:03,097
Full swing!

777
00:33:03,098 --> 00:33:05,166
(Onishi scores with a strong swing.)

778
00:33:06,468 --> 00:33:07,668
Onishi hammers it down!

779
00:33:07,669 --> 00:33:09,436
(The world's next top player never tires.)

780
00:33:09,871 --> 00:33:12,439
(Sigh)

781
00:33:12,440 --> 00:33:15,075
- Reset your base!
- Shujitsu leads 3 to 1.

782
00:33:16,044 --> 00:33:18,412
We can't let them open up a run here.

783
00:33:21,683 --> 00:33:22,549
Hwang Yeon Joo!

784
00:33:22,550 --> 00:33:23,917
Put it away!

785
00:33:23,918 --> 00:33:25,218
Through the middle!

786
00:33:25,219 --> 00:33:26,987
(It comes to the middle.)

787
00:33:26,989 --> 00:33:28,321
They save the ball.

788
00:33:28,322 --> 00:33:29,456
(Successful defense)

789
00:33:29,724 --> 00:33:31,291
Transition counter out on the left!

790
00:33:31,292 --> 00:33:32,292
(Blocked)

791
00:33:34,048 --> 00:33:35,481
Yeon Joo covers the block rebound!

792
00:33:35,482 --> 00:33:36,776
(Fierce rally continues.)

793
00:33:37,132 --> 00:33:37,965
Run it!

794
00:33:37,966 --> 00:33:40,868
Crossed over to the other side.
Outside pin again! Covered!

795
00:33:41,069 --> 00:33:42,302
Where is Hyo Rim setting?

796
00:33:42,303 --> 00:33:43,637
Back to the left! Spike!

797
00:33:44,372 --> 00:33:45,972
(Ironclad defense)

798
00:33:45,973 --> 00:33:47,074
Not an inch of daylight.

799
00:33:47,075 --> 00:33:48,141
Mine!

800
00:33:48,142 --> 00:33:49,276
(Free ball)

801
00:33:49,277 --> 00:33:50,109
Pass it clean!

802
00:33:50,511 --> 00:33:54,347
(I must, this time!)

803
00:33:58,653 --> 00:33:59,853
Back to Hwang Yeon Joo again!

804
00:33:59,854 --> 00:34:01,317
Spike!

805
00:34:01,318 --> 00:34:03,511
(Hits right in the open space)

806
00:34:03,891 --> 00:34:05,258
(Shout out to Hwang Yeon Joo!)

807
00:34:05,259 --> 00:34:06,693
Incredible.

808
00:34:07,162 --> 00:34:10,298
The veteran bails the team out
after a grueling marathon rally!

809
00:34:10,299 --> 00:34:12,399
- I'm just speechless in awe.
- Indeed.

810
00:34:13,968 --> 00:34:17,370
Even without getting
full vertical on her jump,

811
00:34:17,371 --> 00:34:19,005
she relies entirely on craft
and placement to find the floor.

812
00:34:19,340 --> 00:34:20,473
It really is breathtaking.

813
00:34:20,642 --> 00:34:23,477
(At the moment of impact,
she turns her body to attack.)

814
00:34:24,212 --> 00:34:26,547
Just like that!

815
00:34:26,814 --> 00:34:29,015
(Fourth set, Shujitsu High 3:
Wonder Dogs 2)

816
00:34:29,918 --> 00:34:31,251
Ho Bin back to serve.

817
00:34:31,252 --> 00:34:32,552
(Ho Bin's serve)

818
00:34:36,057 --> 00:34:37,090
Rattled on receive!

819
00:34:37,492 --> 00:34:38,392
One, two!

820
00:34:38,393 --> 00:34:39,359
(Three!)

821
00:34:39,360 --> 00:34:40,661
Huge double block on the right!

822
00:34:42,130 --> 00:34:43,172
They kept it alive!

823
00:34:43,172 --> 00:34:44,431
(A full-body defense)

824
00:34:44,432 --> 00:34:45,299
Transition coming!

825
00:34:45,300 --> 00:34:46,133
(A chance to tie)

826
00:34:46,501 --> 00:34:49,770
(This is where we catch up!)

827
00:34:53,208 --> 00:34:55,676
They read the block beautifully
to create the seam, but...

828
00:34:55,677 --> 00:34:56,710
(Attacking error)

829
00:34:56,878 --> 00:34:57,778
Chae Rim!

830
00:34:57,779 --> 00:34:58,979
(Attacking error)

831
00:34:58,980 --> 00:35:00,414
Chae Rim, you cannot give those away.

832
00:35:00,415 --> 00:35:03,183
Stay calm and hit it deeper.

833
00:35:05,787 --> 00:35:07,221
(Breathing heavily)

834
00:35:09,424 --> 00:35:10,991
(The match continues.)

835
00:35:11,059 --> 00:35:12,189
Attack through the middle.

836
00:35:12,594 --> 00:35:14,128
Watch the tip, roll shot!

837
00:35:14,395 --> 00:35:15,228
What should I do?

838
00:35:15,463 --> 00:35:16,296
Swing through!

839
00:35:19,967 --> 00:35:23,169
(Sigh)

840
00:35:29,344 --> 00:35:31,551
We're giving away too many points
like this.

841
00:35:32,714 --> 00:35:37,083
I kept racking my brain trying
to figure out why we couldn't stabilize.

842
00:35:38,553 --> 00:35:39,686
Shaky pass!

843
00:35:39,988 --> 00:35:41,188
Hyo Rim bump set!

844
00:35:41,823 --> 00:35:43,356
(Continued mistakes)

845
00:35:43,591 --> 00:35:46,026
We can't afford back-to-back errors here.

846
00:35:46,027 --> 00:35:49,095
They've got to clean up
the unforced mistakes.

847
00:35:49,297 --> 00:35:52,699
I could tell
Chae Rim was getting exhausted.

848
00:35:53,601 --> 00:35:55,669
(During last year's match)

849
00:35:56,270 --> 00:35:59,506
(Back Chae Rim played all five sets.)

850
00:36:00,575 --> 00:36:03,810
(Her drop in stamina led
to a comeback defeat.)

851
00:36:03,811 --> 00:36:06,580
Our players' stamina clearly
dipped down the stretch.

852
00:36:06,581 --> 00:36:09,850
You could see the fatigue
creeping into their execution.

853
00:36:10,618 --> 00:36:13,854
I wanted to make a change.

854
00:36:14,323 --> 00:36:15,989
Of course, I noticed it right away.

855
00:36:17,925 --> 00:36:20,860
- Chae Rim is running on fumes.
- She's getting fatigued.

856
00:36:20,861 --> 00:36:22,929
(Chae Rim is getting exhausted again.)

857
00:36:23,131 --> 00:36:25,932
I tried to make an immediate assessment...

858
00:36:25,933 --> 00:36:27,767
of where everyone stood physically.

859
00:36:30,371 --> 00:36:31,204
Ye Eun?

860
00:36:34,842 --> 00:36:36,042
(Calling her)

861
00:36:37,612 --> 00:36:39,189
- Chae Rim.
- We'd like to make a substitution.

862
00:36:39,647 --> 00:36:40,914
Chae Rim!

863
00:36:41,549 --> 00:36:42,816
Let's go!

864
00:36:43,318 --> 00:36:45,719
Back Chae Rim checks out,
Lee Ye Eun checks in.

865
00:36:46,821 --> 00:36:50,290
Regardless of the issue,

866
00:36:50,653 --> 00:36:53,499
I was thinking about substitutions,

867
00:36:53,871 --> 00:36:58,312
so I wanted to make the most
of the players on the bench.

868
00:36:59,879 --> 00:37:03,012
I should've subbed Chae Rim out earlier.

869
00:37:04,312 --> 00:37:08,279
(No more second chances.)

870
00:37:08,546 --> 00:37:09,645
Are you okay, Chae Rim?

871
00:37:09,646 --> 00:37:10,546
I'm fine.

872
00:37:11,279 --> 00:37:12,346
I'm good.

873
00:37:13,885 --> 00:37:16,411
(While Chae Rim takes a break)

874
00:37:16,412 --> 00:37:17,612
There's a short one here.

875
00:37:17,613 --> 00:37:18,911
Watch that area closely, Ye Eun.

876
00:37:18,912 --> 00:37:19,679
Okay.

877
00:37:21,279 --> 00:37:22,554
Miyamoto Rio serves.

878
00:37:22,555 --> 00:37:23,779
(Fourth set, Shujitsu High 8
: Wonder Dogs 5)

879
00:37:26,246 --> 00:37:27,212
Ye Eun receives.

880
00:37:27,679 --> 00:37:28,779
That's it.

881
00:37:29,379 --> 00:37:30,179
Nice pass.

882
00:37:30,779 --> 00:37:31,646
She dives for it.

883
00:37:32,146 --> 00:37:32,946
That's it.

884
00:37:34,612 --> 00:37:35,446
A hard hit down the middle.

885
00:37:35,812 --> 00:37:36,579
She keeps it alive...

886
00:37:36,580 --> 00:37:37,911
- with a rolling dig.
- There you go!

887
00:37:37,912 --> 00:37:38,979
Send it high.

888
00:37:39,112 --> 00:37:40,645
(A high set)

889
00:37:40,646 --> 00:37:41,612
Spike.

890
00:37:41,613 --> 00:37:43,479
- They keep it alive.
- Nice, Mei!

891
00:37:43,779 --> 00:37:45,346
Another chance for Shujitsu.

892
00:37:47,479 --> 00:37:49,178
Great defense against the tip.

893
00:37:49,179 --> 00:37:50,444
Now they need to counterattack.

894
00:37:51,379 --> 00:37:52,945
Spike!

895
00:37:52,946 --> 00:37:54,112
Nice.

896
00:37:56,646 --> 00:37:58,279
Great job.

897
00:37:58,646 --> 00:37:59,946
Nice defense.

898
00:38:00,412 --> 00:38:03,046
This is exactly what Coach Kim was
talking about.

899
00:38:03,579 --> 00:38:05,645
That was some incredible defense.

900
00:38:05,646 --> 00:38:08,345
It gives the attackers confidence, right?

901
00:38:08,346 --> 00:38:11,212
Exactly. It makes the game
so much easier for them.

902
00:38:11,612 --> 00:38:12,978
Without making errors,

903
00:38:12,979 --> 00:38:15,812
the Wonder Dogs kept the rally going
and capitalized on their chances.

904
00:38:16,146 --> 00:38:17,867
Chae Rim, you're going back in.

905
00:38:17,868 --> 00:38:18,679
Get ready.

906
00:38:22,246 --> 00:38:23,146
Nice reception.

907
00:38:24,946 --> 00:38:25,846
Spike.

908
00:38:26,446 --> 00:38:27,712
That's defended.

909
00:38:31,046 --> 00:38:32,412
Great coverage on the tip.

910
00:38:33,612 --> 00:38:34,379
Here we go again.

911
00:38:35,312 --> 00:38:36,911
Enkhsoyol!

912
00:38:36,912 --> 00:38:37,846
Enkhsoyol scores.

913
00:38:37,846 --> 00:38:38,670
That's right.

914
00:38:38,694 --> 00:38:39,886
(Another successful attack)

915
00:38:40,179 --> 00:38:42,111
Well done, Enkhsoyol.

916
00:38:42,112 --> 00:38:43,946
(Their offense is coming back to life.)

917
00:38:44,612 --> 00:38:47,211
The cheers are getting louder.

918
00:38:47,212 --> 00:38:48,878
I hope things keep going their way.

919
00:38:48,879 --> 00:38:50,846
They need to keep pushing now.

920
00:38:53,312 --> 00:38:58,079
(The opportunity is coming.)

921
00:38:58,312 --> 00:39:00,779
Chae Rim.

922
00:39:01,179 --> 00:39:02,046
Sub her in.

923
00:39:03,279 --> 00:39:04,411
Ye Eun comes off,

924
00:39:04,412 --> 00:39:05,812
and Chae Rim is back on the court.

925
00:39:06,079 --> 00:39:08,212
(The experienced coach is
making quicker substitutions.)

926
00:39:08,512 --> 00:39:11,645
Chae Rim should've had
some time to recover.

927
00:39:11,646 --> 00:39:12,546
Chae Rim.

928
00:39:12,779 --> 00:39:14,254
Watch for the ball going past you.

929
00:39:19,046 --> 00:39:20,012
It's short.

930
00:39:21,346 --> 00:39:23,712
(Fully recharged)

931
00:39:23,979 --> 00:39:24,912
Chae Rim receives.

932
00:39:25,212 --> 00:39:26,079
A back set.

933
00:39:27,346 --> 00:39:28,746
(The ball goes to Hwang Yeon Joo.)

934
00:39:30,579 --> 00:39:32,046
Hwang Yeon Joo scores.

935
00:39:35,479 --> 00:39:36,479
Nice set.

936
00:39:36,479 --> 00:39:37,412
Thanks.

937
00:39:39,246 --> 00:39:40,978
(The substitution pays off.)

938
00:39:40,979 --> 00:39:43,478
Chae Rim seems to have found
her rhythm again.

939
00:39:43,479 --> 00:39:44,379
Okay.

940
00:39:44,646 --> 00:39:47,111
Yeon Koung's strategy is working.

941
00:39:47,112 --> 00:39:48,645
(The experienced coach knows
how to handle this.)

942
00:39:48,646 --> 00:39:49,911
It's 10 to 8, a two-point lead.

943
00:39:49,912 --> 00:39:50,879
Ho Bin serves.

944
00:39:52,546 --> 00:39:53,479
The reception is shaky.

945
00:39:54,212 --> 00:39:55,345
They rush the ball toward the middle.

946
00:39:55,346 --> 00:39:56,978
They keep it alive.

947
00:39:56,979 --> 00:39:58,246
Take your time.

948
00:40:00,046 --> 00:40:00,812
A tip.

949
00:40:01,679 --> 00:40:02,446
Left.

950
00:40:02,912 --> 00:40:03,812
She's going left.

951
00:40:04,079 --> 00:40:05,145
The angle is off.

952
00:40:05,146 --> 00:40:06,812
- Out.
- It's out.

953
00:40:08,946 --> 00:40:10,012
Well done.

954
00:40:11,446 --> 00:40:14,411
- Nice job.
- That's okay, Chae Rim.

955
00:40:14,412 --> 00:40:16,179
No room for errors.

956
00:40:16,479 --> 00:40:19,646
Now that the Wonder Dogs are
starting to put on the pressure,

957
00:40:20,046 --> 00:40:22,289
Shujitsu is making mistakes
they weren't making before.

958
00:40:23,579 --> 00:40:24,479
Out past the endline,

959
00:40:24,480 --> 00:40:25,629
now it's a one-point difference.

960
00:40:26,179 --> 00:40:27,612
Watch number two.

961
00:40:28,412 --> 00:40:29,912
It grazed the net on the way over.

962
00:40:30,746 --> 00:40:31,546
Onishi.

963
00:40:35,912 --> 00:40:37,111
- Out.
- It's out!

964
00:40:37,112 --> 00:40:38,179
Out again.

965
00:40:38,712 --> 00:40:39,945
Great.

966
00:40:39,946 --> 00:40:41,279
Let's go.

967
00:40:42,112 --> 00:40:44,279
That's your second error.

968
00:40:45,112 --> 00:40:47,778
Consecutive attacking errors have brought
the score to a tie.

969
00:40:47,779 --> 00:40:49,479
(Fourth set, Shujitsu High 10
: Wonder Dogs 10)

970
00:40:50,379 --> 00:40:53,012
(The momentum has shifted.)

971
00:40:53,912 --> 00:40:56,778
They're going to feel
the pressure now too.

972
00:40:56,779 --> 00:40:58,179
(The game is back to square one.)

973
00:40:59,413 --> 00:41:01,678
That's when I thought
the real game was finally beginning.

974
00:41:03,112 --> 00:41:05,679
Both teams seemed nervous.

975
00:41:06,346 --> 00:41:09,579
There had been so many ridiculous mistakes
and errors.

976
00:41:11,346 --> 00:41:14,278
If we could just cut down
on a few of those,

977
00:41:14,279 --> 00:41:15,809
we'd have a much better chance of winning.

978
00:41:17,879 --> 00:41:20,979
(An experienced coach's move
to eliminate errors)

979
00:41:21,312 --> 00:41:22,746
Min Kyeong, come here.

980
00:41:23,146 --> 00:41:24,211
- Min Kyeong.
- Min Kyeong.

981
00:41:24,212 --> 00:41:25,511
Come on, Min Kyeong.

982
00:41:25,512 --> 00:41:27,278
- Substitution.
- You got this.

983
00:41:27,279 --> 00:41:29,412
(Another substitution)

984
00:41:29,746 --> 00:41:31,178
Send one good serve, do one big block.

985
00:41:31,179 --> 00:41:32,779
One good serve, one good defensive play.

986
00:41:33,179 --> 00:41:34,411
- Nice serve.
- Let's go.

987
00:41:34,412 --> 00:41:35,812
Nice serve.

988
00:41:36,112 --> 00:41:38,102
(During practice
for the game against Shujitsu)

989
00:41:39,212 --> 00:41:41,146
(Nice serve)

990
00:41:41,512 --> 00:41:43,511
(Nice defense)

991
00:41:43,512 --> 00:41:44,379
Great, Min Kyeong.

992
00:41:44,380 --> 00:41:47,745
(Min Kyeong stood out both in serving
and defense.)

993
00:41:47,746 --> 00:41:50,446
The Wonder Dogs bring
Ji Min Kyeong onto the court.

994
00:41:50,912 --> 00:41:51,846
How many times is that?

995
00:41:53,212 --> 00:41:55,545
Two substitutions?

996
00:41:55,546 --> 00:41:57,046
Take it slow.

997
00:41:57,779 --> 00:41:58,946
(Starting off)

998
00:42:00,312 --> 00:42:01,346
It went in nicely.

999
00:42:01,646 --> 00:42:02,512
That's it.

1000
00:42:05,079 --> 00:42:05,846
Spike.

1001
00:42:05,847 --> 00:42:07,546
(They break through.)

1002
00:42:08,112 --> 00:42:09,278
Min Kyeong keeps it alive.

1003
00:42:09,279 --> 00:42:10,579
There it is.

1004
00:42:11,446 --> 00:42:13,011
(Chae Rim sets up the second ball.)

1005
00:42:13,012 --> 00:42:13,879
Go for it.

1006
00:42:13,879 --> 00:42:14,746
Hwang Yeon Joo!

1007
00:42:15,046 --> 00:42:15,979
It's covered.

1008
00:42:16,546 --> 00:42:17,312
To the other side.

1009
00:42:17,313 --> 00:42:18,905
(Chae Rim, fully recharged)

1010
00:42:19,012 --> 00:42:20,212
(Full-power spike)

1011
00:42:24,212 --> 00:42:25,512
They keep that alive too.

1012
00:42:26,179 --> 00:42:27,012
Cover!

1013
00:42:28,746 --> 00:42:29,716
(Free ball)

1014
00:42:30,346 --> 00:42:31,745
(The ball goes back to Yeon Joo.)

1015
00:42:31,746 --> 00:42:32,712
Yeon Joo!

1016
00:42:32,946 --> 00:42:34,411
Now she needs to put
a period on this play.

1017
00:42:34,412 --> 00:42:35,312
Hwang Yeon Joo!

1018
00:42:35,313 --> 00:42:36,612
(Here she comes.)

1019
00:42:37,812 --> 00:42:39,111
(Period)

1020
00:42:39,112 --> 00:42:42,646
Yeon Joo tips it over!

1021
00:42:44,842 --> 00:42:46,246
It's in. Bravo.

1022
00:42:46,546 --> 00:42:48,079
- Yeon Joo.
- Well done.

1023
00:42:54,379 --> 00:42:55,512
Nice job.

1024
00:42:56,812 --> 00:42:57,779
Nice defense.

1025
00:43:00,512 --> 00:43:02,246
The timing was incredible too.

1026
00:43:02,846 --> 00:43:04,812
I can't believe I'm watching this again.

1027
00:43:05,579 --> 00:43:08,245
With Min Kyeong on the court,

1028
00:43:08,246 --> 00:43:10,278
they put more power into their serves,

1029
00:43:10,279 --> 00:43:12,979
and their defense was solid too.

1030
00:43:15,146 --> 00:43:19,611
She timed that perfectly
to catch the blockers off guard.

1031
00:43:19,612 --> 00:43:21,479
It was a picture-perfect play.

1032
00:43:22,179 --> 00:43:24,478
They've taken the lead, 11 to 10.

1033
00:43:24,479 --> 00:43:26,046
The comeback is underway.

1034
00:43:26,812 --> 00:43:28,845
- Hwang Yeon Joo!
- Hwang Yeon Joo!

1035
00:43:28,846 --> 00:43:30,779
Great job, Min Kyeong.

1036
00:43:31,379 --> 00:43:33,546
Stay calm, Min Kyeong.

1037
00:43:35,412 --> 00:43:38,311
Compared to Season 1, in Season 2,

1038
00:43:38,312 --> 00:43:41,911
I definitely focused more
on utilizing each player effectively.

1039
00:43:41,912 --> 00:43:45,278
Each player had
their own strengths and weaknesses,

1040
00:43:45,279 --> 00:43:46,911
so I wanted to maximize their potential.

1041
00:43:46,912 --> 00:43:48,011
I wanted to build a system...

1042
00:43:48,012 --> 00:43:51,345
where the whole team could
work together smoothly.

1043
00:43:51,346 --> 00:43:52,511
(Bringing the offense back to life too.)

1044
00:43:52,512 --> 00:43:55,978
Yeon Joo's distinct, gritty look
from her time on the court...

1045
00:43:55,979 --> 00:43:58,412
has finally come back into her eyes.

1046
00:43:58,679 --> 00:44:02,112
She looks like she's about to devour
the entire court.

1047
00:44:07,046 --> 00:44:08,946
- The reception is shaky.
- Nice!

1048
00:44:10,912 --> 00:44:11,846
A tempo attack.

1049
00:44:11,847 --> 00:44:12,878
Nice defense.

1050
00:44:12,879 --> 00:44:13,779
They keep it alive.

1051
00:44:15,079 --> 00:44:16,645
(Here comes the Flame Deer!)

1052
00:44:16,646 --> 00:44:17,846
Let's go, Yeon Joo.

1053
00:44:19,212 --> 00:44:22,878
Hwang Yeon Joo!

1054
00:44:22,879 --> 00:44:24,146
- Let's go, Yeon Joo!
- That's it.

1055
00:44:28,379 --> 00:44:30,845
- Nice set.
- Nice, Min Kyeong.

1056
00:44:30,846 --> 00:44:32,211
That's great, Min Kyeong.

1057
00:44:32,212 --> 00:44:33,646
Nice set.

1058
00:44:34,046 --> 00:44:35,345
This is nerve-racking.

1059
00:44:35,346 --> 00:44:36,346
This is insane.

1060
00:44:37,946 --> 00:44:38,779
It grazes the net.

1061
00:44:40,179 --> 00:44:41,446
(A fully charged reception)

1062
00:44:41,979 --> 00:44:45,579
A difficult ball. Yeon Joo swings.

1063
00:44:47,112 --> 00:44:48,845
(Let the Flame Deer burn!)

1064
00:44:48,846 --> 00:44:50,379
That's right. There it is.

1065
00:44:52,379 --> 00:44:53,745
- That's...
- That's...

1066
00:44:53,746 --> 00:44:56,179
- That's the technique of a legend.
- Exactly.

1067
00:44:56,479 --> 00:44:59,312
She puts a subtle spin
on the ball right there.

1068
00:44:59,712 --> 00:45:02,812
That was absolutely insane.

1069
00:45:03,612 --> 00:45:05,112
It's 15 to 12, a three-point lead.

1070
00:45:08,146 --> 00:45:10,046
(Chae Rim serves.)

1071
00:45:10,179 --> 00:45:11,112
Back Chae Rim serves.

1072
00:45:12,612 --> 00:45:15,379
(Fully charged)

1073
00:45:16,279 --> 00:45:18,079
- A back set.
- The other side.

1074
00:45:19,612 --> 00:45:20,479
(Touch)

1075
00:45:21,012 --> 00:45:21,846
Spike.

1076
00:45:22,379 --> 00:45:23,346
It's a block out.

1077
00:45:23,347 --> 00:45:25,279
(Block out)

1078
00:45:26,179 --> 00:45:27,212
She touched it.

1079
00:45:31,546 --> 00:45:33,411
They keep hitting it
in the opposite direction.

1080
00:45:33,412 --> 00:45:35,612
Why do you keep giving them those touches?

1081
00:45:36,546 --> 00:45:38,245
- Enkhsoyol, it's a powerful serve.
- Okay.

1082
00:45:38,679 --> 00:45:41,279
(Serve alert)

1083
00:45:41,912 --> 00:45:44,878
(Onishi is coming to serve.)

1084
00:45:44,879 --> 00:45:45,978
Send it up.

1085
00:45:45,979 --> 00:45:47,414
This way.

1086
00:45:48,386 --> 00:45:51,012
(Tensed up)

1087
00:45:51,212 --> 00:45:53,445
We have a chance.

1088
00:45:53,446 --> 00:45:54,546
Hit it hard.

1089
00:45:59,112 --> 00:46:00,079
Powerful serve.

1090
00:46:01,046 --> 00:46:02,178
(One shot, one kill)

1091
00:46:02,179 --> 00:46:03,746
It's 15 to 14, just one point apart.

1092
00:46:04,579 --> 00:46:06,846
Oh, no. Please.

1093
00:46:10,746 --> 00:46:12,512
(Onishi serves again.)

1094
00:46:13,146 --> 00:46:14,079
Send it up.

1095
00:46:14,080 --> 00:46:16,312
Jump up.

1096
00:46:20,079 --> 00:46:21,979
It lands inside.

1097
00:46:22,712 --> 00:46:24,712
Onishi scores another ace.

1098
00:46:27,312 --> 00:46:28,879
Throw yourself at the ball!

1099
00:46:31,246 --> 00:46:33,611
If you dodge it, who's going to get it?

1100
00:46:33,612 --> 00:46:35,379
Don't dodge the ball.

1101
00:46:36,179 --> 00:46:38,312
- Got it.
- Catch it.

1102
00:46:40,946 --> 00:46:42,779
Timeout.

1103
00:46:45,846 --> 00:46:47,679
Coach Kim calls a timeout.

1104
00:46:49,012 --> 00:46:52,612
Get over here now!

1105
00:46:52,625 --> 00:46:53,812
- Hurry up.
- Come here!

1106
00:46:54,659 --> 00:46:56,760
Why are you just letting them score
through the middle?

1107
00:46:56,761 --> 00:46:58,696
You have to get your body behind the ball.

1108
00:46:58,697 --> 00:47:00,298
Why are you just letting it drop?

1109
00:47:00,299 --> 00:47:01,732
Do you realize
what the score is right now?

1110
00:47:02,401 --> 00:47:04,635
Why are you just watching it go down?

1111
00:47:04,636 --> 00:47:06,537
- You have to throw your body.
- Yes, Coach.

1112
00:47:06,538 --> 00:47:07,872
(They give away the point
on a careless error.)

1113
00:47:07,873 --> 00:47:11,776
My serve reception is weak,
so I couldn't do what I should have.

1114
00:47:12,177 --> 00:47:14,745
I think that made
the match a lot harder for us.

1115
00:47:15,480 --> 00:47:17,181
Why are you playing like that?

1116
00:47:17,182 --> 00:47:18,816
Use your body and keep the ball up!

1117
00:47:18,817 --> 00:47:20,117
(The harsh words snap them
back to attention.)

1118
00:47:20,118 --> 00:47:21,185
Let's go!

1119
00:47:21,486 --> 00:47:22,586
Let's try again!

1120
00:47:22,887 --> 00:47:24,255
Don't lose your fight, okay?

1121
00:47:24,256 --> 00:47:25,689
- Keep coming at them. Keep attacking.
- Okay.

1122
00:47:25,690 --> 00:47:26,924
It's okay. I know their serves are tough.

1123
00:47:26,925 --> 00:47:29,226
She's telling you to just get the ball up
like you're making a defensive play.

1124
00:47:29,227 --> 00:47:31,596
You have to help each other out.

1125
00:47:31,597 --> 00:47:33,597
- Get ready to cover!
- Okay!

1126
00:47:33,598 --> 00:47:35,166
- Let's take this point!
- You have to help each other!

1127
00:47:35,167 --> 00:47:36,200
- Okay.
- Okay!

1128
00:47:36,201 --> 00:47:37,535
- In 1, 2, 3!
- Let's go!

1129
00:47:38,269 --> 00:47:39,169
Chae Rim,

1130
00:47:39,471 --> 00:47:40,671
do you want to regret this? No, right?

1131
00:47:40,672 --> 00:47:42,972
You've done well up to now.
Now take responsibility, okay?

1132
00:47:42,973 --> 00:47:45,209
Enkhsoyol, take responsibility
for putting the ball away!

1133
00:47:46,010 --> 00:47:47,010
Let's go.

1134
00:47:47,011 --> 00:47:48,144
(Holding hands)

1135
00:47:48,313 --> 00:47:50,114
- Shift over to the right together!
- Okay!

1136
00:47:50,115 --> 00:47:51,248
Stay on the side.

1137
00:47:51,249 --> 00:47:54,084
The older players told me they'd help
cover more of the serve reception,

1138
00:47:54,572 --> 00:47:55,873
so I thought I needed...

1139
00:47:55,887 --> 00:47:59,256
to take more responsibility in attack
and score points for the team.

1140
00:48:00,291 --> 00:48:03,660
Enkhsoyol, go deep. Don't forget.

1141
00:48:04,295 --> 00:48:05,128
Got it.

1142
00:48:06,831 --> 00:48:07,964
The score is tied at 15.

1143
00:48:08,299 --> 00:48:10,300
Onishi has been scoring repeatedly
from the service line.

1144
00:48:10,301 --> 00:48:13,336
(Onishi's third serve
during her dominant run)

1145
00:48:13,758 --> 00:48:16,306
(Nervous)

1146
00:48:20,211 --> 00:48:21,478
Seon Ah receives it.

1147
00:48:21,479 --> 00:48:22,579
That's it. She got it.

1148
00:48:23,681 --> 00:48:24,648
Enkhsoyol, fire!

1149
00:48:26,618 --> 00:48:28,852
Enkhsoyol, go deep.

1150
00:48:31,122 --> 00:48:32,255
Off the block and out!

1151
00:48:32,857 --> 00:48:34,224
Enkhsoyol did it!

1152
00:48:34,225 --> 00:48:35,766
(Another comeback!)

1153
00:48:36,514 --> 00:48:37,914
(Sighing)

1154
00:48:38,416 --> 00:48:40,016
Enkhsoyol!

1155
00:48:40,017 --> 00:48:42,319
Keep it up, okay?

1156
00:48:42,320 --> 00:48:43,754
- Enkhsoyol, good.
- Well done.

1157
00:48:45,349 --> 00:48:47,090
(Seon Ah's reception)

1158
00:48:48,058 --> 00:48:50,026
(A stable set)

1159
00:48:50,427 --> 00:48:52,295
(Enkhsoyol's powerful spike)

1160
00:48:53,063 --> 00:48:56,165
(She scores
against the next-generation world best!)

1161
00:48:56,801 --> 00:48:58,068
Let's do it together!

1162
00:48:58,302 --> 00:49:00,403
Reception first!

1163
00:49:00,806 --> 00:49:03,506
Seon Ah, watch the left!

1164
00:49:05,710 --> 00:49:06,910
Get it up!

1165
00:49:07,411 --> 00:49:08,411
They get the ball up cleanly.

1166
00:49:09,180 --> 00:49:11,214
(Here comes Enkhsoyol, the youngest!)

1167
00:49:11,816 --> 00:49:13,850
Spike! Another point.

1168
00:49:15,152 --> 00:49:19,288
(I knew you could do it, Enkhsoyol!)

1169
00:49:19,289 --> 00:49:20,890
Okay. Nice.

1170
00:49:21,592 --> 00:49:22,625
Great, Enkhsoyol!

1171
00:49:23,093 --> 00:49:24,393
- Enkhsoyol!
- Enkhsoyol!

1172
00:49:24,394 --> 00:49:26,228
(Amazed)

1173
00:49:26,229 --> 00:49:28,698
Enkhsoyol has really matured as a player.

1174
00:49:28,699 --> 00:49:31,033
Yes, she's stepping up
and taking responsibility.

1175
00:49:31,034 --> 00:49:32,768
(Enkhsoyol is improving!)

1176
00:49:38,542 --> 00:49:40,276
Yoshimoto!

1177
00:49:40,711 --> 00:49:42,545
Onishi!

1178
00:49:43,147 --> 00:49:45,281
It's all right.

1179
00:49:45,282 --> 00:49:46,916
Nothing has changed.
Just do what you have to.

1180
00:49:46,917 --> 00:49:48,418
(Nodding)

1181
00:49:49,720 --> 00:49:51,721
(The machine-gun duo regroups.)

1182
00:49:51,722 --> 00:49:53,356
- Wonder Dogs!
- Wonder Dogs!

1183
00:49:53,824 --> 00:49:55,858
Enkhsoyol, get ready.

1184
00:49:55,859 --> 00:49:58,561
(The youngest is ready to go!)

1185
00:49:58,562 --> 00:50:01,430
(Fourth set, Shujitsu High 16
: Wonder Dogs 17)

1186
00:50:06,637 --> 00:50:08,371
(A no-block situation)

1187
00:50:08,372 --> 00:50:09,539
The ball goes to Onishi!

1188
00:50:09,907 --> 00:50:10,874
It's our chance!

1189
00:50:13,844 --> 00:50:14,677
It's out!

1190
00:50:14,678 --> 00:50:16,479
(Line out)

1191
00:50:16,680 --> 00:50:18,447
She's starting to put
too much power into it now!

1192
00:50:18,448 --> 00:50:20,316
(An error from the ace)

1193
00:50:22,553 --> 00:50:23,253
Yoshimoto!

1194
00:50:23,254 --> 00:50:24,554
(Down the line!)

1195
00:50:24,989 --> 00:50:26,923
Okay.

1196
00:50:28,793 --> 00:50:29,860
They get it up with the reception.

1197
00:50:31,362 --> 00:50:32,162
Yoshimoto.

1198
00:50:32,997 --> 00:50:34,097
(Touching)

1199
00:50:35,299 --> 00:50:37,333
It's a block out.

1200
00:50:37,701 --> 00:50:39,201
(Shujitsu's ace duo
immediately answers back.)

1201
00:50:39,202 --> 00:50:40,903
Yoshimoto, nice!

1202
00:50:41,238 --> 00:50:43,472
(Fourth set, Shujitsu High 17
: Wonder Dogs 18)

1203
00:50:43,473 --> 00:50:46,743
Enkhsoyol!
It's okay to hit down this line.

1204
00:50:46,744 --> 00:50:48,044
- It's okay to hit it that way.
- Got it.

1205
00:50:48,713 --> 00:50:49,746
It's 18 to 17.

1206
00:50:51,348 --> 00:50:52,381
(Here comes the youngest again!)

1207
00:50:52,382 --> 00:50:53,516
Stay calm!

1208
00:50:54,018 --> 00:50:55,018
Sharp cross!

1209
00:50:56,086 --> 00:50:57,486
Spike and a point.

1210
00:50:57,487 --> 00:50:58,721
- That's it!
- Good!

1211
00:50:58,722 --> 00:51:00,322
(No, it was a straight shot!)

1212
00:51:01,158 --> 00:51:03,626
(Sighing)

1213
00:51:03,627 --> 00:51:05,261
One more point!

1214
00:51:05,596 --> 00:51:07,397
Let's go!

1215
00:51:09,199 --> 00:51:10,766
(Yoshimoto checks back in.)

1216
00:51:13,003 --> 00:51:13,903
A spike!

1217
00:51:13,904 --> 00:51:15,171
It drops in.

1218
00:51:15,172 --> 00:51:16,672
(Shujitsu immediately pulls
one point back.)

1219
00:51:16,807 --> 00:51:18,708
That dropped.

1220
00:51:19,410 --> 00:51:20,510
It's 19 to 18.

1221
00:51:20,511 --> 00:51:22,045
(Fourth set, Shujitsu High 18
: Wonder Dogs 19)

1222
00:51:22,446 --> 00:51:24,647
It's okay.
Let's get the next one right away.

1223
00:51:24,672 --> 00:51:29,342
(A fierce battle for every single point)

1224
00:51:29,820 --> 00:51:33,523
(One lapse in concentration could turn
the match around.)

1225
00:51:34,158 --> 00:51:37,661
(They need to widen the gap right now.)

1226
00:51:38,295 --> 00:51:39,295
Hyo Rim!

1227
00:51:39,697 --> 00:51:42,966
Even if you run the A-to-C play,
they're already closing in on her.

1228
00:51:42,967 --> 00:51:45,102
Just give it to Yeon Joo.

1229
00:51:45,103 --> 00:51:46,002
Okay.

1230
00:51:48,005 --> 00:51:50,073
(As Enkhsoyol starts to heat up,)

1231
00:51:50,374 --> 00:51:52,508
(Shujitsu immediately shuts
down the left side.)

1232
00:51:53,277 --> 00:51:56,113
(The opposing block is already shifting
left before the set even goes up.)

1233
00:51:56,680 --> 00:51:59,448
(They have to use the right side!)

1234
00:52:00,017 --> 00:52:02,385
(They look to widen the gap
through Yeon Joo.)

1235
00:52:03,153 --> 00:52:04,654
(The right side is ready.)

1236
00:52:04,855 --> 00:52:06,289
(Peeking)

1237
00:52:06,590 --> 00:52:08,291
Ito, they're coming.

1238
00:52:08,292 --> 00:52:09,325
Okay.

1239
00:52:09,927 --> 00:52:11,160
Block the straight shot.

1240
00:52:11,161 --> 00:52:12,929
Onishi, block the straight shot.

1241
00:52:13,364 --> 00:52:15,365
(She has to break through.)

1242
00:52:18,035 --> 00:52:19,035
A short serve.

1243
00:52:19,036 --> 00:52:20,603
To the right!

1244
00:52:20,905 --> 00:52:22,305
- That's it!
- We got it.

1245
00:52:22,673 --> 00:52:23,573
Hit it!

1246
00:52:24,642 --> 00:52:25,809
Yeon Joo with the tip.

1247
00:52:26,911 --> 00:52:27,811
Well done.

1248
00:52:27,812 --> 00:52:29,779
(It worked!)

1249
00:52:30,481 --> 00:52:31,548
There was no one there.

1250
00:52:31,815 --> 00:52:33,249
Yeon Joo!

1251
00:52:36,186 --> 00:52:38,721
(She uses their line defense
against them.)

1252
00:52:39,823 --> 00:52:42,525
How did she find such a sharp angle?

1253
00:52:42,726 --> 00:52:44,894
- They couldn't even get a hand on it.
- Exactly.

1254
00:52:45,729 --> 00:52:48,264
- Just block the right side.
- Okay.

1255
00:52:48,699 --> 00:52:50,400
Now let's go left.

1256
00:52:50,534 --> 00:52:51,400
Okay.

1257
00:52:51,669 --> 00:52:52,702
Okay.

1258
00:52:52,703 --> 00:52:54,004
(Stay focused. One more!)

1259
00:52:54,005 --> 00:52:55,605
Let's go right away!

1260
00:52:59,310 --> 00:53:00,810
Take your time!

1261
00:53:01,745 --> 00:53:02,945
Block!

1262
00:53:03,213 --> 00:53:04,379
Give it back to me!

1263
00:53:04,380 --> 00:53:05,514
- Here they come again.
- Hey!

1264
00:53:05,515 --> 00:53:06,982
Tip. Yeon Joo keeps it alive.

1265
00:53:06,983 --> 00:53:08,250
(Yeon Joo's defense)

1266
00:53:08,752 --> 00:53:09,685
(They're going left!)

1267
00:53:09,686 --> 00:53:10,653
Hit it!

1268
00:53:10,854 --> 00:53:14,390
Spike!

1269
00:53:14,491 --> 00:53:15,524
A three-point gap!

1270
00:53:15,525 --> 00:53:16,826
(Fourth set, Shujitsu High 18
: Wonder Dogs 21)

1271
00:53:16,827 --> 00:53:17,660
That's it.

1272
00:53:20,864 --> 00:53:22,164
(The Wonder Dogs lead by three.)

1273
00:53:22,165 --> 00:53:23,032
Well done.

1274
00:53:23,033 --> 00:53:24,133
That's it!

1275
00:53:24,935 --> 00:53:26,736
(Let's take this to a fifth set!)

1276
00:53:26,737 --> 00:53:28,938
Chae Rim puts it away
with a powerful attack.

1277
00:53:28,939 --> 00:53:30,406
And just before that...

1278
00:53:30,407 --> 00:53:32,074
- It was Yeon Joo!
- Yes, exactly.

1279
00:53:32,176 --> 00:53:35,011
She reacted incredibly quickly
to that tip fake.

1280
00:53:35,012 --> 00:53:38,148
Exactly. That's the kind of play
that comes from veteran experience.

1281
00:53:39,983 --> 00:53:43,652
The right-side hitter...

1282
00:53:44,021 --> 00:53:47,223
The Flame Deer, a 22-season pro veteran,
is back on the court.

1283
00:53:48,325 --> 00:53:49,393
It's incredible.

1284
00:53:49,394 --> 00:53:52,795
I have to give her tremendous credit
for taking on a challenge like this.

1285
00:53:54,231 --> 00:53:55,433
Well...

1286
00:53:55,434 --> 00:53:59,035
Honestly, during my pro career, I spent
much more time off the court than on it.

1287
00:53:59,036 --> 00:54:00,403
I think I spent 7 or 8 years on the bench.

1288
00:54:00,538 --> 00:54:03,806
I think I regretted retiring
without getting enough chances to play.

1289
00:54:04,341 --> 00:54:07,810
So I told myself I had to find
a way back onto the court.

1290
00:54:08,379 --> 00:54:10,780
I wanted to show the world
what I look like playing volleyball.

1291
00:54:13,350 --> 00:54:14,250
Follow it!

1292
00:54:14,818 --> 00:54:15,918
That's it, Yeon Joo!

1293
00:54:16,520 --> 00:54:18,020
My final chapter in volleyball...

1294
00:54:18,922 --> 00:54:20,923
hasn't come yet.

1295
00:54:21,825 --> 00:54:22,691
Yeon Joo.

1296
00:54:24,428 --> 00:54:25,862
- That's it!
- This time, it was a spike!

1297
00:54:25,863 --> 00:54:26,763
Bravo!

1298
00:54:27,631 --> 00:54:30,466
Yeon Joo has finally cracked
open this tightly contested fourth set.

1299
00:54:31,401 --> 00:54:33,502
Number Four...

1300
00:54:34,738 --> 00:54:38,174
That Number Four on the right!

1301
00:54:38,175 --> 00:54:39,675
I just saw it.

1302
00:54:40,110 --> 00:54:43,646
Yeon Joo can barely get off the ground,

1303
00:54:43,647 --> 00:54:45,247
but she's gritting her teeth
and forcing herself to jump.

1304
00:54:49,253 --> 00:54:51,187
For me, I could really feel...

1305
00:54:51,188 --> 00:54:52,655
my energy draining faster...

1306
00:54:53,190 --> 00:54:55,491
because of my age.

1307
00:54:55,994 --> 00:54:57,927
It was honestly exhausting.

1308
00:54:58,929 --> 00:55:00,062
But...

1309
00:55:00,831 --> 00:55:02,765
I wanted to win so badly...

1310
00:55:03,167 --> 00:55:06,970
that all I could think was,
"We have to get to the fifth set."

1311
00:55:07,237 --> 00:55:10,372
(The passionate Flame Deer)

1312
00:55:11,275 --> 00:55:13,209
It's 23 to 21. They're up by 2.

1313
00:55:14,211 --> 00:55:17,273
This rematch is heading
toward a fifth set too.

1314
00:55:17,274 --> 00:55:18,281
(Two points away from the fifth set)

1315
00:55:19,349 --> 00:55:20,416
Let's go!

1316
00:55:21,585 --> 00:55:22,885
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

1317
00:55:23,287 --> 00:55:24,119
Mine!

1318
00:55:24,755 --> 00:55:25,722
Net over!

1319
00:55:25,723 --> 00:55:26,723
It's a chance.

1320
00:55:27,091 --> 00:55:28,291
(Is it going over?)

1321
00:55:28,559 --> 00:55:29,592
Cover!

1322
00:55:30,194 --> 00:55:31,895
Yeon Joo!

1323
00:55:32,095 --> 00:55:33,495
What?

1324
00:55:34,398 --> 00:55:39,335
This time, Yeon Joo completely fooled them
by pretending she was going to set.

1325
00:55:39,603 --> 00:55:41,871
- I know!
- It was a nice move!

1326
00:55:41,872 --> 00:55:43,306
She threw in a subtle little fake.

1327
00:55:43,307 --> 00:55:44,173
(Tricked you)

1328
00:55:44,174 --> 00:55:46,409
That's exactly the kind of thing
that catches them off guard. Nicely done.

1329
00:55:46,410 --> 00:55:47,210
Okay.

1330
00:55:48,178 --> 00:55:51,280
One more to go. Just one! Focus!

1331
00:55:52,249 --> 00:55:54,550
And now it's set point
for the Wonder Dogs.

1332
00:55:54,551 --> 00:55:56,386
One more point,
and we're going to a fifth set!

1333
00:55:56,820 --> 00:55:58,254
(Just one point away from the fifth set)

1334
00:55:58,789 --> 00:55:59,722
Stay calm.

1335
00:56:02,526 --> 00:56:03,560
Chae Rim's serve.

1336
00:56:03,561 --> 00:56:05,628
(Chae Rim's serve)

1337
00:56:07,164 --> 00:56:08,264
Nice serve!

1338
00:56:08,265 --> 00:56:09,298
A shaky reception.

1339
00:56:10,300 --> 00:56:11,100
Here they come!

1340
00:56:11,101 --> 00:56:12,701
(Of all people, Onishi attacks.)

1341
00:56:12,804 --> 00:56:13,636
Onishi.

1342
00:56:14,871 --> 00:56:16,271
(What a shame.)

1343
00:56:16,272 --> 00:56:18,574
She can hit at such a sharp angle.

1344
00:56:18,675 --> 00:56:20,009
They can't let their guard down.

1345
00:56:20,010 --> 00:56:22,078
Onishi will keep coming at them
until the very last point.

1346
00:56:22,079 --> 00:56:24,614
- It's okay!
- Let's get one! We only need one more.

1347
00:56:24,615 --> 00:56:26,082
Just one, everyone!

1348
00:56:26,083 --> 00:56:27,416
- Let's finish it off!
- Let's get one!

1349
00:56:27,417 --> 00:56:28,550
Let's get one right now!

1350
00:56:28,551 --> 00:56:30,619
They need to stop Shujitsu's momentum
right here.

1351
00:56:30,787 --> 00:56:34,189
The Wonder Dogs need to be on their toes.
They have to stay locked in.

1352
00:56:34,190 --> 00:56:35,057
Yes.

1353
00:56:37,261 --> 00:56:40,130
Hit a tough serve.

1354
00:56:40,131 --> 00:56:41,097
Okay!

1355
00:56:43,600 --> 00:56:46,735
But the server is Onishi.

1356
00:56:47,605 --> 00:56:49,939
What a twist of fate.

1357
00:56:49,940 --> 00:56:51,507
They just need to stay strong.

1358
00:56:54,952 --> 00:56:56,985
Hey!

1359
00:56:56,986 --> 00:56:58,451
- Up!
- Don't hesitate!

1360
00:56:58,452 --> 00:57:00,351
Drop!

1361
00:57:00,352 --> 00:57:01,352
(Not that girl!)

1362
00:57:01,353 --> 00:57:02,751
- I'll cover the deep ball.
- Sure.

1363
00:57:02,752 --> 00:57:04,486
- I'll take this side.
- I'll stay on the left.

1364
00:57:04,752 --> 00:57:06,252
Don't back down!

1365
00:57:10,586 --> 00:57:12,819
It's the decisive moment
that may lead to the fifth set.

1366
00:57:14,019 --> 00:57:15,119
Their last obstacle.

1367
00:57:15,386 --> 00:57:19,386
(The final hurdle before the fifth set)

1368
00:57:22,852 --> 00:57:24,218
- That's it! Nice!
- Good.

1369
00:57:24,219 --> 00:57:25,251
She received it.

1370
00:57:25,252 --> 00:57:26,685
- There!
- She sets it up.

1371
00:57:26,686 --> 00:57:27,752
Spike!

1372
00:57:29,652 --> 00:57:30,718
(How far is she going?)

1373
00:57:30,719 --> 00:57:32,651
One down! Toss it to the left!

1374
00:57:32,652 --> 00:57:34,718
- It's over.
- Give it again.

1375
00:57:34,719 --> 00:57:36,452
- Again!
- They keep it tight and try again.

1376
00:57:36,719 --> 00:57:37,752
To the middle.

1377
00:57:38,219 --> 00:57:39,219
One more time!

1378
00:57:39,452 --> 00:57:40,618
- That's it!
- It's over.

1379
00:57:40,619 --> 00:57:41,686
Wait, is it?

1380
00:57:42,152 --> 00:57:44,251
(A never-ending battle)

1381
00:57:44,252 --> 00:57:45,985
Bo Been!

1382
00:57:45,986 --> 00:57:48,319
Moving to the center for the last time!

1383
00:57:50,452 --> 00:57:51,519
She received it!

1384
00:57:51,952 --> 00:57:52,952
(Dizzy)

1385
00:57:52,953 --> 00:57:53,986
High ball.

1386
00:57:54,652 --> 00:57:56,618
- Give it to Enkhsoyol!
- Again!

1387
00:57:56,619 --> 00:57:58,418
You've got this, Enkhsoyol!

1388
00:57:58,419 --> 00:57:59,585
Go deep.

1389
00:57:59,586 --> 00:58:00,619
Hurry up!

1390
00:58:01,086 --> 00:58:02,118
She'll hit it deep!

1391
00:58:02,119 --> 00:58:03,119
Left!

1392
00:58:03,120 --> 00:58:04,552
(Shutting down the deep ball)

1393
00:58:05,219 --> 00:58:06,219
Rip it!

1394
00:58:06,319 --> 00:58:07,319
(Checking)

1395
00:58:07,719 --> 00:58:09,286
- Nice! It's our chance!
- Enkhsoyol!

1396
00:58:13,552 --> 00:58:18,152
Enkhsoyol's push shot on the fourth try!

1397
00:58:18,719 --> 00:58:20,318
(Cheering)

1398
00:58:20,319 --> 00:58:21,485
Nice!

1399
00:58:21,486 --> 00:58:23,252
(Smiling at last)

1400
00:58:23,619 --> 00:58:25,919
(Groaning)

1401
00:58:26,219 --> 00:58:28,752
We're going to a fifth set!

1402
00:58:39,919 --> 00:58:41,852
(Forced a fifth set)

1403
00:58:42,319 --> 00:58:43,586
(We did it.)

1404
00:58:44,052 --> 00:58:46,119
(Can't believe that worked)

1405
00:58:46,552 --> 00:58:48,751
What a nail-biter
for the very first match.

1406
00:58:48,752 --> 00:58:49,752
It's just amazing.

1407
00:58:49,753 --> 00:58:51,152
This is driving me crazy.

1408
00:58:51,519 --> 00:58:52,885
(Sighing)

1409
00:58:52,886 --> 00:58:54,251
This is killing me.

1410
00:58:54,252 --> 00:58:55,852
It's no joke, but fun.

1411
00:58:56,552 --> 00:58:57,552
It's exciting.

1412
00:58:58,486 --> 00:59:00,651
With the score of 23 to 25,

1413
00:59:00,652 --> 00:59:02,918
Shujitsu High School wins the fourth set.

1414
00:59:02,919 --> 00:59:04,118
Just go for it. It's okay.

1415
00:59:04,119 --> 00:59:07,118
- You've got this. I'm sure of it.
- Yes, Coach!

1416
00:59:07,119 --> 00:59:08,551
(Revenge match sets, Shujitsu High 2
: Wonder Dogs 0)

1417
00:59:08,552 --> 00:59:09,585
(Shujitsu High 2 : Wonder Dogs 1)

1418
00:59:09,586 --> 00:59:11,451
We kept hanging on...

1419
00:59:11,452 --> 00:59:12,752
and finally got our chance.

1420
00:59:14,919 --> 00:59:18,585
(It's our turn to make a comeback.)

1421
00:59:18,586 --> 00:59:20,152
With the same rival,

1422
00:59:21,019 --> 00:59:23,252
we're back to even again.

1423
00:59:23,752 --> 00:59:25,251
We lost last time,

1424
00:59:25,252 --> 00:59:26,569
so this time, we're going to win.

1425
00:59:26,570 --> 00:59:27,919
(We'll pay them back
with a reverse sweep.)

1426
00:59:29,319 --> 00:59:32,818
(Strategic timeout for the fifth set)

1427
00:59:32,819 --> 00:59:35,152
It's the same situation as before.

1428
00:59:35,452 --> 00:59:36,586
You didn't score on the first try.

1429
00:59:36,952 --> 00:59:38,918
- The ball will come over again.
- Yes.

1430
00:59:38,919 --> 00:59:41,285
- Just receive it and attack again.
- Understood.

1431
00:59:41,286 --> 00:59:43,351
- Our blocking and digging are good now.
- Yes.

1432
00:59:43,352 --> 00:59:44,818
- So it's fine.
- Right.

1433
00:59:44,819 --> 00:59:46,685
Stay calm. Receive first.

1434
00:59:46,686 --> 00:59:47,718
Yes, Coach!

1435
00:59:47,719 --> 00:59:48,719
(Calm down and receive first!)

1436
00:59:50,886 --> 00:59:56,619
(She quietly steps back
after a quick instruction.)

1437
01:00:01,298 --> 01:00:02,998
The fifth set is a whole new game.

1438
01:00:04,131 --> 01:00:05,397
It's our final battle,

1439
01:00:05,398 --> 01:00:09,664
so it's like starting a match
all over again.

1440
01:00:13,164 --> 01:00:18,031
(As everything is on the line,
she takes longer to decide.)

1441
01:00:19,964 --> 01:00:22,564
We're going to need a new strategy.

1442
01:00:26,064 --> 01:00:27,698
Hyo Rim.

1443
01:00:29,198 --> 01:00:32,764
(The two coaches are busy giving
new instructions.)

1444
01:00:33,731 --> 01:00:36,564
Which coach will have the last laugh?

1445
01:00:38,164 --> 01:00:41,364
(The final set
that will decide their fate)

1446
01:00:42,898 --> 01:00:45,431
(The fifth set is played to 15 points.)

1447
01:00:46,064 --> 01:00:48,731
Every single point matters now.

1448
01:00:49,964 --> 01:00:50,964
Do I start from here?

1449
01:00:51,664 --> 01:00:53,563
Yeon Joo, Ho Bin, and Enkhsoyol,

1450
01:00:53,564 --> 01:00:55,563
the three hitters, are in the front row,

1451
01:00:55,564 --> 01:00:57,264
meaning they'll boost their attacks.

1452
01:00:59,831 --> 01:01:03,463
I figured we'd keep the three hitters
up front as much as possible...

1453
01:01:03,464 --> 01:01:06,498
and attack more aggressively.

1454
01:01:12,098 --> 01:01:15,964
Onishi Yukiji is the first server
for Shujitsu High School.

1455
01:01:17,031 --> 01:01:18,630
You'll serve first, Onishi.

1456
01:01:18,631 --> 01:01:19,631
(Onishi will serve first.)

1457
01:01:19,632 --> 01:01:21,131
Serve it hard.

1458
01:01:21,931 --> 01:01:23,031
Got it.

1459
01:01:24,731 --> 01:01:27,630
(Coach Nishihata plans to score
the first point with a serve.)

1460
01:01:27,631 --> 01:01:29,531
(Glancing)

1461
01:01:29,998 --> 01:01:32,164
Hey, get it up!

1462
01:01:33,464 --> 01:01:35,098
Get it up here!

1463
01:01:43,164 --> 01:01:45,598
(Fifth set, Shujitsu High 0
: Wonder Dogs 0)

1464
01:01:49,531 --> 01:01:50,598
(Groaning)

1465
01:01:51,331 --> 01:01:53,698
(Conceded right away)

1466
01:01:54,764 --> 01:01:56,131
Concentrate!

1467
01:01:56,798 --> 01:02:00,831
It's not easy to hit
such a powerful first serve.

1468
01:02:01,731 --> 01:02:03,498
She was chosen to serve first
for a reason.

1469
01:02:04,731 --> 01:02:07,131
(Her strategy worked.)

1470
01:02:11,231 --> 01:02:12,497
It's 1 to 0.

1471
01:02:12,498 --> 01:02:14,264
They need to stop them now.

1472
01:02:16,598 --> 01:02:19,397
(Onishi continues to serve.)

1473
01:02:19,398 --> 01:02:20,897
Chae Rim, get it on the right.

1474
01:02:20,898 --> 01:02:22,431
You do it!

1475
01:02:22,664 --> 01:02:23,731
Okay.

1476
01:02:25,898 --> 01:02:28,164
I decided I had to step up
and receive the ball.

1477
01:02:32,664 --> 01:02:33,664
She received it.

1478
01:02:33,664 --> 01:02:34,664
There it is.

1479
01:02:36,098 --> 01:02:37,131
(Connecting with a back toss)

1480
01:02:37,464 --> 01:02:38,531
A block.

1481
01:02:42,131 --> 01:02:43,164
(Chae Rim defends again.)

1482
01:02:43,431 --> 01:02:45,031
- Hyo Rim.
- Hit it!

1483
01:02:45,198 --> 01:02:46,564
(Enkhsoyol this time)

1484
01:02:50,298 --> 01:02:51,331
They defend.

1485
01:02:51,598 --> 01:02:53,564
The right!

1486
01:02:53,964 --> 01:02:55,564
(Rushing to Yeon Joo)

1487
01:02:56,398 --> 01:02:57,464
Give it to Enkhsoyol.

1488
01:02:59,264 --> 01:03:01,363
- There!
- Enkhsoyol again!

1489
01:03:01,364 --> 01:03:02,364
She scored!

1490
01:03:02,431 --> 01:03:05,431
- Yes!
- Nice!

1491
01:03:06,164 --> 01:03:08,264
(A well-focused attack)

1492
01:03:10,264 --> 01:03:14,263
Shujitsu High School expected the ball
to go to Yeon Joo.

1493
01:03:14,264 --> 01:03:18,031
Instead, Coach Kim used Enkhsoyol
on the other side.

1494
01:03:18,831 --> 01:03:20,698
Nice toss, Hyo Rim.

1495
01:03:21,831 --> 01:03:23,197
Yeon Joo is on fire again,

1496
01:03:23,198 --> 01:03:25,997
so both blockers are focused on her,
ready to defend.

1497
01:03:25,998 --> 01:03:27,963
Enkhsoyol is doing well too,
so use her at the right moment.

1498
01:03:27,964 --> 01:03:29,264
It depends on the quick attack.

1499
01:03:29,731 --> 01:03:32,064
(She knew Shujitsu High School
would target Yeon Joo.)

1500
01:03:32,798 --> 01:03:36,031
(A battle of wits and deception)

1501
01:03:36,431 --> 01:03:38,931
(Riding this momentum,)

1502
01:03:39,198 --> 01:03:40,731
(Ho Bin serves.)

1503
01:03:42,098 --> 01:03:43,464
Left!

1504
01:03:44,098 --> 01:03:45,864
(Quickly setting to the left)

1505
01:03:46,031 --> 01:03:47,398
One, two!

1506
01:03:47,698 --> 01:03:49,531
(Three!)

1507
01:03:51,098 --> 01:03:52,131
It's a block out.

1508
01:03:52,431 --> 01:03:54,131
This is what I mean!

1509
01:03:54,531 --> 01:03:57,164
Timing!

1510
01:03:58,064 --> 01:04:00,398
(Smiling)

1511
01:04:00,598 --> 01:04:03,398
- They meant to target Yeon Joo.
- Right.

1512
01:04:03,698 --> 01:04:04,798
Timing.

1513
01:04:05,464 --> 01:04:07,697
Yeon Joo, you're fast.

1514
01:04:07,698 --> 01:04:08,698
Too fast.

1515
01:04:09,464 --> 01:04:10,863
The slow balls!

1516
01:04:10,864 --> 01:04:12,064
Watch the drop!

1517
01:04:13,431 --> 01:04:17,464
(Next, Kato Uta serves.)

1518
01:04:17,998 --> 01:04:19,130
Faster!

1519
01:04:19,131 --> 01:04:20,198
- Enkhsoyol receives.
- Nice!

1520
01:04:20,731 --> 01:04:21,764
- Right!
- Hit it!

1521
01:04:21,898 --> 01:04:22,964
Right!

1522
01:04:23,331 --> 01:04:24,331
(Approaching)

1523
01:04:24,498 --> 01:04:25,698
Left. Chae Rim, one.

1524
01:04:25,898 --> 01:04:26,898
Hit it!

1525
01:04:27,631 --> 01:04:28,631
(Oops!)

1526
01:04:28,632 --> 01:04:30,430
- Go! Nice!
- One-on-one!

1527
01:04:30,431 --> 01:04:31,463
All right!

1528
01:04:31,464 --> 01:04:32,464
Chae Rim!

1529
01:04:34,931 --> 01:04:36,564
(Disappointed)

1530
01:04:37,231 --> 01:04:41,531
(An intense tactical battle
between the two coaches)

1531
01:04:43,631 --> 01:04:45,830
The Wonder Dogs
can still turn things around.

1532
01:04:45,831 --> 01:04:46,997
(Fifth set, Shujitsu High 4
: Wonder Dogs 3)

1533
01:04:46,998 --> 01:04:48,098
A one-point difference.

1534
01:04:48,864 --> 01:04:52,331
I think it's time for them
to start concentrating more.

1535
01:04:53,598 --> 01:04:56,098
(Yeon Joo serves.)

1536
01:04:56,531 --> 01:04:58,897
(Yeon Joo, target number one!)

1537
01:04:58,898 --> 01:05:01,498
(The target area for the serve)

1538
01:05:04,831 --> 01:05:05,897
A shaky reception!

1539
01:05:05,898 --> 01:05:06,931
That's it.

1540
01:05:07,631 --> 01:05:08,664
They're scrambling!

1541
01:05:09,531 --> 01:05:10,531
A free ball!

1542
01:05:11,631 --> 01:05:12,631
A chance to tie!

1543
01:05:14,164 --> 01:05:15,298
(Chae Rim spikes.)

1544
01:05:15,898 --> 01:05:18,231
(The ball pops high into the air!)

1545
01:05:19,598 --> 01:05:20,931
But it's saved.

1546
01:05:21,698 --> 01:05:23,064
It's a free ball, though.

1547
01:05:25,998 --> 01:05:27,464
Chae Rim again!

1548
01:05:27,664 --> 01:05:29,164
(Shujitsu defends once more.)

1549
01:05:29,964 --> 01:05:31,197
She spikes it over.

1550
01:05:31,198 --> 01:05:32,231
Set!

1551
01:05:32,431 --> 01:05:33,464
Bring it down!

1552
01:05:34,864 --> 01:05:35,864
Chae Rim.

1553
01:05:36,198 --> 01:05:38,963
(It's blocked!)

1554
01:05:38,964 --> 01:05:40,163
Toss!

1555
01:05:40,164 --> 01:05:41,831
(About to counterattack!)

1556
01:05:43,664 --> 01:05:44,964
It's going straight!

1557
01:05:47,998 --> 01:05:50,097
No! Okay.

1558
01:05:50,098 --> 01:05:51,988
Net! That's four hits!

1559
01:05:52,048 --> 01:05:55,738
(Four-hit violation: A team touches
the ball four times before returning it.)

1560
01:05:55,852 --> 01:05:57,820
(Four-hit violation confirmed)

1561
01:05:58,722 --> 01:06:00,457
(Relentless attacks force an error.)

1562
01:06:00,458 --> 01:06:01,958
- Thanks, Chae Rim. Nice!
- It was nothing.

1563
01:06:02,859 --> 01:06:04,026
It's tied at four.

1564
01:06:04,728 --> 01:06:06,962
The Wonder Dogs battle back to a tie!

1565
01:06:07,398 --> 01:06:09,165
Now is their chance to take the lead.

1566
01:06:12,069 --> 01:06:15,370
Hyo Rim, set it to the right!

1567
01:06:15,371 --> 01:06:16,405
Yes, Coach.

1568
01:06:16,406 --> 01:06:18,474
(Coach Kim calls for a right-side attack.)

1569
01:06:22,612 --> 01:06:23,979
That threw them off a little.

1570
01:06:26,049 --> 01:06:27,316
Yeon Joo times the dig perfectly!

1571
01:06:27,317 --> 01:06:28,384
There you go!

1572
01:06:28,885 --> 01:06:30,219
And they get it over!

1573
01:06:35,292 --> 01:06:36,525
Yu Kyung with the dig!

1574
01:06:36,526 --> 01:06:37,360
Mine!

1575
01:06:38,228 --> 01:06:39,262
(A fierce defensive battle)

1576
01:06:39,263 --> 01:06:40,129
Chae Rim.

1577
01:06:41,431 --> 01:06:42,965
Quick attack! Hurry!

1578
01:06:43,100 --> 01:06:45,300
An attack up the middle.
But there's the block.

1579
01:06:45,736 --> 01:06:46,569
(Then comes a decoy.)

1580
01:06:46,937 --> 01:06:47,637
Hyo Rim!

1581
01:06:47,638 --> 01:06:48,304
(The decoy jump)

1582
01:06:48,505 --> 01:06:50,339
(The Flame Deer springs into action!)

1583
01:06:52,309 --> 01:06:54,443
(A clever push shot)

1584
01:06:55,011 --> 01:06:56,111
A tip!

1585
01:06:56,646 --> 01:06:58,880
It's in!

1586
01:06:59,049 --> 01:07:01,717
It's in!

1587
01:07:01,718 --> 01:07:03,419
It's in bounds!

1588
01:07:03,653 --> 01:07:04,686
Yeon Joo!

1589
01:07:04,955 --> 01:07:07,255
That's it!

1590
01:07:08,759 --> 01:07:10,760
It dropped right
into the defense's blind spot.

1591
01:07:13,430 --> 01:07:14,997
That's a work of art!

1592
01:07:14,998 --> 01:07:16,632
(Volleyball at its finest)

1593
01:07:18,034 --> 01:07:19,736
(Fifth set, Shujitsu High 4
: Wonder Dogs 5)

1594
01:07:19,737 --> 01:07:20,802
The Wonder Dogs go up 5 to 4!

1595
01:07:21,671 --> 01:07:22,571
- Hwang Yeon Joo!
- Hwang Yeon Joo!

1596
01:07:23,240 --> 01:07:24,173
- Hwang Yeon Joo!
- Hwang Yeon Joo!

1597
01:07:25,075 --> 01:07:26,942
And Yeon Joo is at the heart of it all.

1598
01:07:26,943 --> 01:07:28,110
(Yeon Joo is leading the comeback.)

1599
01:07:29,145 --> 01:07:30,145
(Stealing a glance)

1600
01:07:31,581 --> 01:07:34,683
Set one to the right.

1601
01:07:34,684 --> 01:07:36,285
(Nodding)

1602
01:07:36,820 --> 01:07:40,589
- Wonder Dogs!
- Wonder Dogs!

1603
01:07:43,193 --> 01:07:44,260
The quick attack is blocked.

1604
01:07:44,261 --> 01:07:45,127
Nice block!

1605
01:07:45,829 --> 01:07:46,929
Move in!

1606
01:07:49,766 --> 01:07:51,533
(Shujitsu uses a decoy jump.)

1607
01:07:52,769 --> 01:07:54,903
From the right! Off the block and out.

1608
01:07:55,272 --> 01:07:56,138
Shoot.

1609
01:07:58,476 --> 01:08:01,043
Shujitsu just pulled off...

1610
01:08:01,044 --> 01:08:03,246
the same play Coach Kim used earlier.

1611
01:08:06,550 --> 01:08:09,619
Volleyball is all about trying
to outsmart each other.

1612
01:08:10,253 --> 01:08:12,354
Even when you know what's coming,
you still fall for it.

1613
01:08:12,889 --> 01:08:14,623
(One move with the serve)

1614
01:08:17,894 --> 01:08:19,661
(Another with a surprise attack
from the left)

1615
01:08:19,662 --> 01:08:21,497
Enkhsoyol again! A quick attack!

1616
01:08:23,033 --> 01:08:27,703
(Their strategies even mirror each other.)

1617
01:08:28,204 --> 01:08:31,039
(The fifth and deciding set)

1618
01:08:31,308 --> 01:08:34,410
(A fierce battle of wits)

1619
01:08:35,011 --> 01:08:35,811
It's tied at five.

1620
01:08:35,812 --> 01:08:37,412
Finish it on the first try!

1621
01:08:37,413 --> 01:08:39,481
- Let's get another one!
- Finish it on the first try!

1622
01:08:40,217 --> 01:08:42,184
(Yoshimoto serves.)

1623
01:08:43,153 --> 01:08:44,186
A solid reception.

1624
01:08:44,621 --> 01:08:45,588
(Bo Been gets her chance.)

1625
01:08:45,589 --> 01:08:46,522
Bo Been.

1626
01:08:47,724 --> 01:08:48,590
Bo Been.

1627
01:08:48,591 --> 01:08:49,458
(A slide attack)

1628
01:08:50,193 --> 01:08:52,461
(The defense is thrown off balance.)

1629
01:08:52,629 --> 01:08:54,363
She tips it over.

1630
01:08:55,031 --> 01:08:56,465
The set goes left,

1631
01:08:56,833 --> 01:08:57,833
and it's off the block.

1632
01:08:58,635 --> 01:08:59,935
(The counterattack continues.)

1633
01:09:00,203 --> 01:09:01,770
Onishi! The ball pops high into the air.

1634
01:09:05,308 --> 01:09:06,174
Watch it!

1635
01:09:06,175 --> 01:09:07,276
(But the ball comes back over?)

1636
01:09:07,277 --> 01:09:09,044
- Bo Been!
- It's going over!

1637
01:09:09,446 --> 01:09:10,279
It's okay.

1638
01:09:10,280 --> 01:09:12,348
(A chance for a direct kill)

1639
01:09:12,515 --> 01:09:13,448
Now...

1640
01:09:19,722 --> 01:09:20,388
Sorry.

1641
01:09:21,130 --> 01:09:22,058
I'm sorry.

1642
01:09:22,392 --> 01:09:24,193
We'll get the next one.

1643
01:09:24,194 --> 01:09:25,694
(The moment they let their guard down,)

1644
01:09:25,895 --> 01:09:27,496
(the score turns against them.)

1645
01:09:27,497 --> 01:09:28,663
Shujitsu leads 6 to 5.

1646
01:09:28,664 --> 01:09:30,265
(Fifth set, Shujitsu High 6
: Wonder Dogs 5)

1647
01:09:30,266 --> 01:09:31,099
A spike!

1648
01:09:34,304 --> 01:09:35,704
Off the block and out.

1649
01:09:36,173 --> 01:09:37,740
They can't afford another mistake.

1650
01:09:37,741 --> 01:09:40,075
Watch the timing.

1651
01:09:44,447 --> 01:09:46,682
(Back-to-back defensive errors)

1652
01:09:47,617 --> 01:09:49,017
They can't keep it in play.

1653
01:09:50,186 --> 01:09:52,521
The players look a little rattled.

1654
01:09:52,622 --> 01:09:55,591
We need to get the next point!

1655
01:09:55,592 --> 01:09:58,161
With Yeon Joo and Enkhsoyol
in the back row,

1656
01:09:58,162 --> 01:09:59,561
they're struggling to score.

1657
01:10:00,630 --> 01:10:05,100
(Back-row players can't attack
from in front of the attack line.)

1658
01:10:05,201 --> 01:10:08,170
They need to score to get
both hitters back up front.

1659
01:10:09,339 --> 01:10:10,406
(To unleash their hitters,)

1660
01:10:10,407 --> 01:10:12,508
Chae Rim, let's get another one!

1661
01:10:12,942 --> 01:10:15,710
(they have to find a way to score.)

1662
01:10:19,362 --> 01:10:20,182
Guys,

1663
01:10:20,516 --> 01:10:22,785
watch the timing of your blocks!

1664
01:10:22,786 --> 01:10:25,254
Take your time with the blocks!

1665
01:10:26,156 --> 01:10:30,359
We needed solid blocks
to set up our counterattacks,

1666
01:10:30,360 --> 01:10:32,128
so that's what I kept focusing on.

1667
01:10:32,129 --> 01:10:34,096
Blocking and defense are key.

1668
01:10:34,497 --> 01:10:36,832
Get your timing right!

1669
01:10:36,833 --> 01:10:38,200
Wait just a moment longer!

1670
01:10:39,737 --> 01:10:40,903
Yoshimoto Kanade.

1671
01:10:40,904 --> 01:10:41,771
(Yoshimoto serves.)

1672
01:10:43,173 --> 01:10:44,473
- Get it up.
- Chae Rim receives.

1673
01:10:45,709 --> 01:10:47,476
A tip off a high set! It's blocked.

1674
01:10:47,577 --> 01:10:48,610
Oh, come on.

1675
01:10:49,679 --> 01:10:51,180
Onishi on the left!

1676
01:10:51,247 --> 01:10:52,447
One, two.

1677
01:10:52,882 --> 01:10:54,583
(Three!)

1678
01:10:55,685 --> 01:10:58,587
A spike! And it's blocked!

1679
01:11:00,590 --> 01:11:01,523
Nice one!

1680
01:11:03,427 --> 01:11:04,660
Nice block.

1681
01:11:08,131 --> 01:11:11,200
- Bo Been the Light!
- Bo Been the Light!

1682
01:11:11,534 --> 01:11:16,071
Your hands came too far inward
on that attack.

1683
01:11:16,072 --> 01:11:18,573
Great block. Take your time. It's okay.

1684
01:11:18,574 --> 01:11:19,941
(Fifth set, Shujitsu High 9
: Wonder Dogs 6)

1685
01:11:20,110 --> 01:11:21,610
Enkhsoyol is back up front!

1686
01:11:22,812 --> 01:11:24,746
Good positioning!

1687
01:11:25,815 --> 01:11:26,915
(Enkhsoyol is back in the front row.)

1688
01:11:26,916 --> 01:11:28,116
I'm right here!

1689
01:11:29,519 --> 01:11:31,153
Hyo Rim.

1690
01:11:31,388 --> 01:11:32,621
Set to Enkhsoyol.

1691
01:11:33,757 --> 01:11:34,623
Enkhsoyol!

1692
01:11:36,426 --> 01:11:37,293
(Nodding)

1693
01:11:40,296 --> 01:11:42,430
Watch the left-side attack!

1694
01:11:43,533 --> 01:11:46,902
(Shujitsu is keeping a close eye
on Enkhsoyol.)

1695
01:11:52,075 --> 01:11:53,642
Miyake Hina is up to serve.

1696
01:11:53,643 --> 01:11:55,077
(Miyake Hina serves.)

1697
01:11:57,414 --> 01:11:58,814
Chae Rim gets it up nicely.

1698
01:11:58,948 --> 01:11:59,848
Go for it!

1699
01:12:00,350 --> 01:12:02,017
Deep!

1700
01:12:02,585 --> 01:12:03,885
The set goes up!

1701
01:12:06,790 --> 01:12:08,991
A huge spike! She scores!

1702
01:12:09,192 --> 01:12:10,759
(A crushing spike for the point)

1703
01:12:11,728 --> 01:12:13,529
(The crowd erupts.)

1704
01:12:13,697 --> 01:12:16,365
(That's what I'm talking about!)

1705
01:12:19,069 --> 01:12:22,104
With Enkhsoyol in the front row,

1706
01:12:22,105 --> 01:12:24,272
the Wonder Dogs need to score
as many points as possible.

1707
01:12:24,273 --> 01:12:25,140
Exactly.

1708
01:12:25,141 --> 01:12:26,041
(The mighty Enkhsoyol!)

1709
01:12:28,511 --> 01:12:31,179
(Just a two-point gap)

1710
01:12:32,549 --> 01:12:34,950
(They need to close the gap.)

1711
01:12:36,052 --> 01:12:38,086
- Min Kyeong.
- Min Kyeong!

1712
01:12:39,556 --> 01:12:42,291
Bo Been comes off, and Min Kyeong subs in.

1713
01:12:42,826 --> 01:12:44,627
It's a tactical move by Coach Kim.

1714
01:12:44,628 --> 01:12:47,163
An outside hitter comes in
for a middle blocker.

1715
01:12:47,164 --> 01:12:48,030
Right.

1716
01:12:48,398 --> 01:12:52,534
(The substitution strategy worked
in the fourth set too.)

1717
01:12:52,535 --> 01:12:54,870
She's looking to shore up the defense.

1718
01:12:54,871 --> 01:12:57,106
(Strengthening their back-row defense)

1719
01:12:58,708 --> 01:13:00,309
(Min Kyeong serves.)

1720
01:13:00,610 --> 01:13:01,810
Boom!

1721
01:13:02,011 --> 01:13:03,011
A good reception!

1722
01:13:03,146 --> 01:13:04,046
Kato Uta.

1723
01:13:04,481 --> 01:13:05,413
A powerful spike!

1724
01:13:06,749 --> 01:13:07,716
Min Kyeong defends with a dig.

1725
01:13:07,717 --> 01:13:08,583
(Nice dig!)

1726
01:13:10,820 --> 01:13:12,320
(The ball goes to Enkhsoyol.)

1727
01:13:12,889 --> 01:13:14,256
Enkhsoyol swings!

1728
01:13:14,257 --> 01:13:15,224
(Shujitsu's defense holds firm.)

1729
01:13:16,659 --> 01:13:17,559
Up the middle!

1730
01:13:18,495 --> 01:13:21,096
- What a dig!
- That's it, Chae Rim!

1731
01:13:21,931 --> 01:13:22,931
(Neither side gives an inch.)

1732
01:13:22,932 --> 01:13:23,999
Now it's a free ball!

1733
01:13:25,235 --> 01:13:26,101
A hard hit!

1734
01:13:26,836 --> 01:13:28,069
Chae Rim receives it again!

1735
01:13:29,472 --> 01:13:31,039
A chance to counterattack.

1736
01:13:31,040 --> 01:13:31,973
There you go. Nice set.

1737
01:13:32,742 --> 01:13:33,875
(Enkhsoyol goes on the attack.)

1738
01:13:35,578 --> 01:13:36,444
Shujitsu defends.

1739
01:13:36,679 --> 01:13:37,579
No tipping!

1740
01:13:39,749 --> 01:13:40,716
Onishi!

1741
01:13:41,251 --> 01:13:42,885
(A touch)

1742
01:13:42,886 --> 01:13:44,587
A spike!

1743
01:13:47,156 --> 01:13:49,991
(So close!)

1744
01:13:50,060 --> 01:13:52,594
Hit it. Look at the score!

1745
01:13:55,298 --> 01:14:01,103
(The gap widens again.)

1746
01:14:03,606 --> 01:14:08,110
(If they concede five more points,
their hopes for revenge are over.)

1747
01:14:08,778 --> 01:14:10,078
Mei is up to serve.

1748
01:14:10,079 --> 01:14:11,913
(Abe Mei serves.)

1749
01:14:13,116 --> 01:14:16,118
Mei, aim for Zone Three.

1750
01:14:16,119 --> 01:14:17,486
(Glancing)

1751
01:14:20,423 --> 01:14:22,959
(Enkhsoyol is targeted again.)

1752
01:14:23,054 --> 01:14:24,954
It could be a short one.

1753
01:14:26,062 --> 01:14:28,697
Watch out. She's got a fast serve.

1754
01:14:34,971 --> 01:14:36,772
It's out!

1755
01:14:36,773 --> 01:14:37,673
Out.

1756
01:14:40,176 --> 01:14:42,911
(A huge sigh of relief)

1757
01:14:43,880 --> 01:14:44,847
What are you doing?

1758
01:14:44,848 --> 01:14:45,981
It's 10 to 8, a two-point gap.

1759
01:14:46,215 --> 01:14:50,118
This is our best attacking lineup
right now.

1760
01:14:50,554 --> 01:14:52,788
We need to make the most
of every hitter we have...

1761
01:14:52,789 --> 01:14:55,090
and use them as much as possible.

1762
01:14:55,825 --> 01:14:57,893
Enkhsoyol! Get ready to attack.

1763
01:14:58,595 --> 01:14:59,595
Yes, Coach.

1764
01:15:00,263 --> 01:15:04,066
Enkhsoyol had her shaky moments,

1765
01:15:04,067 --> 01:15:08,837
but she's someone who can deliver
when we need a point.

1766
01:15:09,273 --> 01:15:11,307
I wanted to trust her to the end.

1767
01:15:13,843 --> 01:15:15,243
Hyo Rim is up to serve.

1768
01:15:15,244 --> 01:15:16,378
(Hyo Rim serves.)

1769
01:15:18,281 --> 01:15:19,348
A good reception!

1770
01:15:19,882 --> 01:15:21,683
Kato Uta. A spike!

1771
01:15:22,919 --> 01:15:23,919
Chae Rim with the dig.

1772
01:15:24,087 --> 01:15:25,154
That's it!

1773
01:15:26,956 --> 01:15:27,889
Shujitsu digs it out.

1774
01:15:29,993 --> 01:15:31,193
A pipe attack up the middle!

1775
01:15:31,194 --> 01:15:32,094
(This time, a pipe attack)

1776
01:15:32,395 --> 01:15:33,261
Set to Enkhsoyol.

1777
01:15:33,697 --> 01:15:34,563
Hyo Rim!

1778
01:15:35,765 --> 01:15:36,832
Enkhsoyol swings!

1779
01:15:37,533 --> 01:15:39,601
A free ball! Stay calm.

1780
01:15:39,602 --> 01:15:40,502
Again!

1781
01:15:41,170 --> 01:15:42,036
C!

1782
01:15:44,607 --> 01:15:45,908
(Enkhsoyol takes flight.)

1783
01:15:45,909 --> 01:15:47,709
Nice!

1784
01:15:48,578 --> 01:15:51,373
She puts it away! The point is hers!

1785
01:15:51,550 --> 01:15:52,750
They're closing the gap!

1786
01:15:52,783 --> 01:15:53,982
The score is now 10 to 9.

1787
01:15:53,983 --> 01:15:55,383
That's it!

1788
01:16:02,116 --> 01:16:05,116
(Go, Deep-soyol!)

1789
01:16:05,816 --> 01:16:07,483
Wonder Dogs are within one!

1790
01:16:09,816 --> 01:16:10,982
Target number four.

1791
01:16:10,983 --> 01:16:12,116
Keep it on the line.

1792
01:16:12,449 --> 01:16:14,449
(Target zone)

1793
01:16:14,783 --> 01:16:17,583
(A chance to catch up)

1794
01:16:18,183 --> 01:16:21,216
(Let's ride this momentum
for one more point.)

1795
01:16:34,076 --> 01:16:34,984
Service error.

1796
01:16:35,549 --> 01:16:37,249
(Disappointed sigh)

1797
01:16:37,483 --> 01:16:39,883
(A service error
at the worst possible time)

1798
01:16:40,883 --> 01:16:41,883
Just one more point!

1799
01:16:42,449 --> 01:16:43,582
(The deficit stretches back to 2 points.)

1800
01:16:43,583 --> 01:16:44,683
Shujitsu leads 11 to 9.

1801
01:16:46,549 --> 01:16:48,683
- They have to keep their composure.
- Exactly.

1802
01:16:54,716 --> 01:16:55,849
Watch the net!

1803
01:17:01,816 --> 01:17:02,748
What a break.

1804
01:17:02,749 --> 01:17:04,316
- Huge break for us.
- What a relief.

1805
01:17:04,616 --> 01:17:06,615
(The other team gives one right back.)

1806
01:17:06,616 --> 01:17:08,882
We've got an opening now.

1807
01:17:08,883 --> 01:17:10,215
Come on, Enkhsoyol.

1808
01:17:10,216 --> 01:17:11,427
Take advantage of this.

1809
01:17:12,483 --> 01:17:13,515
We're deep in set five now.

1810
01:17:13,516 --> 01:17:16,115
Back-to-back service errors...

1811
01:17:16,116 --> 01:17:17,733
just show how gassed these players are.

1812
01:17:19,649 --> 01:17:20,548
(Both sides running on fumes)

1813
01:17:20,549 --> 01:17:22,415
In the fifth set, nobody has fresh legs.

1814
01:17:22,416 --> 01:17:24,048
We're exhausted,
and they're hitting the wall too.

1815
01:17:24,049 --> 01:17:26,349
(Pushing stamina to the limit)

1816
01:17:26,649 --> 01:17:30,316
You could visibly see
the fatigue settling in.

1817
01:17:31,649 --> 01:17:33,949
(We need something to turn this around.)

1818
01:17:35,883 --> 01:17:37,086
Should we bring in Ye Eun?

1819
01:17:38,683 --> 01:17:39,916
Ye Eun!

1820
01:17:41,183 --> 01:17:42,148
Enkhsoyol, switch!

1821
01:17:42,149 --> 01:17:43,448
(Ye Eun enters the game again.)

1822
01:17:43,449 --> 01:17:45,149
We have to make something happen.

1823
01:17:45,649 --> 01:17:46,948
Lee Ye Eun checks in.

1824
01:17:46,949 --> 01:17:49,489
Back in the 2022-23 season,

1825
01:17:49,514 --> 01:17:54,415
she was part of Hi-Pass's
historic reverse sweep for the title.

1826
01:17:54,416 --> 01:17:57,015
She was the hero whose clutch serving
turned Game Three around.

1827
01:17:57,016 --> 01:17:57,916
That's right.

1828
01:17:58,749 --> 01:18:00,683
- Just rip it with confidence.
- Yes, Coach.

1829
01:18:06,416 --> 01:18:07,349
Great serve.

1830
01:18:08,649 --> 01:18:09,515
Hard swing.

1831
01:18:09,516 --> 01:18:10,783
- Dug up.
- Go for C!

1832
01:18:11,916 --> 01:18:12,916
(Set goes to Yeon Joo.)

1833
01:18:13,216 --> 01:18:14,191
Go to the edge!

1834
01:18:14,216 --> 01:18:15,049
Hwang Yeon Joo!

1835
01:18:16,916 --> 01:18:18,316
(Tap)

1836
01:18:18,616 --> 01:18:20,216
She goes for the wipe-off!

1837
01:18:25,816 --> 01:18:28,816
Down!

1838
01:18:31,983 --> 01:18:33,283
(Chu)

1839
01:18:33,949 --> 01:18:35,516
Tied up at 11 to 11!

1840
01:18:36,982 --> 01:18:39,239
(Cheering)

1841
01:18:39,549 --> 01:18:40,949
(Weak knees)

1842
01:18:42,083 --> 01:18:46,483
- Hwang Yeon Joo!
- Hwang Yeon Joo!

1843
01:18:46,649 --> 01:18:48,715
Huge touch, Yeon Joo!

1844
01:18:48,716 --> 01:18:50,348
Watch your timing.

1845
01:18:50,373 --> 01:18:53,073
Dial in the timing, no matter what.

1846
01:18:53,649 --> 01:18:56,482
Wonder Dogs weather the storm
and pull level at last.

1847
01:18:56,483 --> 01:18:57,716
Tied up at 11 to 11.

1848
01:19:01,121 --> 01:19:02,070
I'm serving.

1849
01:19:03,183 --> 01:19:04,083
- Boom!
- Boom!

1850
01:19:04,949 --> 01:19:06,449
It rattled the pass.

1851
01:19:09,316 --> 01:19:10,616
One, two!

1852
01:19:14,416 --> 01:19:15,448
Where's the cover?

1853
01:19:15,449 --> 01:19:16,683
Right through the seam.

1854
01:19:17,049 --> 01:19:19,048
Where did that land?

1855
01:19:19,049 --> 01:19:20,283
- Cut right through the block.
- In the seam?

1856
01:19:21,183 --> 01:19:23,316
(Shujitsu edges ahead by one again.)

1857
01:19:24,849 --> 01:19:29,616
(Three points away from the finish line)

1858
01:19:29,949 --> 01:19:33,316
Takiguchi Rin checks in for Shujitsu.

1859
01:19:35,516 --> 01:19:39,348
Shujitsu is looking
to generate points off the serve.

1860
01:19:39,349 --> 01:19:40,282
Right.

1861
01:19:40,283 --> 01:19:41,648
Let's go!

1862
01:19:41,649 --> 01:19:42,648
We can take this!

1863
01:19:42,649 --> 01:19:43,916
Hold your ground!

1864
01:19:44,663 --> 01:19:45,715
(Glancing)

1865
01:19:48,816 --> 01:19:50,715
Yeon Joo, bail out on number one.

1866
01:19:50,716 --> 01:19:52,083
If she cuts inside, pull your hands back.

1867
01:19:52,283 --> 01:19:54,183
(Understood.)

1868
01:19:58,749 --> 01:19:59,748
(Great pass!)

1869
01:19:59,749 --> 01:20:00,716
Chae Rim passes...

1870
01:20:01,283 --> 01:20:03,132
and transitions to hit!
A cross-court shot.

1871
01:20:05,183 --> 01:20:07,016
(Ball goes to Yoshimoto.)

1872
01:20:07,069 --> 01:20:08,070
This is it.

1873
01:20:09,483 --> 01:20:11,649
(Pulling back)

1874
01:20:21,189 --> 01:20:23,443
(Too shocked to speak)

1875
01:20:24,100 --> 01:20:24,900
Nice... wait.

1876
01:20:25,907 --> 01:20:27,373
(Everyone stands up.)

1877
01:20:27,573 --> 01:20:29,040
(Gasp)

1878
01:20:29,307 --> 01:20:30,907
(Frozen)

1879
01:20:31,373 --> 01:20:34,440
(Everyone falls silent.)

1880
01:20:34,766 --> 01:20:36,466
Throw your body at the ball!

1881
01:20:39,473 --> 01:20:41,740
(See?)

1882
01:20:42,507 --> 01:20:45,007
(It's called body-on-the-line volleyball.)

1883
01:20:46,773 --> 01:20:48,072
- My bad!
- You're good.

1884
01:20:48,073 --> 01:20:50,706
Pulling your hands back was
the 100 percent right call.

1885
01:20:50,707 --> 01:20:51,806
Right, exactly.

1886
01:20:51,807 --> 01:20:52,840
Great awareness.

1887
01:20:55,373 --> 01:20:57,772
(A bold move by a seasoned coach)

1888
01:20:57,773 --> 01:20:59,911
Yeon Joo pulled her hands away cleanly.

1889
01:20:59,936 --> 01:21:03,606
I just didn't expect the ball
to sail that far wide.

1890
01:21:03,607 --> 01:21:05,573
(A great collaboration)

1891
01:21:06,640 --> 01:21:07,707
Beautifully read.

1892
01:21:07,993 --> 01:21:10,499
I never could have imagined...

1893
01:21:10,973 --> 01:21:12,872
Yeon Joo and I would be here as mentors,

1894
01:21:12,873 --> 01:21:14,536
with Yeon Joo out there
battling on the court.

1895
01:21:14,673 --> 01:21:17,917
Seeing something
I never even dreamed of...

1896
01:21:17,942 --> 01:21:20,709
play out in real life is unbelievable.

1897
01:21:20,851 --> 01:21:22,631
I'm just so grateful...

1898
01:21:22,656 --> 01:21:25,284
that I could come through for Yeon Koung.

1899
01:21:25,943 --> 01:21:30,109
(The Yeon sisters' dynamic is
as strong as ever.)

1900
01:21:30,851 --> 01:21:32,617
(Fifth set, Shujitsu High 12
: Wonder Dogs 12)

1901
01:21:32,642 --> 01:21:34,042
Knotted up at 12 to 12.

1902
01:21:39,818 --> 01:21:40,650
Spike.

1903
01:21:40,651 --> 01:21:41,484
Nice dig!

1904
01:21:42,284 --> 01:21:43,051
Hwang Yeon Joo.

1905
01:21:44,451 --> 01:21:45,283
- A roll shot.
- Left!

1906
01:21:45,284 --> 01:21:46,450
Dug up in the back row.

1907
01:21:46,451 --> 01:21:47,317
Pushed out to the left!

1908
01:21:47,318 --> 01:21:48,217
(Yoshimoto flies once more.)

1909
01:21:48,218 --> 01:21:51,018
Number one!

1910
01:21:52,451 --> 01:21:53,751
(Pulls away)

1911
01:21:57,684 --> 01:21:58,451
Out.

1912
01:21:59,018 --> 01:22:00,051
That's out!

1913
01:22:02,018 --> 01:22:03,417
Yeon Joo!

1914
01:22:03,418 --> 01:22:04,184
Nice one!

1915
01:22:09,351 --> 01:22:10,384
What a read.

1916
01:22:12,151 --> 01:22:13,818
(In)

1917
01:22:14,651 --> 01:22:15,698
Wait, that wasn't out?

1918
01:22:16,884 --> 01:22:17,718
(It's not out?)

1919
01:22:17,984 --> 01:22:19,150
Is it in?

1920
01:22:19,151 --> 01:22:21,217
- That sailed out!
- It's out!

1921
01:22:21,218 --> 01:22:22,817
- That was clearly out.
- Why?

1922
01:22:22,818 --> 01:22:23,684
Out!

1923
01:22:24,051 --> 01:22:25,818
- That went out.
- No way.

1924
01:22:26,818 --> 01:22:28,084
Coach Kim asks for a video review.

1925
01:22:29,384 --> 01:22:31,650
(Please)

1926
01:22:31,651 --> 01:22:32,681
Come on.

1927
01:22:33,818 --> 01:22:35,317
It clipped the line.

1928
01:22:35,618 --> 01:22:37,384
Shake it off.
That definitely caught the line.

1929
01:22:42,627 --> 01:22:43,425
(Right on the line)

1930
01:22:43,451 --> 01:22:44,551
It's in.

1931
01:22:46,751 --> 01:22:49,851
(Fifth set, Shujitsu High 13
: Wonder Dogs 12)

1932
01:22:50,051 --> 01:22:51,351
Good no-call.

1933
01:22:54,351 --> 01:22:55,971
Let's get this side-out right here.

1934
01:22:57,384 --> 01:22:58,783
Shujitsu leads 13 to 12.

1935
01:22:58,784 --> 01:22:59,742
Just a single point in it.

1936
01:23:01,460 --> 01:23:02,693
Get your feet under you for the pass!

1937
01:23:02,718 --> 01:23:04,146
Watch the drop!

1938
01:23:04,318 --> 01:23:05,483
Watch for the short floater!

1939
01:23:05,484 --> 01:23:07,417
- Secure the first contact!
- Got it.

1940
01:23:07,418 --> 01:23:10,551
(A fierce competition for a single point)

1941
01:23:11,584 --> 01:23:12,451
(Huff)

1942
01:23:14,218 --> 01:23:15,151
Kato Uta serves.

1943
01:23:17,618 --> 01:23:18,617
Ye Eun handles it.

1944
01:23:18,618 --> 01:23:19,495
Set me a B.

1945
01:23:20,751 --> 01:23:21,584
A back pass.

1946
01:23:21,851 --> 01:23:23,017
(Ruse worked.)

1947
01:23:23,018 --> 01:23:23,883
There it is.

1948
01:23:23,884 --> 01:23:24,783
Mine!

1949
01:23:24,808 --> 01:23:26,242
(Yeon Joo ready to strike)

1950
01:23:30,418 --> 01:23:31,983
Yeon Joo tooled the block perfectly.

1951
01:23:31,984 --> 01:23:33,518
(Block touch-out to score)

1952
01:23:34,418 --> 01:23:35,751
Yeon Joo!

1953
01:23:36,151 --> 01:23:38,784
(Yeon Joo ties the score.)

1954
01:23:42,984 --> 01:23:44,683
She's deliberately
tooling the outside hand...

1955
01:23:44,684 --> 01:23:48,184
so their back row has zero chance
of picking it up.

1956
01:23:55,751 --> 01:23:57,718
It's okay.

1957
01:24:00,484 --> 01:24:01,783
(Shujitsu High 13 : Wonder Dogs 13)

1958
01:24:01,784 --> 01:24:02,950
(The match goes back to square one.)

1959
01:24:02,951 --> 01:24:04,018
Deadlocked at 13 to 13!

1960
01:24:07,518 --> 01:24:08,784
(Glance)

1961
01:24:10,451 --> 01:24:11,550
Natsuki.

1962
01:24:11,551 --> 01:24:13,250
No, hold on.

1963
01:24:13,251 --> 01:24:14,883
Do we still make the move?

1964
01:24:15,084 --> 01:24:17,984
(Miki considers a substitute.)

1965
01:24:20,184 --> 01:24:22,684
(Yeon Koung doesn't hesitate
to switch out.)

1966
01:24:23,612 --> 01:24:24,750
Great job!

1967
01:24:24,751 --> 01:24:26,450
Ha Hyo Rim checks out,

1968
01:24:26,451 --> 01:24:28,351
and Yoon Young In comes in.

1969
01:24:29,251 --> 01:24:31,017
You did great.

1970
01:24:31,018 --> 01:24:31,883
Where's Bo Been?

1971
01:24:31,908 --> 01:24:34,308
- Bo Been, run the offense!
- Yes, Coach.

1972
01:24:36,018 --> 01:24:38,618
(During strategy meeting
before the fifth set)

1973
01:24:38,918 --> 01:24:40,476
She matches up way better here
than Ye Dam.

1974
01:24:40,951 --> 01:24:42,426
- Let's go with Young In.
- Rather than Ye Dam...

1975
01:24:42,451 --> 01:24:44,288
(Young In for better blocks)

1976
01:24:44,313 --> 01:24:45,447
- I'll get her ready.
- Good.

1977
01:24:45,768 --> 01:24:48,236
She'll play as a blocker,
but she'll also attack when needed.

1978
01:24:48,237 --> 01:24:49,017
Exactly.

1979
01:24:49,472 --> 01:24:51,173
One block, one dig.

1980
01:24:51,174 --> 01:24:52,040
(Stop them with a block or...)

1981
01:24:52,142 --> 01:24:53,221
Attack from the right.

1982
01:24:53,710 --> 01:24:56,111
(get past the block.)

1983
01:24:56,688 --> 01:24:57,981
(Get to match point first.)

1984
01:24:57,982 --> 01:25:00,349
It's 13 to 13, and Yeon Joo is serving.

1985
01:25:01,284 --> 01:25:03,118
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

1986
01:25:03,119 --> 01:25:04,019
- Boom.
- Boom.

1987
01:25:04,721 --> 01:25:05,800
Right side!

1988
01:25:06,102 --> 01:25:06,902
(That's it!)

1989
01:25:09,492 --> 01:25:10,425
Heavy hit!

1990
01:25:12,796 --> 01:25:14,309
She breaks right through the block!

1991
01:25:14,497 --> 01:25:15,397
Nice job.

1992
01:25:15,899 --> 01:25:17,445
- She keeps it alive!
- That's it!

1993
01:25:17,634 --> 01:25:18,500
Young In.

1994
01:25:18,835 --> 01:25:20,502
- Chae Rim.
- Young In sets it up.

1995
01:25:20,503 --> 01:25:21,303
You have to put it down!

1996
01:25:21,304 --> 01:25:23,205
- Hit it!
- Put it away!

1997
01:25:23,206 --> 01:25:25,353
Just one more point. We can do this!

1998
01:25:26,874 --> 01:25:28,343
(Fighting determination
with determination)

1999
01:25:28,344 --> 01:25:29,244
Come on!

2000
01:25:30,880 --> 01:25:31,593
Left!

2001
01:25:32,252 --> 01:25:32,882
It's going left!

2002
01:25:32,906 --> 01:25:33,730
Watch number one!

2003
01:25:33,762 --> 01:25:34,496
Young In, please!

2004
01:25:34,851 --> 01:25:35,898
One, two.

2005
01:25:36,219 --> 01:25:37,386
One, two.

2006
01:25:37,707 --> 01:25:38,382
Touch!

2007
01:25:38,419 --> 01:25:39,320
Spike!

2008
01:25:40,990 --> 01:25:42,023
Dug up!

2009
01:25:42,024 --> 01:25:42,937
That's right!

2010
01:25:43,092 --> 01:25:44,065
(Let's go.)

2011
01:25:44,090 --> 01:25:44,973
Set a C-quick!

2012
01:25:45,447 --> 01:25:47,062
(Chae Rim gets ready again.)

2013
01:25:47,063 --> 01:25:47,896
Chae Rim!

2014
01:25:47,897 --> 01:25:49,131
- Swing through!
- Come on!

2015
01:25:49,132 --> 01:25:50,232
You have to take the swing!

2016
01:25:50,233 --> 01:25:51,133
Stay calm.

2017
01:25:51,734 --> 01:25:52,447
Hit it!

2018
01:25:52,702 --> 01:25:54,182
Swing!

2019
01:25:54,207 --> 01:25:56,613
(They need to reach match point.)

2020
01:25:57,774 --> 01:25:58,907
Chae Rim tips it over.

2021
01:26:00,276 --> 01:26:01,176
Swing through!

2022
01:26:01,911 --> 01:26:03,311
Please, just keep it in play!

2023
01:26:03,312 --> 01:26:05,146
Oh, no.

2024
01:26:07,321 --> 01:26:09,584
(Squeezing their eyes shut)

2025
01:26:09,585 --> 01:26:11,653
Chae Rim rolls it over.

2026
01:26:14,671 --> 01:26:16,051
(Trembling)

2027
01:26:18,804 --> 01:26:23,346
(What made the difference was...)

2028
01:26:23,787 --> 01:26:25,254
(Oh, no.)

2029
01:26:27,096 --> 01:26:28,030
(one unforced error.)

2030
01:26:28,062 --> 01:26:29,028
Another unforced error.

2031
01:26:32,146 --> 01:26:33,836
(Shujitsu at match point)

2032
01:26:34,551 --> 01:26:35,456
Oh, no.

2033
01:26:36,352 --> 01:26:37,686
(A quick glance)

2034
01:26:43,786 --> 01:26:45,120
I mean...

2035
01:26:45,121 --> 01:26:46,901
I played way too passively there.

2036
01:26:47,624 --> 01:26:49,103
I regret that so much.

2037
01:26:51,834 --> 01:26:54,736
(After all those unforced errors...)

2038
01:26:55,101 --> 01:26:56,368
I'm so sorry.

2039
01:26:56,762 --> 01:26:59,564
(The attacks were getting
more and more cautious.)

2040
01:26:59,639 --> 01:27:00,639
Chae Rim.

2041
01:27:00,640 --> 01:27:02,674
- Adjust the angle and finish the play.
- Chae Rim!

2042
01:27:02,675 --> 01:27:05,377
We can still do this.

2043
01:27:05,378 --> 01:27:08,346
I felt the weight of every single point.

2044
01:27:09,695 --> 01:27:13,565
(Trapped in Shujitsu's shackles,)

2045
01:27:15,321 --> 01:27:17,232
(she's mentally overwhelmed.)

2046
01:27:17,757 --> 01:27:20,258
Things were slipping away,
and I got tunnel vision.

2047
01:27:24,497 --> 01:27:25,430
Hey.

2048
01:27:26,098 --> 01:27:26,998
Chae Rim.

2049
01:27:30,002 --> 01:27:31,013
Chae Rim.

2050
01:27:31,771 --> 01:27:32,737
Chae Rim.

2051
01:27:36,227 --> 01:27:37,093
Hey.

2052
01:27:37,885 --> 01:27:39,587
Chae Rim, you're fine!

2053
01:27:40,066 --> 01:27:41,522
Chae Rim, you're fine!

2054
01:27:41,547 --> 01:27:42,947
(Nods)

2055
01:27:45,618 --> 01:27:46,785
It's okay!

2056
01:27:47,600 --> 01:27:49,228
(You did well.)

2057
01:27:49,822 --> 01:27:50,622
(Mental coaching)

2058
01:27:50,623 --> 01:27:52,157
(Deep breath)

2059
01:27:52,158 --> 01:27:53,792
You're okay, Chae Rim. Go again!

2060
01:27:54,060 --> 01:27:55,060
(Taps)

2061
01:27:55,061 --> 01:27:56,395
Let's get this side-out.

2062
01:27:58,030 --> 01:27:59,298
Just this one.

2063
01:27:59,299 --> 01:28:00,365
Just one point.

2064
01:28:00,733 --> 01:28:01,900
(Fifth set, Shujitsu High 14
: Wonder Dogs 13)

2065
01:28:01,901 --> 01:28:02,867
Let's go!

2066
01:28:02,868 --> 01:28:05,277
(We'll get one together.)

2067
01:28:05,951 --> 01:28:08,753
(The match isn't over.)

2068
01:28:08,875 --> 01:28:12,110
I genuinely thought
we could still win this.

2069
01:28:12,577 --> 01:28:14,811
I was so grateful when they told me...

2070
01:28:15,039 --> 01:28:17,140
it was okay and that they had my back.

2071
01:28:18,116 --> 01:28:21,302
Just because my attacks aren't falling
doesn't mean...

2072
01:28:21,675 --> 01:28:23,231
I can't contribute in other ways.

2073
01:28:23,256 --> 01:28:25,090
I'm getting this done.

2074
01:28:25,091 --> 01:28:26,542
(Determined)

2075
01:28:27,793 --> 01:28:30,161
Float serve, move your feet!

2076
01:28:30,463 --> 01:28:31,730
Get it on the first pass!

2077
01:28:31,731 --> 01:28:32,898
(One, two)

2078
01:28:37,508 --> 01:28:38,546
Left!

2079
01:28:39,453 --> 01:28:42,071
(Chae Rim is the serving target.)

2080
01:28:42,341 --> 01:28:43,475
Let's go!

2081
01:28:44,877 --> 01:28:46,712
Will Shujitsu close out the match?

2082
01:28:46,737 --> 01:28:48,590
I've got the back row.
Watch the short ball!

2083
01:28:49,315 --> 01:28:51,684
Or can the Wonder Dogs force a deuce?

2084
01:28:52,078 --> 01:28:53,845
Match point for Shujitsu.

2085
01:28:57,056 --> 01:28:58,890
- Mine!
- Feet moving!

2086
01:28:59,659 --> 01:29:00,949
They're colliding on the pass!

2087
01:29:00,950 --> 01:29:02,994
- That's it!
- Just one!

2088
01:29:02,995 --> 01:29:05,230
(If they can't receive it, it's over.)

2089
01:29:05,307 --> 01:29:07,208
Just because my spikes aren't working
doesn't mean...

2090
01:29:07,233 --> 01:29:08,977
I can't contribute in other ways.

2091
01:29:10,069 --> 01:29:11,168
Chae Rim makes a clutch pass.

2092
01:29:11,571 --> 01:29:12,437
Put it down.

2093
01:29:12,438 --> 01:29:14,204
Quick attack! That's right.

2094
01:29:14,228 --> 01:29:14,740
She's up.

2095
01:29:14,741 --> 01:29:15,807
(A fast approach for the quick attack)

2096
01:29:16,976 --> 01:29:18,310
Touch!

2097
01:29:19,311 --> 01:29:20,812
Off the block and out. Kim Bo Been!

2098
01:29:20,813 --> 01:29:21,746
There it is!

2099
01:29:22,882 --> 01:29:24,583
(Fifth set, Shujitsu High 14
: Wonder Dogs 14)

2100
01:29:24,584 --> 01:29:25,951
- Great job!
- Nice job!

2101
01:29:26,252 --> 01:29:28,153
(The match isn't over yet.)

2102
01:29:28,554 --> 01:29:31,639
- Yes!
- Let's go!

2103
01:29:31,664 --> 01:29:34,592
- Great work!
- Thanks, everyone!

2104
01:29:35,063 --> 01:29:37,722
(Thank goodness.)

2105
01:29:38,689 --> 01:29:41,257
(Thankfully, they're level again.)

2106
01:29:43,135 --> 01:29:45,970
(Gritting her teeth)

2107
01:29:46,912 --> 01:29:48,874
That was way too close.

2108
01:29:48,875 --> 01:29:49,809
(Barely brushing the ball)

2109
01:29:49,810 --> 01:29:52,344
Touched off the outside fingers, right?

2110
01:29:53,512 --> 01:29:55,413
(That was a close one.)

2111
01:29:57,083 --> 01:29:59,718
What a scare. My heart almost dropped.

2112
01:30:00,145 --> 01:30:01,995
(I can't watch.)

2113
01:30:02,088 --> 01:30:03,198
We're deep in set five.

2114
01:30:04,457 --> 01:30:07,259
Every single rally in this deciding set
is a battle.

2115
01:30:07,792 --> 01:30:09,403
Hopefully they can ride this momentum...

2116
01:30:09,428 --> 01:30:11,263
after clawing back from the brink.

2117
01:30:11,264 --> 01:30:12,768
In their very first match,

2118
01:30:12,792 --> 01:30:15,466
they've pushed it all the way
to a fifth-set deuce.

2119
01:30:15,467 --> 01:30:16,211
Exactly.

2120
01:30:17,069 --> 01:30:19,600
(Deuce: When the score is tied
with one point left to win,)

2121
01:30:19,601 --> 01:30:21,572
(a team must score
two consecutive points to win.)

2122
01:30:22,881 --> 01:30:25,086
- Stay locked in. We're okay!
- Let's go!

2123
01:30:29,133 --> 01:30:31,768
(A substitution during deuce)

2124
01:30:32,317 --> 01:30:34,618
(Again?)

2125
01:30:36,322 --> 01:30:38,266
- Enkhsoyol, swing hard!
- Fast swing!

2126
01:30:38,291 --> 01:30:39,000
Sure.

2127
01:30:39,759 --> 01:30:41,525
Enkhsoyol, trust yourself and go for it!

2128
01:30:41,526 --> 01:30:42,904
- You have to swing through!
- Got it!

2129
01:30:43,897 --> 01:30:45,474
Onishi versus Enkhsoyol.

2130
01:30:45,631 --> 01:30:48,434
Coach Kim's tactical substitution
matches them up once again.

2131
01:30:49,101 --> 01:30:50,112
Enkhsoyol.

2132
01:30:50,236 --> 01:30:52,547
- Target number two!
- Got It!

2133
01:30:53,739 --> 01:30:55,417
Let's go, Onishi!

2134
01:30:56,041 --> 01:30:56,918
Okay!

2135
01:30:58,178 --> 01:30:59,821
- Aim for number two!
- Got it.

2136
01:30:59,846 --> 01:31:01,313
(You always run into your enemies
at deuce.)

2137
01:31:01,314 --> 01:31:02,981
Come on, just two more points!

2138
01:31:02,982 --> 01:31:05,150
Pass it clean, please!

2139
01:31:05,151 --> 01:31:06,828
- Please!
- Just get a clean pass!

2140
01:31:07,253 --> 01:31:08,820
(Deep breath)

2141
01:31:08,955 --> 01:31:10,722
This next point is everything.

2142
01:31:10,723 --> 01:31:11,589
(Chae Rim serves carefully.)

2143
01:31:13,293 --> 01:31:16,395
- One block, one dig!
- Young In, where's your spot?

2144
01:31:16,396 --> 01:31:17,429
Over here!

2145
01:31:17,496 --> 01:31:18,963
Right here, number two!

2146
01:31:19,632 --> 01:31:21,199
Onishi!

2147
01:31:22,435 --> 01:31:24,569
One, two!

2148
01:31:24,570 --> 01:31:25,847
Onishi rises up!

2149
01:31:26,539 --> 01:31:27,706
She hits through the seam!

2150
01:31:27,707 --> 01:31:29,307
(The block is broken through.)

2151
01:31:31,617 --> 01:31:32,854
Please!

2152
01:31:33,879 --> 01:31:35,079
- Out!
- Out!

2153
01:31:35,080 --> 01:31:36,380
Long!

2154
01:31:36,381 --> 01:31:37,682
Out!

2155
01:31:39,819 --> 01:31:43,122
(The ace made an attacking error.)

2156
01:31:43,123 --> 01:31:46,858
No touch, no touch!

2157
01:31:46,859 --> 01:31:49,961
(Frozen in place)

2158
01:31:55,734 --> 01:31:57,602
(It feels like being
192 centimeters tall.)

2159
01:31:58,237 --> 01:31:59,514
Yes!

2160
01:32:00,308 --> 01:32:02,183
It's out!

2161
01:32:03,042 --> 01:32:04,009
(Fifth set, Shujitsu High 14
: Wonder Dogs 15)

2162
01:32:04,010 --> 01:32:04,876
Great read!

2163
01:32:05,277 --> 01:32:06,778
(The coaching staff on the bench)

2164
01:32:06,779 --> 01:32:07,712
Awesome job!

2165
01:32:07,713 --> 01:32:09,881
(Now, the Wonder Dogs have the momentum.)

2166
01:32:10,449 --> 01:32:11,460
(The warm-up zone)

2167
01:32:11,484 --> 01:32:12,317
(Just 1 point to victory)

2168
01:32:12,318 --> 01:32:17,456
(Players' friends and family
in the stands)

2169
01:32:17,623 --> 01:32:18,890
Hey!

2170
01:32:19,291 --> 01:32:20,124
Hey!

2171
01:32:20,526 --> 01:32:22,360
Just one more! Dial in your timing!

2172
01:32:23,395 --> 01:32:25,496
Block and dig!

2173
01:32:28,667 --> 01:32:30,067
Cover the roll shots.

2174
01:32:31,136 --> 01:32:33,170
(Unwavering)

2175
01:32:34,707 --> 01:32:36,441
It's fine. Stay loose.

2176
01:32:36,442 --> 01:32:38,743
Shake it off.

2177
01:32:41,146 --> 01:32:43,748
- One point at a time.
- You can do it!

2178
01:32:44,582 --> 01:32:45,949
(Shujitsu is...)

2179
01:32:45,974 --> 01:32:48,509
(putting its faith in its exhausted ace.)

2180
01:32:50,235 --> 01:32:54,438
(The exhausting final stretch
of the fifth set)

2181
01:32:55,427 --> 01:32:56,894
Hang in there, team!

2182
01:32:56,895 --> 01:32:58,363
(All they need is...)

2183
01:32:58,364 --> 01:32:59,430
Please.

2184
01:32:59,799 --> 01:33:01,333
(just one point.)

2185
01:33:01,358 --> 01:33:02,668
All focus on this rally.

2186
01:33:03,836 --> 01:33:06,638
From here on out,
they're playing for match point.

2187
01:33:06,639 --> 01:33:07,539
Exactly.

2188
01:33:07,540 --> 01:33:10,341
(The final chapter of an intense battle)

2189
01:33:10,488 --> 01:33:11,121
(Sigh)

2190
01:33:11,803 --> 01:33:14,091
(Back Chae Rim serves.)

2191
01:33:16,348 --> 01:33:17,214
Nice!

2192
01:33:18,150 --> 01:33:20,318
(Onishi gets ready to attack.)

2193
01:33:20,371 --> 01:33:23,239
Slide over, Bo Been!

2194
01:33:23,656 --> 01:33:24,554
Spike!

2195
01:33:24,578 --> 01:33:25,333
Stuffed!

2196
01:33:25,491 --> 01:33:26,424
Kim Bo Been coming up huge!

2197
01:33:26,425 --> 01:33:27,425
That's it!

2198
01:33:29,595 --> 01:33:31,062
What a dig!

2199
01:33:31,697 --> 01:33:32,897
Here it comes again!

2200
01:33:32,898 --> 01:33:34,032
Mine!

2201
01:33:34,333 --> 01:33:35,633
- Onishi!
- Onishi!

2202
01:33:35,634 --> 01:33:36,745
They go back to her!

2203
01:33:36,869 --> 01:33:38,480
Onishi rising for another swing.

2204
01:33:39,338 --> 01:33:40,338
Crushed!

2205
01:33:40,339 --> 01:33:41,306
Dug up!

2206
01:33:41,974 --> 01:33:42,840
Enkhsoyol!

2207
01:33:42,841 --> 01:33:45,043
Wonder Dogs counter! Enkhsoyol!

2208
01:33:45,511 --> 01:33:46,411
(Jumps to his feet)

2209
01:33:46,412 --> 01:33:48,213
- Please!
- Enkhsoyol!

2210
01:33:48,514 --> 01:33:49,380
Enkhsoyol.

2211
01:33:49,415 --> 01:33:50,625
Enkhsoyol, finish it!

2212
01:33:50,883 --> 01:33:51,783
Enkhsoyol!

2213
01:33:53,385 --> 01:33:54,618
Didn't get all of it!

2214
01:33:54,954 --> 01:33:56,521
(A missed opportunity)

2215
01:33:58,691 --> 01:34:00,091
Free ball!

2216
01:34:00,798 --> 01:34:03,166
(Seizing the opportunity)

2217
01:34:03,414 --> 01:34:04,681
Stay on your toes!

2218
01:34:07,299 --> 01:34:08,243
Onishi!

2219
01:34:08,567 --> 01:34:09,844
Mine! Left side!

2220
01:34:11,642 --> 01:34:12,580
Come on!

2221
01:34:13,873 --> 01:34:15,006
Onishi!

2222
01:34:15,207 --> 01:34:16,274
One, two!

2223
01:34:16,275 --> 01:34:17,475
Watch the tip!

2224
01:34:21,990 --> 01:34:24,091
She just keeps hammering away
without showing any fatigue.

2225
01:34:24,116 --> 01:34:25,049
(Full power throughout the fifth set)

2226
01:34:25,229 --> 01:34:26,585
(Hit like a zombie.)

2227
01:34:26,586 --> 01:34:28,506
Hang in there!

2228
01:34:28,530 --> 01:34:29,821
(Hold on like a zombie.)

2229
01:34:30,155 --> 01:34:31,967
Watch the jump timing!

2230
01:34:32,224 --> 01:34:34,603
Take a breath.
Look for the split in the court.

2231
01:34:34,626 --> 01:34:35,570
Move it fast!

2232
01:34:36,462 --> 01:34:37,462
Full swing!

2233
01:34:37,463 --> 01:34:39,064
(They lose the point off the block.)

2234
01:34:39,531 --> 01:34:41,198
(I knew you could do it.)

2235
01:34:41,800 --> 01:34:43,734
(The ace got the better of them.)

2236
01:34:44,606 --> 01:34:45,673
(Fifth set, Shujitsu High 15
: Wonder Dogs 15)

2237
01:34:45,698 --> 01:34:47,931
- Nice!
- One more! Thanks!

2238
01:34:48,532 --> 01:34:50,918
Nice play, Onishi.

2239
01:34:52,373 --> 01:34:53,573
Dang it!

2240
01:34:54,666 --> 01:34:56,966
(Failed to end the match)

2241
01:34:57,939 --> 01:34:59,839
(Sigh)

2242
01:35:00,839 --> 01:35:03,073
(This isn't how it's supposed to be.)

2243
01:35:04,073 --> 01:35:05,806
You have to swing!

2244
01:35:06,739 --> 01:35:07,773
Put it away!

2245
01:35:09,864 --> 01:35:10,638
Got it.

2246
01:35:12,173 --> 01:35:13,539
(Sigh)

2247
01:35:15,221 --> 01:35:18,939
At that point in the match,
I had to take the swing.

2248
01:35:19,293 --> 01:35:23,493
No matter how many times she gets blocked,
she keeps coming back until she scores.

2249
01:35:24,006 --> 01:35:25,206
Swing through!

2250
01:35:26,106 --> 01:35:30,173
I knew I had to step up and deliver.

2251
01:35:32,774 --> 01:35:34,454
- Wonder Dogs!
- Wonder Dogs!

2252
01:35:35,439 --> 01:35:36,339
It's 15 to 15.

2253
01:35:36,980 --> 01:35:37,980
Deuce again.

2254
01:35:40,706 --> 01:35:42,773
(Glaring)

2255
01:35:43,339 --> 01:35:44,539
It's okay.

2256
01:35:46,143 --> 01:35:46,914
(A high-stakes, one-point battle)

2257
01:35:46,939 --> 01:35:48,476
Number two is coming!

2258
01:35:48,673 --> 01:35:50,872
- Keep your eyes on number two.
- More aggressively.

2259
01:35:50,873 --> 01:35:52,405
Enkhsoyol, you've got to terminate.

2260
01:35:52,406 --> 01:35:53,273
Got it!

2261
01:35:58,173 --> 01:35:59,806
They have to get this side-out.

2262
01:36:00,339 --> 01:36:02,123
- Mine!
- Okay, cover.

2263
01:36:02,239 --> 01:36:02,857
Set it up.

2264
01:36:03,173 --> 01:36:04,072
Bo Been!

2265
01:36:04,097 --> 01:36:05,197
Bo Been is open.

2266
01:36:05,379 --> 01:36:06,745
- There it is.
- Looks good.

2267
01:36:07,873 --> 01:36:08,872
Set it up.

2268
01:36:08,873 --> 01:36:10,006
(Sliding to a halt)

2269
01:36:10,273 --> 01:36:11,673
(Enkhsoyol?)

2270
01:36:11,839 --> 01:36:12,772
(Rising up...)

2271
01:36:12,773 --> 01:36:13,738
(to face a double block)

2272
01:36:13,739 --> 01:36:14,639
Not working.

2273
01:36:16,806 --> 01:36:19,739
(Over the double block)

2274
01:36:20,273 --> 01:36:21,272
(Over Onishi)

2275
01:36:21,273 --> 01:36:22,905
Keep your eyes on the ball!

2276
01:36:22,906 --> 01:36:23,773
Swing!

2277
01:36:24,039 --> 01:36:25,073
Put it down!

2278
01:36:26,775 --> 01:36:27,857
Enkhsoyol!

2279
01:36:27,882 --> 01:36:29,081
(Powering through the double block)

2280
01:36:29,106 --> 01:36:30,305
Keep swinging just like that!

2281
01:36:30,330 --> 01:36:31,786
- Don't roll it.
- I'll swing.

2282
01:36:32,039 --> 01:36:32,939
(Proud)

2283
01:36:33,739 --> 01:36:34,906
Great pass!

2284
01:36:36,173 --> 01:36:39,339
Enkhsoyol is carrying the offense.

2285
01:36:41,039 --> 01:36:43,538
(Enkhsoyol strikes back.)

2286
01:36:43,539 --> 01:36:44,772
There it is!

2287
01:36:44,797 --> 01:36:47,663
(Deep into deuce)

2288
01:36:49,881 --> 01:36:51,305
You've got to swing like that!

2289
01:36:51,306 --> 01:36:53,739
You're way above them. Just rip it!

2290
01:36:54,139 --> 01:36:55,005
I will.

2291
01:36:55,006 --> 01:36:57,006
(Nodding)

2292
01:36:57,839 --> 01:37:01,173
Match point for the Wonder Dogs.

2293
01:37:01,539 --> 01:37:03,205
Enkhsoyol, don't drop your elbow.

2294
01:37:03,206 --> 01:37:04,705
Enkhsoyol, we're feeding you every ball.

2295
01:37:04,706 --> 01:37:05,505
- Stay ready.
- Okay.

2296
01:37:05,506 --> 01:37:07,272
- Let's back up Enkhsoyol!
- One more point!

2297
01:37:07,273 --> 01:37:09,006
(Wonder Dogs completely locked in)

2298
01:37:09,739 --> 01:37:11,839
(There is always a gap in the court.)

2299
01:37:12,273 --> 01:37:14,306
(Just one point away from victory)

2300
01:37:15,973 --> 01:37:17,205
(Kim Bo Been the Light serves.)

2301
01:37:17,206 --> 01:37:19,605
Watch number two.
I've got this line covered.

2302
01:37:19,606 --> 01:37:20,939
Cover her up!

2303
01:37:21,506 --> 01:37:23,239
(Kim Bo Been's family cheering her on)

2304
01:37:28,706 --> 01:37:30,038
Long!

2305
01:37:30,039 --> 01:37:31,306
(Costly error!)

2306
01:37:32,039 --> 01:37:35,173
(Fifth set, Shujitsu High 16
: Wonder Dogs 16)

2307
01:37:36,473 --> 01:37:37,451
Shoot.

2308
01:37:39,239 --> 01:37:41,239
My heart is in my throat.

2309
01:37:43,573 --> 01:37:44,325
In!

2310
01:37:44,806 --> 01:37:45,960
Wait, is it out?

2311
01:37:46,639 --> 01:37:48,006
Out!

2312
01:37:49,373 --> 01:37:51,473
(A recurring mistake...)

2313
01:37:52,106 --> 01:37:53,672
(turns into a fatal break.)

2314
01:37:53,673 --> 01:37:55,439
This is pure agony.

2315
01:37:56,373 --> 01:37:57,805
Triple deuce!

2316
01:37:58,839 --> 01:37:59,640
Oh, no...

2317
01:38:00,406 --> 01:38:01,506
My fault.

2318
01:38:04,431 --> 01:38:06,472
How do I get that point back?

2319
01:38:06,497 --> 01:38:07,530
My fault.

2320
01:38:07,771 --> 01:38:08,948
We'll focus on the next one.

2321
01:38:08,973 --> 01:38:09,938
Take a breath.

2322
01:38:09,939 --> 01:38:11,339
- It's just one missed serve.
- Yes, Coach.

2323
01:38:13,206 --> 01:38:14,972
When the pressure is this suffocating,

2324
01:38:14,973 --> 01:38:16,672
you can only focus on the next ball.

2325
01:38:16,673 --> 01:38:18,838
All we can do is play the next point.

2326
01:38:18,839 --> 01:38:19,939
(Eyes on the next point, not the last.)

2327
01:38:20,473 --> 01:38:22,773
Her serves are fast.

2328
01:38:24,806 --> 01:38:25,705
One more point!

2329
01:38:25,706 --> 01:38:27,838
This floater is coming in slow.

2330
01:38:27,839 --> 01:38:29,873
- Just lock in on this one point.
- Let's do it.

2331
01:38:30,639 --> 01:38:32,106
They need to pick themselves back up.

2332
01:38:32,173 --> 01:38:33,773
Nice serve, Mei!

2333
01:38:35,506 --> 01:38:37,111
Pass it perfectly!

2334
01:38:37,473 --> 01:38:40,072
No, we have to finish it
while Enkhsoyol is in the front row.

2335
01:38:40,073 --> 01:38:41,505
To get Enkhsoyol in rhythm,

2336
01:38:41,506 --> 01:38:43,372
Back Chae Rim has to deliver a clean set.

2337
01:38:43,373 --> 01:38:45,672
Keep eyes on number two.
I've got the sideline!

2338
01:38:45,673 --> 01:38:46,505
Chae Rim!

2339
01:38:46,506 --> 01:38:48,438
Cover Enkhsoyol.

2340
01:38:48,439 --> 01:38:49,505
Got it!

2341
01:38:49,506 --> 01:38:50,705
Let's do it.

2342
01:38:50,706 --> 01:38:52,526
- Chae Rim, give Enkhsoyol the call.
- Okay.

2343
01:38:53,973 --> 01:38:55,806
Watch for the roll shot from the left pin.

2344
01:38:56,239 --> 01:38:58,973
Every single second is agonizing.

2345
01:38:59,906 --> 01:39:00,972
(I can barely look.)

2346
01:39:00,973 --> 01:39:03,139
Stay composed, Mei! Just get the serve in!

2347
01:39:03,439 --> 01:39:04,206
Mine!

2348
01:39:08,803 --> 01:39:10,190
(Cheering in relief)

2349
01:39:11,673 --> 01:39:13,838
(Shujitsu serves into the net.)

2350
01:39:13,839 --> 01:39:15,606
Service error!

2351
01:39:17,273 --> 01:39:18,873
(What just happened?)

2352
01:39:19,839 --> 01:39:21,473
(A lucky break)

2353
01:39:21,739 --> 01:39:22,706
(Chuckling)

2354
01:39:25,806 --> 01:39:27,639
That was...

2355
01:39:28,006 --> 01:39:29,006
What a gift.

2356
01:39:30,373 --> 01:39:32,239
Just one more point!

2357
01:39:33,973 --> 01:39:36,306
(Fifth set, Shujitsu High 16
: Wonder Dogs 17)

2358
01:39:36,673 --> 01:39:38,406
Let's go, Wonder Dogs!

2359
01:39:40,906 --> 01:39:42,106
This is so brutal.

2360
01:39:43,339 --> 01:39:45,072
Let's go, Wonder Dogs!

2361
01:39:45,073 --> 01:39:46,106
Come on!

2362
01:39:46,339 --> 01:39:47,839
One final point!

2363
01:39:49,706 --> 01:39:51,218
Another match point!

2364
01:39:51,253 --> 01:39:53,203
(Third match point for the Wonder Dogs)

2365
01:39:54,739 --> 01:39:56,857
- Let's go!
- Stay patient.

2366
01:39:57,632 --> 01:39:58,726
Take your time.

2367
01:39:58,748 --> 01:40:00,211
(Exhaling deeply)

2368
01:40:00,235 --> 01:40:02,005
My legs felt like lead.

2369
01:40:02,006 --> 01:40:05,065
My palms were burning,
and I could barely breathe.

2370
01:40:06,133 --> 01:40:07,433
Chae Rim!

2371
01:40:07,806 --> 01:40:10,405
Focus, you hear me?

2372
01:40:10,579 --> 01:40:12,279
We end it right here!

2373
01:40:13,201 --> 01:40:16,067
If even one of us lets up,
we lose this match.

2374
01:40:16,334 --> 01:40:17,966
(Time to wake up from the nightmare)

2375
01:40:17,967 --> 01:40:19,266
We should hold the line.

2376
01:40:19,267 --> 01:40:21,034
Set the block!

2377
01:40:21,393 --> 01:40:23,226
Watch the setter from the back row.

2378
01:40:23,434 --> 01:40:24,734
I'll drop back.

2379
01:40:25,601 --> 01:40:27,467
(One holds the defense,)

2380
01:40:28,234 --> 01:40:30,201
(while another bides her time.)

2381
01:40:30,534 --> 01:40:31,366
Yeon Joo, time your jump!

2382
01:40:31,367 --> 01:40:32,900
Here comes number two.

2383
01:40:32,901 --> 01:40:34,034
Watch number two.

2384
01:40:34,801 --> 01:40:36,967
Bring it home, Onishi!

2385
01:40:37,267 --> 01:40:39,700
(Both sides anticipating number two)

2386
01:40:39,701 --> 01:40:41,302
Enkhsoyol, keep your platform steady!

2387
01:40:42,993 --> 01:40:45,026
Slide to the right!

2388
01:40:46,634 --> 01:40:47,375
Okay!

2389
01:40:48,537 --> 01:40:49,310
Okay!

2390
01:40:50,001 --> 01:40:51,901
(It isn't Number 2 but Number 7.)

2391
01:40:54,001 --> 01:40:56,600
(Number 2 is just a decoy.)

2392
01:40:56,601 --> 01:40:58,234
Yu Kyung, set up the dig!

2393
01:40:59,701 --> 01:41:02,201
(Will they avenge their loss...)

2394
01:41:03,134 --> 01:41:05,567
(or get caught off guard?)

2395
01:41:06,734 --> 01:41:07,600
- Boom!
- Boom!

2396
01:41:07,601 --> 01:41:08,534
Great serve.

2397
01:41:08,967 --> 01:41:10,601
(The decoy play unfolds.)

2398
01:41:10,967 --> 01:41:12,734
- Number two!
- She's coming.

2399
01:41:13,887 --> 01:41:15,553
(Dashing right as planned)

2400
01:41:16,134 --> 01:41:17,001
Right side!

2401
01:41:17,267 --> 01:41:18,366
(Miyamoto takes the swing.)

2402
01:41:18,367 --> 01:41:19,766
It's not Onishi!

2403
01:41:19,767 --> 01:41:20,567
They're going opposite.

2404
01:41:21,001 --> 01:41:22,243
It's on the right pin.

2405
01:41:22,867 --> 01:41:23,900
Only a solo block up!

2406
01:41:23,901 --> 01:41:24,834
Trouble!

2407
01:41:25,201 --> 01:41:27,266
Cross-court! Chae Rim!

2408
01:41:27,267 --> 01:41:28,767
(A year-long nightmare)

2409
01:41:30,134 --> 01:41:32,067
Ever since that loss last year,

2410
01:41:32,534 --> 01:41:34,122
I wanted this payback so badly.

2411
01:41:36,501 --> 01:41:37,992
This is dangerous.

2412
01:41:45,333 --> 01:41:46,051
(Huh?)

2413
01:41:47,201 --> 01:41:48,333
Out!

2414
01:41:48,334 --> 01:41:49,170
That's wide.

2415
01:41:50,467 --> 01:41:53,367
- Out!
- It's out!

2416
01:41:53,655 --> 01:41:54,155
(Out)

2417
01:41:54,534 --> 01:41:56,934
(Attack error sails wide.)

2418
01:42:01,934 --> 01:42:03,867
(Cheering)

2419
01:42:05,967 --> 01:42:07,166
(Cheering)

2420
01:42:07,167 --> 01:42:09,934
(Cheering)

2421
01:42:16,267 --> 01:42:19,734
(Set score, 2:3)

2422
01:42:23,062 --> 01:42:25,242
(Wonder Dogs 3 : Shujitsu High 2)

2423
01:42:25,267 --> 01:42:28,966
The Wonder Dogs pull off
a thrilling comeback...

2424
01:42:28,967 --> 01:42:30,645
in their revenge match,

2425
01:42:30,842 --> 01:42:32,900
taking game one!

2426
01:42:32,901 --> 01:42:36,101
(Wonder Dogs seal the reverse sweep!)

2427
01:42:36,759 --> 01:42:38,659
The set score finishes 3 to 2.

2428
01:42:39,610 --> 01:42:42,076
(We had lost in a reverse sweep.)

2429
01:42:42,883 --> 01:42:44,668
(This time, we take the reverse sweep.)

2430
01:42:44,701 --> 01:42:47,200
I'm almost feeling dizzy.

2431
01:42:47,201 --> 01:42:50,267
(Are you sure it's not a dream?)

2432
01:42:51,134 --> 01:42:53,001
(Letting it out)

2433
01:42:54,634 --> 01:42:56,233
It still hasn't sunk in.

2434
01:42:56,234 --> 01:42:58,834
Wonder Dogs take the win!

2435
01:43:00,534 --> 01:43:02,501
- Incredible fight!
- Thank you!

2436
01:43:03,101 --> 01:43:04,366
(Wonder Dogs capture their first win.)

2437
01:43:04,367 --> 01:43:05,413
We actually did it.

2438
01:43:06,867 --> 01:43:09,334
Straight out of a movie script.

2439
01:43:09,967 --> 01:43:12,300
You couldn't write a match like this
if you tried.

2440
01:43:12,301 --> 01:43:13,200
Seriously.

2441
01:43:13,201 --> 01:43:14,301
(Shaking her head)

2442
01:43:15,010 --> 01:43:17,692
This is too much. I'm losing my mind.

2443
01:43:17,867 --> 01:43:19,067
We survived.

2444
01:43:22,967 --> 01:43:24,500
You all played your hearts out.

2445
01:43:24,501 --> 01:43:26,300
You've done an amazing job.

2446
01:43:26,301 --> 01:43:27,267
Chae Rim.

2447
01:43:32,901 --> 01:43:34,034
(Covering her eyes for her)

2448
01:43:36,134 --> 01:43:37,201
(Holding back)

2449
01:43:47,001 --> 01:43:48,001
Why are you crying?

2450
01:43:49,634 --> 01:43:50,501
You okay?

2451
01:43:56,734 --> 01:44:00,567
(Holding back tears during the handshake)

2452
01:44:00,901 --> 01:44:02,567
(Sobbing)

2453
01:44:05,334 --> 01:44:07,801
(Trying to hold it together)

2454
01:44:08,467 --> 01:44:10,434
Great job out there.

2455
01:44:10,893 --> 01:44:12,359
(Crying)

2456
01:44:12,634 --> 01:44:14,001
I'm so proud of you.

2457
01:44:14,467 --> 01:44:15,367
Chae Rim?

2458
01:44:18,301 --> 01:44:19,233
Chae Rim!

2459
01:44:19,234 --> 01:44:21,843
- This is only game one!
- Why are you crying?

2460
01:44:21,867 --> 01:44:23,734
We just played our first match!

2461
01:44:26,667 --> 01:44:29,367
I think I finally saw a way forward.

2462
01:44:30,067 --> 01:44:32,000
I had so many regrets
after that first loss.

2463
01:44:32,534 --> 01:44:34,233
You have to throw your body at the ball!

2464
01:44:34,234 --> 01:44:35,067
Understood.

2465
01:44:36,001 --> 01:44:37,101
I gritted my teeth,

2466
01:44:38,467 --> 01:44:39,974
and played like everything
was on the line.

2467
01:44:40,567 --> 01:44:43,434
(Chae Rim locked in.)

2468
01:44:43,939 --> 01:44:45,354
You can't just throw in the towel now.

2469
01:44:45,379 --> 01:44:48,442
(Hang in there, and anything is possible!)

2470
01:44:50,902 --> 01:44:54,004
After leaving
Korea Expressway Corporation,

2471
01:44:54,005 --> 01:44:56,640
I almost walked away
from volleyball entirely,

2472
01:44:56,641 --> 01:45:00,177
but somehow, I held on
and kept pushing forward.

2473
01:45:00,445 --> 01:45:02,246
I transitioned to beach volleyball,

2474
01:45:02,447 --> 01:45:04,448
then kept playing in college.

2475
01:45:04,449 --> 01:45:07,551
As long as the ball was in the air,
I wasn't ready to let go.

2476
01:45:09,788 --> 01:45:13,357
I knew we'd have to face Shujitsu again,

2477
01:45:13,358 --> 01:45:15,126
and the fear of losing was real.

2478
01:45:15,127 --> 01:45:16,010
No!

2479
01:45:16,128 --> 01:45:17,552
The weight on my shoulders was immense.

2480
01:45:17,576 --> 01:45:19,113
Could we actually pull this off?

2481
01:45:20,832 --> 01:45:22,432
You were all incredible out there.

2482
01:45:22,433 --> 01:45:23,756
Keep your heads up.

2483
01:45:23,781 --> 01:45:25,669
It's okay. You played your hearts out.

2484
01:45:26,237 --> 01:45:27,337
Come on, we've got this!

2485
01:45:27,362 --> 01:45:28,806
(There, there.)

2486
01:45:30,095 --> 01:45:32,930
(A much-needed victory)

2487
01:45:33,611 --> 01:45:36,330
I'm just so overwhelmed with relief.

2488
01:45:38,188 --> 01:45:39,967
Chae Rim, you held the line.

2489
01:45:41,286 --> 01:45:43,203
Now that it's over and we won...

2490
01:45:43,321 --> 01:45:44,254
Proud of you.

2491
01:45:45,823 --> 01:45:46,923
Yes!

2492
01:45:49,994 --> 01:45:51,294
They pulled it off!

2493
01:45:52,330 --> 01:45:54,682
- This match took years off my life.
- I can't take this anymore. Send me home.

2494
01:45:55,133 --> 01:45:56,934
Man, that drained everything out of me.

2495
01:45:58,038 --> 01:45:59,005
How did they pull that off?

2496
01:45:59,037 --> 01:45:59,870
(All right, that's enough.)

2497
01:46:00,439 --> 01:46:02,540
Since stepping away from pro play,

2498
01:46:03,167 --> 01:46:07,821
I don't think I've felt
that kind of adrenaline.

2499
01:46:07,853 --> 01:46:09,579
I've been to hell and back.

2500
01:46:09,881 --> 01:46:12,449
(Dreaming of launching an eighth team)

2501
01:46:12,450 --> 01:46:13,534
Free ball! Run the offense!

2502
01:46:13,785 --> 01:46:16,153
(A rude awakening for the rookie coach)

2503
01:46:17,075 --> 01:46:18,142
(Barking out orders)

2504
01:46:18,565 --> 01:46:19,840
I ended up raising my voice.

2505
01:46:20,558 --> 01:46:22,158
Chae Rim with the roll shot!

2506
01:46:22,159 --> 01:46:23,126
Chae Rim!

2507
01:46:23,127 --> 01:46:25,279
Take a breath. You're fine.

2508
01:46:25,304 --> 01:46:26,747
I kept telling them not to dwell on it.

2509
01:46:27,332 --> 01:46:29,333
I tried to lift their spirits,
reminding them how well they were playing.

2510
01:46:29,358 --> 01:46:30,358
One! Two!

2511
01:46:30,470 --> 01:46:32,336
Onishi. Roofed!

2512
01:46:32,337 --> 01:46:33,537
There it is!

2513
01:46:33,538 --> 01:46:36,156
I finally set the clipboard down
so I could match their rhythm directly.

2514
01:46:36,181 --> 01:46:37,584
You've got this!

2515
01:46:37,609 --> 01:46:40,361
I truly gave it everything I had.

2516
01:46:40,882 --> 01:46:44,895
(How did you feel when you finally won?)

2517
01:46:45,917 --> 01:46:48,118
We survived. We took the match.

2518
01:46:49,521 --> 01:46:50,504
What a relief.

2519
01:46:51,222 --> 01:46:52,522
Man, that completely took it out of me.

2520
01:46:52,523 --> 01:46:54,108
I think I lost a few years off my life.

2521
01:46:54,192 --> 01:46:55,876
I'm hanging up the clipboard.

2522
01:46:56,194 --> 01:46:57,561
Never coaching again.

2523
01:46:57,929 --> 01:47:00,614
If they come calling for Season Three,
it's an immediate no. No chance.

2524
01:47:00,965 --> 01:47:02,616
Never putting myself through this again.

2525
01:47:02,901 --> 01:47:04,301
Snap out of it, Yeon Koung.

2526
01:47:04,302 --> 01:47:07,737
Commit this exact feeling
to memory right now.

2527
01:47:07,738 --> 01:47:09,206
Don't let them sweet-talk you.

2528
01:47:09,474 --> 01:47:11,058
Don't fall into the trap again.

2529
01:47:12,377 --> 01:47:15,045
Honestly, it's hard to put into words.

2530
01:47:15,360 --> 01:47:16,263
It's just...

2531
01:47:17,482 --> 01:47:20,284
I think this is the beauty of sports.

2532
01:47:20,785 --> 01:47:22,252
There's no script to follow.

2533
01:47:22,253 --> 01:47:23,789
You can't rehearse any of it.

2534
01:47:23,790 --> 01:47:25,388
It's just two teams out there...

2535
01:47:25,389 --> 01:47:28,191
leaving every drop of sweat on the court,

2536
01:47:28,593 --> 01:47:32,195
with everything decided
by the thinnest of margins.

2537
01:47:32,983 --> 01:47:35,051
It's just...

2538
01:47:36,935 --> 01:47:37,868
pure joy.

2539
01:47:38,536 --> 01:47:40,370
Winning feels amazing,

2540
01:47:40,371 --> 01:47:44,474
and it feels like we're genuinely unified
heading into Season Two.

2541
01:47:44,475 --> 01:47:46,109
(They pulled through together!)

2542
01:47:46,134 --> 01:47:47,761
(Their next opponent)

2543
01:47:48,097 --> 01:47:50,465
(The Wonder Dogs' captain,)

2544
01:47:50,497 --> 01:47:52,131
(Pyo Seung Ju)

2545
01:47:54,300 --> 01:47:56,269
I'm Pyo Seung Ju of the Pink Spiders.

2546
01:47:56,270 --> 01:47:57,009
(Yesterday's teammate is...)

2547
01:47:57,062 --> 01:47:59,264
Number six, Lee Na Yeon.

2548
01:48:00,165 --> 01:48:01,785
(today's opponent.)

2549
01:48:01,933 --> 01:48:02,900
Nice!

2550
01:48:02,901 --> 01:48:04,878
I'm bringing everything I've got
to take this win.

2551
01:48:05,737 --> 01:48:07,571
(The first live match of Season Two)

2552
01:48:07,596 --> 01:48:09,116
Their first professional opponent is...

2553
01:48:09,608 --> 01:48:11,008
the Pink Spiders.

2554
01:48:11,777 --> 01:48:13,010
Target Enkhsoyol on serve.

2555
01:48:13,011 --> 01:48:14,321
- Enkhsoyol?
- Yeah.

2556
01:48:14,880 --> 01:48:16,347
Seung Ju on the left.

2557
01:48:18,417 --> 01:48:19,283
Puts it down!

2558
01:48:20,398 --> 01:48:23,300
(An opponent who knows me inside out)

2559
01:48:23,789 --> 01:48:25,857
Keep attacking through Seung Ju.

2560
01:48:26,734 --> 01:48:27,934
Enkhsoyol!

2561
01:48:27,959 --> 01:48:29,633
(An opponent I know inside out)

2562
01:48:29,893 --> 01:48:30,862
(Yes, Coach!)

2563
01:48:30,863 --> 01:48:31,695
That's it!

2564
01:48:31,696 --> 01:48:33,607
(A battle to exploit
each other's weaknesses)

2565
01:48:33,632 --> 01:48:35,533
Go for the kill!

2566
01:48:35,719 --> 01:48:37,010
Collapse inside!

2567
01:48:37,161 --> 01:48:39,237
(Pink Spiders vs. Pink Spiders)

2568
01:48:39,237 --> 01:48:40,204
Heavy swing!

2569
01:48:40,339 --> 01:48:41,272
What a dig!

2570
01:48:41,273 --> 01:48:43,258
(Wonder Dogs vs. Wonder Dogs)

2571
01:48:43,283 --> 01:48:44,542
Can they pop it up?

2572
01:48:44,543 --> 01:48:46,453
There it is!

2573
01:48:47,646 --> 01:48:49,180
The Wonder Dogs are fired up!

2574
01:48:49,181 --> 01:48:50,215
(The Wonder Coach 2)

2575
01:48:50,240 --> 01:48:51,240
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
